| Hard delete of any record | Permanently excluded — soft delete only on all tables; statutory data may be archived but never hard-deleted |

## 2.3 Assumptions

- Tenant home region is India; data residency requirement flag is set to India with a DR replica in a second Indian region.

- Release 1 tenants operate at a scale of up to 500 active employees plus 5 years of historical records.

- Architecture must support up to 100 tenants without re-engineering, but the post-migration go-live will operate at a single-tenant scale.

- Google Workspace is the assumed identity provider for tenants choosing SSO. Tenants on username/password may opt for self-hosted credentials.

- Biometric devices and IP-based attendance restrictions require prior device and location registration in P04 Tenant & Org Admin by Organisation Admin or Platform Super Admin before M05 configuration can be activated.

- BGV vendor selection (primary plus configurable additional vendors) and bank file format (NEFT / RTGS — Phase 2) are confirmed by the customer at provisioning.

- All AI calls are made from the backend; the AI API key is never exposed to the browser, and PII is stripped from prompts server-side.

## 2.4 Constraints

| **Constraint type** | **Detail** |
| --- | --- |
| Technical — page size & breakpoints | Responsive web supporting 375 px (mobile), 768 px (tablet), 1280 px (desktop). Mobile touch targets minimum 44 × 44 px on all interactive elements. |
| Technical — accessibility | WCAG 2.1 AA compliance — all web screens must pass automated checks. |
| Technical — browser support | Modern evergreen browsers (latest two major versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari). No support for Internet Explorer. |
| Technical — encryption | TLS minimum version enforced across all connections. AES-256-GCM for PII at rest. Per-tenant KMS keys with envelope encryption pattern. |
| Operational — deployment | Zero-downtime production deployments. Scheduled maintenance window Sundays 01:00 – 04:00 IST only. |
| Regulatory — DPDPA 2023 | Consent capture, right of access, right of correction, right of erasure (non-statutory data), data fiduciary obligations are all mandatory from Day 1. |
| Regulatory — POSH Act 2013 | Mandatory policy, complaint intake, ICC routing, and training tracking from Day 1. |
| Regulatory — statutory retention | Statutory data (payroll, PF, TDS) has legally mandated minimum retention; hard delete is blocked at both application and database layers. |
| Regulatory — audit log retention | Minimum 7 years. After 2 years entries may be archived to cold storage but must remain queryable within 24 hours. |
| Security — VAPT | External Vulnerability Assessment & Penetration Testing ahead of the single post-migration go-live. All Critical and High findings must be resolved before live data is loaded. Zero Critical or High CVEs in production at go-live. |
| Security — MFA | Multi-Factor Authentication enforced by default for HR Admin and Organisation Admin roles. |
| Data integrity — deletes | No hard deletes on any table — soft delete with timestamp only. |
| Data integrity — referential integrity | All foreign key constraints enforced at the database layer. |
| Data integrity — uniqueness | Employee ID, company email, PAN (per active employees), and Aadhaar are unique constraints enforced at the database layer. |
| Audit completeness | 100% of mutations captured via database-level trigger; zero gaps permitted. No application bug, developer action, or API bypass can suppress an audit entry. |

# 3. User Roles & Permissions

[RBAC — single source of truth] The RBAC Design Document v1.7 is the authoritative single source for the access-control model: role taxonomy, the permission matrix, field-level access, capability flags, individual entitlements, and User Assignment Groups. Sections 3.2–3.10 below are retained as business context; where they differ from the RBAC Design Document, the RBAC Design Document governs. Workspace model (owned by the Foundation FS): a user's workspaces (Me / My Team / Admin) derive from role holdings; Admin workspaces are exclusive (self-service suppressed) while operational people-scoped roles — Manager, HOD, UAG Head, HRBP — are non-exclusive and retain self-service; Tasks and Notifications persist across every workspace including Admin. Phase-1 capability flags are four — BGV review, Letter Admin, Asset Custodian, and Department Head — Asset Audit Certify — plus two HOD configurable grants (report visibility; per-workflow approval authority). Change Manager is not a Phase-1 flag.

## 3.1 Role Taxonomy Overview

PrimeSoft HRMS Phase 1 defines 18 distinct roles spanning platform administration, organisational administration, HR operations, module administration, manager hierarchy, specialist functions, and individual access. A user may hold more than one role simultaneously. Where a user holds more than one role, the more restrictive permission applies — a less permissive role never elevates access granted by a more permissive one (Conflict Resolution Rule). **Exception — defined inheritance:** HR Admin is a defined superset of the nine operational module-admin roles (§3.1.1); its inherited permissions are part of the HR Admin role definition itself, not a multi-role combination, so the Conflict Resolution Rule does not down-scope HR Admin to a module admin’s narrower reach.

Access control operates at four layers, applied in combination for every user session: (a) Module-level — whether a module is visible at all; (b) Field & Section level — visibility and editability of fields and form sections; (c) Data-level (row-level security) — which records a role can see, scoped by reporting chain, department, contribution level, UAG, or entity; (d) Action-level — what a user can do within a record (View Only, Edit, Approve/Reject, Download, Admin Rights).

**PII Protection Ceiling — PII fields carry system-enforced protection ceilings. No Organisation Admin, Module Admin, or any other role can override these ceilings upward. PII protection is data-driven, not hard-coded at any level: the classification and masking rules are configuration set at the platform level and establish a protection floor. Organisation Admin may tighten protection further at group or entity level, but no role or level can widen PII exposure above the platform-set ceiling. Exceptions are explicit platform-level grants (e.g. Office Admin national ID access) and are fixed — not configurable.**

## 3.2 Platform Roles

| **Role** | **Code** | **Scope** | **Core mandate** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Platform Super Admin | platform_super_admin | All tenants | Tenant provisioning · segment and geography selection · platform master data · cross-tenant analytics · migration tooling tenant-level operations (provisioning, staging environment, dry run execution) |
| Organisation Admin | org_admin | Single tenant — all entities | Org structure · **User Assignment Group (UAG) creation (shared with HR Admin)** · workflow configuration · field-level RBAC · integration credentials · SSO policy · individual entitlement grants (mandatory expiry, audit-logged) · **cross-entity HR data visibility within the tenant** (consolidated reports, group-level org chart, group attrition view, internal mobility across entities) — the only role with cross-entity visibility inside a tenant. Org Admin does NOT perform per-employee HR transactions; those remain with the entity-scoped HR Admin. · **cross-entity HR data visibility within the tenant** (group-level headcount, attrition, mobility, ex-employee history). Operates above the entity boundary; does NOT replace per-entity HR Admins for entity-scoped HR operations. |

## 3.3 Entity-Scoped Operational Roles

**Entity scope reminder.** All roles in this section operate within a single legal entity. The HR Administrator, Finance Admin, HRBP, Office Admin, CEO, and the module-specific admins (Onboarding, Offboarding, Leave, Attendance, Performance, Document, Recruitment) all have single-entity scope. **No HR transaction crosses entity boundaries** — every leave application, separation, payroll run, statutory return, and employee record edit stays within the entity that owns the employee. **Cross-entity visibility within a tenant is owned by Org Admin alone** (see §3.2 Platform Roles). **Platform Super Admin is cross-tenant, not cross-entity** — it should not be used to bridge entities within a single tenant. If an HR Administrator needs cross-entity insight (e.g. a group-wide attrition report or to check whether a separated employee from Entity A has been rehired into Entity B), the request is routed to Org Admin, who provides the consolidated view.

**Entity scope reminder.** All operational roles in this section are scoped to a **single legal entity** within the tenant. In a Group Company deployment with multiple entities (e.g. a holding company with subsidiaries across geographies — Solutions Pvt Ltd in India, Global Inc in the US, Services Pte Ltd in Singapore), each entity is staffed with its own HR Admin, Finance Admin, Office Admin and module admins (Onboarding, Leave, Attendance, Performance, Document, Offboarding, Recruitment). **No transactional flow crosses entity boundaries** — every leave application, attendance regularisation, payroll component, statutory filing, separation FnF, and grievance stays within the employee’s entity of record. Cross-entity activities (group headcount reports, group attrition, ex-employee lookup across entities, internal mobility scouting across entities) are owned by **Org Admin** per §3.2; HR Admin is **not** the channel for cross-entity visibility. Platform Super Admin is cross-tenant (all customers) and is also **not** the channel for cross-entity visibility within a single tenant.

| **Role** | **Code** | **Scope** | **Core mandate** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| HR Administrator | hr_admin | Single entity | **Superset operational role — HR Admin can perform all functions of every module admin within the entity.** Full employee lifecycle · policy and document management · **project master (§4.2.21, entity-scoped)** · **User Assignment Group (UAG) creation and management — including project-scoped UAGs, location selection, and employee tagging (one employee → one UAG). UAG is access-control only; leave / shift / holiday are assigned via the Assignment Framework (§4.2.17), not the UAG** · **offer letter generation (jointly with Recruitment Admin)** · audit log access · leave encashment case-by-case authorisation (HR Admin only). HR Admin inherits the complete permission set of Recruitment Admin, Onboarding Admin, Leave Admin, Attendance Admin, Document Admin, Performance Admin, Offboarding Admin, Office Admin, and Analytics Admin (see §3.1.1). Module admins remain available for delegation, but any task a module admin can do, HR Admin can also do directly. |
| Finance Admin | finance_admin | Single entity | Cost centre management. Phase 2 adds payroll approval and individual payslip view/download. Joint module admin on M10 for configuration purposes only (no hike approval authority in Phase 1 scope). |
| HRBP | hrbp | Directly assigned employees (individually or via UAG) | HR operations for assigned employees · grievance intake · policy advisory · engagement oversight · leave application approval and rejection for directly assigned employees · attendance request approval. Business unit assignment optional. |
| Office Admin | office_admin | Single entity | Employee directory · date of birth view · national ID view and upload (PAN, Aadhaar, Passport, Driving Licence) · bank account entry and update (masked after entry). No payroll, compensation, performance, leave, or attendance access. |
| CEO | ceo | Single entity | Standard employee self-service access otherwise. (Final approver for hike and compensation decisions — Phase 2.) |
| Onboarding Admin | onboarding_admin | M02 only — single entity | Configure onboarding checklists · manage task assignments · configure buddy assignments · track onboarding completion · manage BGV vendor profiles · assign verification packages. Capability flag: BGV review (grantable by Org Admin). |
| Separation Admin (Offboarding Admin) | offboarding_admin | M03 only — single entity | Owns the separation surface: configure FnF clearance workflows and separation checklists · build and version the exit interview form (M11 form-builder) · read exit interview raw responses (Exit Interview Reader, within UAG) · schedule / track the exit interview · oversee the FnF clearance board and clear/hold per stage · initiate org-side termination (Separation Initiator) · track offboarding completion. Confidentiality of raw exit responses is hard-coded to HR Admin, Separation Admin, and HRBP (within UAG) (F.3 / DE11; CHRO removed — no CHRO role exists per DE16). FnF payroll settlement remains with HR Admin (Phase 2 with Finance Admin). HR Admin retains this full surface as a superset role (§3.1.1). |
| Leave Admin | leave_admin | M04 only — single entity | Configure leave types, policies, accrual rules · override balances · manage holiday calendar · approve and reject individual leave requests within entity scope. Encashment authorisation is HR Admin only — Leave Admin cannot authorise individual encashment requests. Leave-type DEFINITION and leave-policy ASSIGNMENT (Assignment-Framework targeting) are shared functions: Leave Admin, Org Admin and HR Admin all have full define-and-assign access, RBAC-configurable (default: full edit for all three). |
| Attendance Admin | attendance_admin | M05 only — single entity | Configure shifts and rosters · manage biometric device mapping · lock and unlock attendance periods · override punch records · approve and reject all attendance request types · eligible approver from Stage 1. |
| Performance Admin | performance_admin | M09 only — single entity | Configure appraisal cycles · manage goal frameworks · initiate and close cycles · manage calibration sessions. Subject to contribution level, department, field, and section entitlement configuration per user. |
| Recruitment Admin | recruitment_admin | Recruitment module — all requisitions within entity | Full ATS visibility · offer letter generation (jointly with HR Admin) · recruiter assignment · pipeline oversight · reporting. Subject to all five entitlement dimensions. |
| Recruiter | recruiter | Recruitment module — assigned requisitions only | ATS and pipeline management · candidate communication · BGC initiation. **Cannot generate offer letters** (Recruitment Admin or HR Admin only). Visibility restricted to assigned requisitions only. |
| Document Admin | document_admin | M11 only — single entity | Configure policy library register · manage policy clusters and acknowledgement requirements · configure letter template register and merge fields · manage employee document vault settings · manage sign-off engine · manage versioning rules. Capability flag: Letter Admin (grantable by Org Admin). |
| Analytics Admin | analytics_admin | M16 only — entity-scoped by default | Create and publish custom report definitions · schedule report delivery · manage dashboard layouts. Analytics is available to all users — data visibility for every user governed by their own role entitlements. Tenant-wide configuration available via individual entitlement granted by Org Admin. |
| IT Admin | it_admin | M17 only — single entity | Asset master · device assignment and return · IT provisioning tasks · FnF clearance queue. |
| Service Desk Admin | service_desk_admin | M17 service desk — entity-scoped | Configures service desk: categories, queues, SLAs, escalation chains, catalog items, KB taxonomy. Marks tickets Out-of-Scope. Joint module ownership with IT Admin. |
| Service Desk Agent | service_desk_agent | M17 — assigned queues only | Acts on tickets in assigned queues: pick up, reply, transition states. Cannot reassign cross-queue without Queue Lead approval. |

**M17 Assets & IT roles and capability flags. **M17 introduces two distinct operational roles — Service Desk Admin (module-admin for the service desk surface) and Service Desk Agent (queue-bound operational role) — alongside the existing IT Admin role that owns the asset master, provisioning, and FnF clearance. Three capability flags support M17:

- **Asset Custodian** — granted by Org Admin to named users at locations or for asset classes; location-scoped asset handling (assignment, return, periodic stock count); cannot configure module-level settings.

- **Department Head — Asset Audit Certify** — granted by default to every HOD at provisioning; receives the annual asset list scoped to their department, verifies or delegates, flags discrepancies, and certifies the team's reconciliation within 10 business days. HODs cannot edit asset records — flagging produces an audit-exception ticket to IT Admin.

- **Change Manager (Phase 1.5)** — Phase 1 the IT Asset Manager double-hats; whether this becomes a distinct role or a capability flag is decided at Phase 1.5 design.

**PII handling for M17 fields. **Tier 1 (licence keys) is encrypted at rest with view events audited. Tier 2 (purchase cost, serial number, MAC address, IP / management IP, insurance policy reference) is masked in list responses to non-privileged roles. Insurance Policy Reference is visible only to Finance Admin and IT Asset Manager; Server IP and Network Infrastructure Management IP are visible to Infra Ops / Network Ops custodians, IT Asset Manager, and CISO.

### 3.1.1 HR Admin as the operational superset role

HR Admin is the **single operational superset role** within an entity. Every permission held by any of the nine module-specific admin roles is also held by HR Admin. This means HR Admin can directly perform every configuration, approval, override, and oversight action that the following roles can perform, without needing the module-admin role to be separately assigned:

| **Module admin role** | **Module** | **Functions HR Admin inherits** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Recruitment Admin | M08 | Full ATS visibility · requisition management · recruiter assignment · pre-offer issuance · document review · offer letter generation · pipeline oversight · recruitment reporting |
| Onboarding Admin | M02 | Configure onboarding checklists · task assignments · buddy assignments · BGV vendor profiles · verification packages · onboarding completion tracking |
| Leave Admin | M04 | Configure leave types / policies / accrual rules · override balances · manage holiday calendar · approve and reject leave requests · (plus HR Admin’s exclusive encashment authorisation) |
| Attendance Admin | M05 | Configure shifts and rosters · biometric device mapping · lock / unlock attendance periods · override punch records · approve and reject attendance request types |
| Document Admin | M11 | Configure policy library register · policy clusters and acknowledgement requirements · letter template register and merge fields · employee document vault settings · sign-off engine · versioning rules |
| Performance Admin | M09 | Configure appraisal periods and cycles · manage goal frameworks · initiate and close cycles · manage calibration sessions · (jointly owns appraisal-period definition with Performance Admin per FR-M09-001) |
| Offboarding Admin (Exit Admin) | M03 | Configure FnF clearance workflows · exit interview templates · separation checklists · offboarding completion tracking · (plus HR Admin’s FnF settlement authority) |
| Office Admin | M01 | Employee directory · date-of-birth view · national ID view and upload (PAN, Aadhaar, Passport, Driving Licence) · bank account entry and update |
| Analytics Admin | M16 | Create and publish custom report definitions · schedule report delivery · manage dashboard layouts (entity-scoped) |

**Rules governing the superset:**

- **Inheritance is one-directional.** HR Admin ⊇ each module admin. No module admin inherits HR Admin’s broader permissions (e.g. Leave Admin cannot do recruitment tasks; Onboarding Admin cannot do attendance tasks).

- **Module admins remain assignable for delegation.** An entity may still appoint a dedicated Leave Admin, Attendance Admin, etc. to distribute operational load. The superset relationship does not remove the module-admin roles — it means HR Admin does not *require* them to act in those areas.

- **PII protection ceilings still apply.** The superset does not elevate HR Admin above any system-enforced PII ceiling. HR Admin’s PII access is governed by §3.1’s PII Protection Ceiling rules, not widened by inheriting module-admin permissions.

- **Entity scope is preserved.** HR Admin’s superset applies only within their own entity. Cross-entity visibility remains with Org Admin per §3.2 — inheriting module-admin permissions does not grant cross-entity reach.

- **Joint-authority patterns are unaffected.** Where a function is explicitly joint (offer letter generation with Recruitment Admin; appraisal-period definition with Performance Admin), HR Admin’s inherited permission satisfies one side of the joint authority; it does not bypass approvals that require a second distinct role (e.g. CEO co-signature on above-threshold offers).

## 3.4 Manager Hierarchy Roles

| **Role** | **Code** | **Data scope** | **Action level** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Manager (L1) | l1_manager | Direct and indirect reports | Full operational permissions — attendance, leave, performance, workflow approvals · team analytics scoped to reporting chain |
| L2 Manager | l2_manager | Reporting subtree | Progressively reduced vs L1 |
| L3 Manager | l3_manager | Reporting subtree | Progressively reduced vs L2 |
| L4 Manager | l4_manager | Reporting subtree | Progressively reduced vs L3 |
| L5 Manager+ | l5_manager | Reporting subtree | Minimal permissions — read-only |
| HOD | hod | Entire assigned department | Department-wide read visibility · minimal write · workflow tab access · compensation and rating visibility off by default (Org Admin per-user configurable) · workflow approval authority off by default (Org Admin per-workflow per-user configurable) |
| UAG Head | uag_head | Assigned User Assignment Group | Same entitlements as HOD scoped to assigned group · compensation and rating visibility off by default (Org Admin per-user configurable) · workflow approval authority cannot be granted under any configuration (hard system ceiling) |
| Skip-level Manager | skip_level_manager | Full reporting subtree | Read visibility only — no write or approval actions · retains access to published ratings after calibration window closes |
| Dotted Line Manager | dotted_line_manager | Dotted-line reportees | Limited read visibility — personal and employment details only. No appraisal access. |

## 3.5 Individual Access Roles

| **Role** | **Code** | **Access boundary** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Employee | employee | Own data within entity — self-service profile · leave and expense requests · payslip and document access · Chat Agent · appraisals · employee directory and org chart · own analytics |
| Candidate / Pre-joining | candidate | Recruitment portal (candidate state) · Pre-joining portal (post-offer acceptance state). Candidate: own application status · document upload · BGC consent. Pre-joining: offer letter · onboarding forms · policy documents · Chat Agent. No live HRMS access in either state. |

## 3.6 Data Scoping Dimensions

Five dimensions can be combined to define what records a user can see:

- Reporting Chain — Manager roles see records of their direct and indirect reports only. Skip-level Managers see their full subtree but cannot approve or edit.

- Department — HOD sees all employees in their assigned department regardless of reporting line.

- User Assignment Group (UAG) — A named group of one or more employees, optionally scoped to a project and its locations. Created and managed by HR Admin or Organisation Admin. An employee belongs to at most one UAG. UAG is an RBAC (access-control) construct only — it defines who can see and act on a population (e.g. UAG Head scope). It does NOT carry leave, shift, or holiday entitlement; those are assigned via the Assignment Framework (§4.2.17). UAG Head has same entitlements as HOD scoped to their group, except workflow approval authority (hard ceiling).

- HRBP Assignment — HRBPs are assigned employees directly, individually or via UAG. Data scope limited to directly assigned employees, refined by entitlement dimensions.

- Contribution Level — Additional filter applied within a role’s normal scope. Levels: Intern, Associate, Individual Contributor, Lead, Senior Lead, Manager, Senior Manager, CEO. Used in performance calibration scoping, hike recommendation banding (Phase 2), and recruitment entitlement configuration.

- Entity — HR Admin, Finance Admin, and Office Admin are scoped to their single entity. Cross-entity access requires explicit privilege granted by Organisation Admin and is audit-logged.

- Individual Entitlement — Time-bound access beyond a role’s default profile, granted by Organisation Admin within PII protection ceilings. All individual entitlements require Org Admin approval, are audit-logged, carry a mandatory expiry date, and are automatically revoked on expiry.

