## 3.10 Capability Flag Registry

Capability flags are grantable extensions to existing roles. A flag is NOT a role — it is an opt-in capability that an Organisation Admin grants to a specific user’s existing role assignment. Grant and revoke events are audit-logged to P05.

**Skills ****&**** Assets visibility.** An employee’s **Skills / Competency Profile** is visible to the employee, their management chain (L1–L5, HOD/UAG Head) for deployment and development decisions, but **not to HR Admin, HRBP, or Finance Admin** on the employee record. **Assigned Assets** are owned by **IT Admin (M17)** and are visible to the employee and their direct manager (via Team Assets); they are **not surfaced on the HR Admin or HRBP employee-detail view** — HR Admin engages with assets only for FnF recovery escalation (FR-M17-004). This keeps the HR employee record focused on HR-domain data and avoids HR seeing IT asset inventory or skills taxonomy by default.

**FY26 HOD visibility revision.** Education Qualifications and Certifications are visible to the HOD / UAG Head — in addition to the employee and the L1–L5 management chain — for development and deployment decisions, consistent with the Skills / Competency Profile rule above. Education and Certifications are visible to HR Admin, HRBP, Managers (L1–L5), and the HOD / UAG Head, plus the employee on their own record. By contrast, the Skills / Competency Profile and date of birth remain restricted: Skills are visible to the employee and the L1–L5 / HOD chain but not to HR Admin, HRBP or Finance; date of birth is visible only to HR Admin, Office Admin and the employee (no manager, HOD, HRBP, peer or social-surface visibility, and no year-masking). Previous-employment, references and languages follow the same chain visibility as Education / Certifications; the statutory detail entities (PF / EPS / ESIC / gratuity / LWF / PT / insurance) are visible to the employee, HR Admin and Finance / Payroll Admin only. Full per-entity rows are added to the §3.9 matrix in the M01 functional specification. This revision also flips Probation Status, Confirmation Date, Contract Start Date, Contract End Date, Notice Period, and Previous Employment History from H to V for the HOD / UAG Head in the field-level access matrix above.

| **Flag** | **Grantable on** | **Capability granted** | **Capability NOT granted** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| BGV review | Onboarding Admin · HR Admin | View Verification Reports tab on candidate records · view vendor BGV results per check (Verified · Discrepancy · Pending · Unable to Verify) · record disposition on Discrepancy alerts (retain, investigate, initiate separation) · view BGV result history on Employee Profile post-completion | Edit candidate-submitted form fields (Allow BGV Admin to edit user inputs = No per M02 §A.1) · view BGV results for employees outside the role’s existing data scope · approve onboarding completion |
| Letter Admin | Document Admin · HR Admin | Author and manage letter templates in M11 register · configure merge-field bindings · designate additional editors per template · approve template content for activation · publish and unpublish templates · manage template versioning | Edit policy library content · manage employee document vault contents · alter retention or disposal rules · access documents outside the role’s existing data scope |
| Asset Custodian | IT Admin · IT Asset Manager | Hold custodial responsibility for assigned assets · confirm periodic asset audit for held assets | Edit the asset register · reassign or write-off assets (IT Admin only) |
| Department Head — Asset Audit Certify | HOD / UAG Head | Certify the periodic asset-audit attestation for the department's assigned assets | Edit the asset register · reassign/write-off |

# 4. Data Model

This section defines every entity in the PrimeSoft HRMS Phase 1 platform. Every entity supports soft-delete only — no hard deletes anywhere in the platform. Every entity carries the platform audit columns described below in §4.1. Every entity within a tenant context carries tenant_id (non-nullable); every entity holding organisational data also carries entity_id as a child of tenant_id. All foreign-key relationships are enforced at the database layer. Every entity migrated from Darwinbox carries a darwinbox_source_id column for permanent source-to-state traceability.

## 4.1 Platform Audit Columns — Required on Every Entity

Every entity below extends a base column set. To avoid repetition, the column set is defined once here and referenced throughout. Field tables in §4.2 onward show only the entity-specific columns; the audit columns are implied.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid | Y | Primary key. UUID v4. | auto |
| tenant_id | uuid | Y | FK → tenants.id. Non-nullable on every table. All queries automatically scoped — no query may return data from another tenant. | — |
| entity_id | uuid | Conditional | FK → entities.id. Required on all tables holding organisational data (employee-affiliated, payroll-affiliated, etc.). | — |
| created_at | timestamp (UTC) | Y | Insertion timestamp. Set by database default. | now() |
| created_by | uuid | Y | FK → users.id of the actor who created the record. System events use the well-known SYSTEM user id. | — |
| updated_at | timestamp (UTC) | Y | Last mutation timestamp. Set by database trigger on every UPDATE. | now() |
| updated_by | uuid | Y | FK → users.id of the actor who last mutated the record. | — |
| deleted_at | timestamp (UTC) | N | Soft-delete timestamp. NULL means active. Hard delete blocked at database layer. | NULL |
| deleted_by | uuid | N | FK → users.id of the actor who soft-deleted the record. | NULL |
| darwinbox_source_id | string(64) | N | Source-system identifier from Darwinbox. Populated on migrated rows; NULL for natively created records. Indexed. | NULL |

## 4.2 Tenancy & Organisation Entities

### 4.2.1 tenants

Top-level multi-tenant container. One row per customer organisation. Created by Platform Super Admin at provisioning.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| tenant_name | string(200) | Y | Legal name of the organisation. | — |
| display_name | string(60) | Y | Short name for UI headers and notifications. | — |
| logo_url | string(500) | N | PNG/JPG, max 2MB, recommended 300×100 px. | NULL |
| registration_number | string(50) | N | CIN or equivalent. | NULL |
| company_pan | string(10) | N | Employer PAN (10-char alphanumeric). | NULL |
| registered_address | text | N | Multi-line address. | NULL |
| deployment_model | enum | Y | STANDALONE · MULTI_TENANT_SAAS · GROUP_COMPANY. Set at provisioning. Upgradeable through configuration only — no data migration required. | STANDALONE |
| industry_segment | enum | Y | IT_SERVICES (Phase 1 target) · BFSI · MANUFACTURING · RETAIL · HEALTHCARE. Locked at provisioning. Drives default cascade. | IT_SERVICES |
| primary_geography | enum | Y | INDIA (Phase 1 target). Locked at provisioning. Drives tax slabs, social security, labour law defaults. | INDIA |
| financial_year_start_month | integer | Y | Month number 1-12. Locked to 4 (April) for Indian entities. | 4 |
| calendar_week_start_day | enum | Y | MONDAY · SUNDAY. | MONDAY |
| working_days_per_week | integer | Y | 5 or 6. Overridable per location. | 5 |
| currency | string(3) | Y | ISO 4217. INR for Phase 1. | INR |
| language | string(5) | Y | BCP 47. en-IN for Phase 1. | en-IN |
| data_residency_region | string(50) | Y | India home region with DR replica in second Indian region. | IN-1 |
| status | enum | Y | PROVISIONING · ACTIVE · SUSPENDED · DEPROVISIONED. | PROVISIONING |

