### 4.2.3 departments

Hierarchical department structure. Maximum depth of 9 levels supported in Phase 1. Departments roll up to top-level departments through parent_department_id. Each department can carry multiple head-role assignments distinct from the operational HOD.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| department_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| department_code | string(40) | Y | Unique within tenant. | — |
| department_name | string(200) | Y | Display name. | — |
| parent_department_id | uuid | N | FK → departments.id. NULL for top-level departments. Recursive depth capped at 9 levels. | NULL |
| entity_id | uuid | Y | FK → entities.id (legal entity scope). | — |
| business_unit_id | uuid | N | FK → business_units.id (optional grouping above department). | NULL |
| project_allocated | string(120) | N | Services-business linkage to project. | NULL |
| top_department_flag | boolean | Y | TRUE if this is a level-1 department (computed from parent_department_id IS NULL). | FALSE |
| hod_user_id | uuid | N | Head of Department — operational lead. Drives approval routing and reporting hierarchy. | NULL |
| performance_hod_user_id | uuid | N | Distinct head responsible for performance reviews if different from operational HOD. | NULL |
| functional_head_user_id | uuid | N | Functional head (technical/practice leader). | NULL |
| head_hr_user_id | uuid | N | Dedicated HR head for this department (HRBP supervisor level). | NULL |
| group_hr_head_user_id | uuid | N | Group-level HR head (cross-department). | NULL |
| head_level_access | enum | N | Access scope grant for the head roles above: DEPARTMENT_ONLY · DEPARTMENT_AND_SUB · BUSINESS_UNIT · ENTITY · TENANT. | DEPARTMENT_AND_SUB |
| level_1_label | string(120) | N | Tenant-configurable display label for hierarchy level 1 (e.g. “Division”, “Vertical”). | “Department” |
| level_2_label | string(120) | N | Level 2 label (e.g. “Sub-Department”, “Practice”). | “Sub-Department” |
| level_3_label | string(120) | N | Level 3 label. | “Team” |
| level_4_label | string(120) | N | Level 4 label. | “Sub-Team” |
| level_5_label | string(120) | N | Level 5 label. | NULL |
| level_6_label | string(120) | N | Level 6 label. | NULL |
| level_7_label | string(120) | N | Level 7 label. | NULL |
| level_8_label | string(120) | N | Level 8 label. | NULL |
| level_9_label | string(120) | N | Level 9 label. | NULL |
| capability_tag | string(120) | N | Optional capability classification (e.g. “Engineering”, “Operations”). | NULL |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

*Relationships: Self-referencing via parent_department_id. Many-to-one with entities. Referenced by employment_history.department_id. The five head-role FKs (hod, performance_hod, functional_head, head_hr, group_hr_head) all link to users.id and are scoped by head_level_access for permission resolution.*

**Constraints:**

- Cycle prevention enforced on parent_department_id (no department can be its own ancestor).

- Hierarchy depth capped at 9; deeper inserts rejected with validation error.

- Department codes immutable post-creation; renames affect display name only.

