## 4.5 Leave Management Entities (M04)

### 4.5.1 leave_types

Master catalogue of leave types. Phase 1 ships with the migrated Darwinbox set: SL (Sick Leave), PL (Privilege Leave), PL_CC (Contract/Consultant PL), WWC (Working Women with Child), WL (Wedding Leave), PATL (Paternity Leave), ML (Maternity Leave), ADL (Adoption Leave), MCL (Miscarriage Leave), SPL (Special Leave), SBL (Sabbatical Leave), OH_*_26 (Optional Holidays per location/BU), Unpaid/LOP.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| leave_code | string(20) | Y | Unique within tenant. | — |
| leave_name | string(120) | Y | Display name. | — |
| category | enum | Y | PAID · UNPAID · OPTIONAL_HOLIDAY · SABBATICAL · SPECIAL. | PAID |
| credit_basis | enum | Y | ACCRUAL · ANNUAL_CREDIT · CONTINUOUS_CYCLE_PER_EVENT · CONTINUOUS_CYCLE_ONCE_PER_TENURE · ON_DEMAND_CREDITED · NA. | — |
| accrual_frequency | enum | N | QUARTERLY · MONTHLY · ANNUAL · NA. | NA |
| accrual_point | enum | N | BEGIN_OF_PERIOD · END_OF_PERIOD · YEAR_START · ON_APPLICATION · NA. | NA |
| pro_rata_on_join | boolean | Y | Whether new joiners receive pro-rated balance. | TRUE |
| carry_forward_enabled | boolean | Y | Whether unused balance carries to next year. | FALSE |
| carry_forward_cap_days | integer | N | Max days that can be carried forward. | NULL |
| encashable | boolean | Y | Whether the leave type is eligible for FnF encashment. | FALSE |
| encashment_formula | string(200) | N | e.g. “basic_pay / 30 × days”. | NULL |
| half_day_allowed | boolean | Y | Whether half-day applications are accepted. | FALSE |
| attachment_required_after_days | integer | N | After this many days, document attachment is mandatory. | NULL |
| min_advance_notice_days | integer | Y | Minimum days between application date and leave start date. | 0 |
| max_future_dated_days | integer | Y | Max days into the future an application can be raised. | 0 |
| max_past_dated_days | integer | Y | Max days in the past an application can cover (subject to global toggle). | 31 |
| visible_during_probation | boolean | Y | Platform-enforced — not configurable per leave type at runtime. | FALSE |
| applicable_during_probation | boolean | Y | Platform-enforced. | FALSE |
| visible_during_notice | boolean | Y | Platform-enforced. | FALSE |
| applicable_during_notice | boolean | Y | Platform-enforced. | FALSE |
| approval_flow_stages | integer | Y | 1 = standard single-flow. 2 = mandatory two-stage (ML, ADL, MCL, SPL, SBL). | 1 |
| gender_filter | enum | N | ALL · MALE_ONLY · FEMALE_ONLY. | ALL |
| marital_status_filter | json array | N | Array of allowed marital statuses. e.g. [“MARRIED”, “DIVORCED”]. | [] |
| religion_filter | json array | N | Optional eligibility filter restricting the leave type to specific religions (e.g. festival leave). Available but currently unused (all leave types = none). | [] |
| youngest_child_applicability | json object | N | Optional eligibility filter gating the leave type by the employee’s youngest child: enabled flag, optional nationality (is/not list), consider-future-DOB flag, and an age-range block (from / to / type / age-basis) with a max-leave-per-range cap. Used by WWC, Paternity and Adoption leave in the current config. NULL = no child-based gating. | NULL |
| employment_type_filter | json array | N | Array of allowed employment types. | [] |
| assignment_framework_id | uuid | Y | FK → assignment_rules.id (§4.2.17). The Assignment Framework rule that targets the population this leave policy applies to (replaces the former UAG binding). Plus optional group_company scope. Entitlement frameworks are configured mutually exclusive by employment type — see resolution rule (§4.5). | — |
| lifetime_cap | integer | N | e.g. WL = 1 per tenure. | NULL |
| once_per_event_cap | integer | N | e.g. ML per Maternity Benefit Act. | NULL |
| clubbing_restricted_with | json array | N | Array of leave_codes that cannot be clubbed with this type. | [] |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

**Sample data:**

| **leave_code** | **leave_name** | **credit_basis** | **encashable** | **approval_flow_stages** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| SL | Sick Leave | ACCRUAL (quarterly) | FALSE | 1 |
| PL | Privilege Leave | ACCRUAL (quarterly) | TRUE (HR Admin) | 1 |
| ML | Maternity Leave | CONTINUOUS_CYCLE_PER_EVENT | FALSE | 2 |

Half-day sessions. When a leave type’s application unit permits half-day, the apply-leave form offers a First half (morning) / Second half (afternoon) choice via half_day_sessions (BOTH · FIRST_ONLY · SECOND_ONLY · NONE). Each half deducts 0.5 day; the worked session is preserved for attendance.

### 4.5.2 leave_policies

Per-grade or per-employee-group leave entitlement mapping. Links leave types to specific entitlements (e.g. 15 days SL/year for Grade B1).

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| policy_name | string(120) | Y | e.g. “Standard Full-Time Policy”. | — |
| leave_type_id | uuid | Y | FK → leave_types.id. | — |
| grade_id | uuid | N | FK → grades.id. NULL means applies to all grades. | NULL |
| employment_type_filter | json array | N | Array of employment types. | [] |
| annual_entitlement_days | decimal(5,2) | Y | Days per year. e.g. 12.00 SL, 24.00 PL. | — |
| accrual_amount_per_period | decimal(5,2) | N | e.g. 3.00 SL per quarter. | NULL |
| effective_from | date | Y | Policy version start. | — |
| effective_to | date | N | Policy version end. NULL means current. | NULL |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

**Sample data:**

| **policy_name** | **leave_type** | **annual_entitlement_days** | **accrual_amount_per_period** |
