### 4.5.6 holiday_calendars (calendar master)

Holiday calendar / optional-holiday set assigned via the Assignment Framework (§4.2.17). Optional Holiday is treated as a leave type: each optional-holiday policy is tagged to a framework rule (typically scoped by project and/or work location, e.g. “Project A”, “Group Company 1 + Mumbai”). Frameworks are configured to be mutually exclusive so each employee resolves to exactly one optional-holiday policy; the “Group Company + location” frameworks are maintained manually as the default for employees not on a project-specific calendar. The per-policy Maximum-per-year value is the cap. Mandatory and National holidays are tagged by location / work area (per the holiday master). UAG plays no role in holiday assignment.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| calendar_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| calendar_name | string(160) | Y | e.g. “Mumbai – Project A”, “Mumbai – Project B”, “Hyderabad – General”. | — |
| calendar_code | string(40) | Y | Unique within tenant. | — |
| calendar_year | integer | N | Calendar year this set applies to; NULL = perennial. | NULL |
| scope_type | enum | Y | CITY · LOCATION · CLIENT_PROJECT · UAG · TENANT. Describes what the calendar represents (informational). | CLIENT_PROJECT |
| location_label_id | uuid | N | FK → locations.id. Descriptive label ONLY — non-unique; multiple calendars may share the same location. Does not drive calendar selection. | NULL |
| served_uag_ids | array(uuid) | N | FK → assignment_rules.id. The Assignment Framework rule that targets the population for this holiday/optional-holiday set. Frameworks are configured mutually exclusive (see resolution rule). | [] |
| is_default | boolean | Y | One default calendar per tenant for employees whose UAG has no calendar set. | FALSE |
| description | string(500) | N | Free text. | NULL |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

Sample data — note Mumbai appears on three rows (multiple calendars, same location):

| **calendar_name** | **scope_type** | **location_label** | **served UAGs** | **# holidays** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Mumbai – Project A | CLIENT_PROJECT | Mumbai (MUM-EUR) | ProjA-Mumbai | 11 |
| Mumbai – Project B | CLIENT_PROJECT | Mumbai (MUM-EUR) | Project B-Mumbai | 12 |
| Mumbai – General Staff | CITY | Mumbai (MUM-EUR) | Mumbai-General | 14 |
| Hyderabad – General | CITY | Hyderabad (HYD-QC) | Hyd-General | 13 |
| Default (tenant) | TENANT | — | fallback | 10 |

*Relationships: One holiday_calendars row owns many holiday_calendar entries (§4.5.6.1) via holiday_calendar.calendar_id, and may be referenced by many UAGs (§4.2.7). The location_label_id is informational and intentionally non-unique — several calendars may carry the same location. National holidays are flagged on the entries and surface in every employee’s resolved list regardless of calendar.*

### 4.5.6.1 holiday_calendar (per-holiday entries)

Per-holiday entry with recurring-rule support. Static one-off holidays and recurring (e.g. New Year’s Day annually, second Saturday of every month) supported.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| calendar_id | uuid | Y | FK → holiday_calendars.id (§4.5.6). The named calendar this holiday entry belongs to. A holiday may be added to multiple calendars (one entry per calendar, or shared by reference per implementation). | — |
| holiday_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| holiday_name | string(200) | Y | Display name. | — |
| holiday_code | string(40) | Y | Unique within tenant. | — |
| holiday_date | date | Y | Calendar date. For recurring, this is the first occurrence. | — |
| day_name | enum | Y | Computed: MON · TUE · etc. | computed |
| repeat_next_year | boolean | Y | Whether to auto-create for next year. | FALSE |
| holiday_type | enum | Y | MANDATORY · OPTIONAL · NATIONAL. | MANDATORY |
| applicable_locations | array(uuid) | Y | FK list → locations.id. Empty = all locations. | [] |
| work_area_code_filter | array(string) | N | Filter by work_area_code. | [] |
| applicable_to_uag_id | uuid | N | Override via assignment if needed. | NULL |
| is_recurring | boolean | Y | TRUE for recurring patterns. | FALSE |
| recurring_holiday_type | enum | N | STATIC_DATE · DAY_OF_MONTH. Required if is_recurring=TRUE. | NULL |
| static_month | integer | N | If STATIC_DATE: month (1-12). | NULL |
| static_date | integer | N | If STATIC_DATE: day of month (1-31). | NULL |
| occurrence | enum | N | If DAY_OF_MONTH: FIRST · SECOND · THIRD · FOURTH · LAST. | NULL |
| occurrence_month | integer | N | If DAY_OF_MONTH: month (1-12). | NULL |
| occurrence_day | enum | N | If DAY_OF_MONTH: SUN · MON · TUE · WED · THU · FRI · SAT. | NULL |
| holiday_starts_from_year | integer | N | If recurring: first year of recurrence. | NULL |
| additional_configurations | jsonb | N | Tenant-specific extras (e.g. half-day flag, regional variants). | NULL |
| is_half_day | boolean | Y | Half-day holiday support. | FALSE |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

*Relationships: Each entry belongs to one holiday_calendars row (§4.5.6) via calendar_id. applicable_locations / work_area_code_filter remain available for finer location scoping WITHIN a calendar but do not select the calendar (the UAG does). National-type entries surface in every employee’s resolved list. See the holiday-resolution rule below.*

Leave & holiday resolution (configuration rule, not an engine). (a) Leave entitlement: leave policies are assigned via the Assignment Framework (§4.2.17). Entitlement frameworks are mutually exclusive by employment type (e.g. Full-Time & Associate vs Contract & Consultant), so an employee resolves to exactly one entitlement policy per leave type — no precedence engine is required. (b) Optional holidays: treated as a leave type, also framework-assigned. Optional-holiday frameworks are configured mutually exclusive (typically by project, with “Group Company + location” frameworks maintained manually as the default), so an employee resolves to exactly one optional-holiday policy; its per-policy Maximum-per-year value is the cap. (c) Mandatory / National holidays are applied by location / work area and surface for all in-scope employees. The system does NOT compute a union, fallback, or precedence — mutual exclusivity is a configuration responsibility. Risk note: because exclusivity is manual, default (“Group Company + location”) frameworks must exclude project-specific populations; a periodic disjointness audit (or Include/Exclude on the default framework) is recommended. If overlapping frameworks are ever introduced, a precedence rule or tenant-level optional-holiday ceiling must be defined.

### 4.5.7 leave_platform_settings

Tenant-level Leave Management platform configuration. Singleton entity (one row per tenant). Drives global defaults that policies can override.

Settings are organised into 30+ functional clusters. Each cluster is a logical grouping of related toggles.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| platform_setting_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| tenant_id | uuid | Y | FK → tenants.id. Unique (one row per tenant). | — |

**Cluster 1 — Application Rules:**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| allow_previous_year_applications | boolean | Y | Permit applying leave for dates in the previous calendar year. | FALSE |
| make_reason_mandatory | boolean | Y | Require employee to select a reason from leave_reasons_master. | TRUE |
| make_message_mandatory | boolean | Y | Require free-text message on application. | FALSE |
| make_rejection_reason_mandatory | boolean | Y | Approver must select rejection reason. | TRUE |
| display_pay_rate_on_application | boolean | Y | Show calculated pay impact to applicant. | FALSE |
| disable_comp_off_display | boolean | Y | Hide comp-off balance from employee view. | FALSE |

**Cluster 2 — Revocation Rules:**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
