### 4.5.9 leave_tenure_brackets

Per-leave-type tenure-bracketed allotment rules. Replaces a free-form schedule with structured rows.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| tenure_bracket_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| leave_type_id | uuid | Y | FK → leave_types.id. | — |
| use_group_date_of_joining | boolean | Y | Calculate tenure from group_date_of_joining vs date_of_joining. | TRUE |
| from_year | integer | Y | Inclusive lower bound (in years of service). | — |
| to_year | integer | Y | Inclusive upper bound. | — |
| number_of_leaves | numeric(6,2) | Y | Allotment for this bracket. | — |
| max_availed_per_year | numeric(6,2) | N | Cap on availment per year within bracket. | NULL |
| sort_order | integer | Y | Bracket sequence. | 1 |

*Relationships: Many-to-one with leave_types. Composite logic: tenure brackets evaluated in sort_order, first match wins.*

### 4.5.10 leave_date_specific_rules

Date-specific eligibility rules — leave applications tied to life events (Marriage, Birth of Child, Bereavement, etc.).

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| date_specific_rule_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| leave_type_id | uuid | Y | FK → leave_types.id. | — |
| dependent_standard | enum | Y | EMPLOYEE_LIFE_EVENT · DEPENDENT_LIFE_EVENT · CUSTOM_DATES. | — |
| relation | enum | N | SELF · SPOUSE · CHILD · PARENT · SIBLING · GRANDPARENT · IN_LAW. Required if DEPENDENT_LIFE_EVENT. | NULL |
| event_type | enum | N | MARRIAGE · CHILD_BIRTH · ADOPTION · DEATH · ILLNESS · OTHER. | NULL |
| max_leave_allowed | numeric(6,2) | Y | Cap on leave for this event. | — |
| custom_event_name | string(200) | N | Custom dated event name if dependent_standard = CUSTOM_DATES. | NULL |
| custom_date | date | N | Specific date for custom event. | NULL |
| validity_window_days_before | integer | N | Days before event date that leave can be applied. | 7 |
| validity_window_days_after | integer | N | Days after event date that leave can be applied. | 30 |

*Relationships: Many-to-one with leave_types.*

