## 4.6 Attendance Entities (M05)

### 4.6.1 shifts

Shift master with expanded behavioural toggles. Linked to weekly_off_patterns master.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| shift_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| shift_name | string(120) | Y | Display name. | — |
| shift_code | string(40) | Y | Unique within tenant. | — |
| description | string(500) | N | Free text. | NULL |
| assignment_type | enum | Y | UAG · GROUP_COMPANY · ALL. | UAG |
| assignment_framework | string(120) | N | Framework reference. | NULL |
| group_company_id | uuid | N | FK → entities.id. | NULL |
| applicable_to_uag_id | uuid | N | FK → assignment_rules.id. | NULL |
| start_time | time | Y | Shift start. | — |
| end_time | time | Y | Shift end. | — |
| is_overnight_shift | boolean | Y | TRUE if end_time < start_time (crosses midnight). | computed |
| weekly_off_pattern_id | uuid | N | FK → weekly_off_patterns.id (new — replaces inline weekly off array). | NULL |
| show_for_shift_change_request | boolean | Y | Available in shift-change requests. | TRUE |
| attendance_policy_id | uuid | N | FK → attendance_policies.id. | NULL |
| is_wfh_shift | boolean | Y | Marks WFH-eligible shift. | FALSE |
| do_not_generate_ot_on_weekday | boolean | Y | Suppress OT on weekdays. | FALSE |
| do_not_generate_ot_on_weekly_off | boolean | Y | Suppress OT on W-Off. | FALSE |
| do_not_generate_ot_on_holiday | boolean | Y | Suppress OT on holidays. | FALSE |
| timezone_for_clockin_warning | string(60) | N | IANA timezone for “missed punch” alerts. | NULL |
| is_null_shift | boolean | Y | Null shift — no expected punches. | FALSE |
| ignore_punches_on_null_shift | boolean | Y | If null shift, ignore any punches recorded. | FALSE |
| mapped_to_alternative_work_schedule | boolean | Y | Linked to AWS variant. | FALSE |
| alternative_work_schedule_ref | string(120) | N | Reference to AWS. | NULL |
| standard_working_hours_basis | enum | Y | DAILY · WEEKLY · CYCLE. | DAILY |
| standard_working_hours | numeric(4,2) | Y | Expected hours per basis unit. | 8.00 |
| is_standard_shift | boolean | Y | Marks this as the standard / default shift. | FALSE |
| leave_deduction_factor | numeric(4,2) | N | Multiplier when leave is deducted per shift hour. | 1.00 |
| ot_policy_id | uuid | N | FK → leave_compoff_policies.id (when OT generation needed). | NULL |
| break_policy_id | uuid | N | FK to break policy (separate entity, defined per tenant). | NULL |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

*Relationships: Many-to-one with weekly_off_patterns, attendance_policies, leave_compoff_policies, assignment_rules.*

### 4.6.2 attendance_policies

Attendance policy assignments. Phase 1 migrated set: ATPY_4 (All Employees primary), ATPY_5 (Probation), ATPY_1 (CEO). ATPY_2 excluded as test artefact.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| policy_code | string(20) | Y | ATPY_4 · ATPY_5 · ATPY_1. | — |
| policy_name | string(120) | Y |  | — |
| mark_attendance_based_on | enum | Y | BOTH_IN_AND_OUT (default — single punch counts as incomplete) · IN_ONLY · OUT_ONLY. | BOTH_IN_AND_OUT |
| back_dating_window_days | integer | Y | Max past days for regularisation and Out Duty (32 for ATPY_4/5; 30 for ATPY_1). | 32 |
| monthly_regularisation_limit | integer | N | Max regularisation requests per calendar month (7 for ATPY_4/5; NULL for ATPY_1). | 7 |
| overtime_enabled | boolean | Y | Whether overtime tracking is enabled for this policy. | TRUE |
| absconding_threshold_calendar_days | integer | Y | Default 7. Configurable per tenant by Org Admin, per entity by HR Admin. | 7 |
| assignment_framework_id | uuid | Y | FK → assignment_rules.id (§4.2.17). Population this attendance policy applies to (Assignment Type = Assignment Framework │ Group Company wise). Replaces any UAG link. | — |
| optional_holiday_limit_days | int | N | Cap on optional holidays an employee under this policy may avail per year (ties to the optional-holiday leave type / holiday group). | NULL |
| buffer_before_after_shift | json | N | Allow buffer time before/after shift: enabled flag + pre-time and post-time (hours) used when matching punches to the shift. | NULL |
| roster_change_past_window_days | int | N | Restrict roster changes for past N days. | NULL |
| checkin_request_config | json | N | Check-in / clock-in request rules: allow from WFH / Out-Duty; allow for weekly-offs and holidays; auto approve/reject clock-in requests. (Clock-in cluster.) | {} |
| regularisation_request_config | json | N | Attendance-regularization request rules: enable; allow past-dated (with day limit); application limits; show shift/attendance info during application & approval; auto approve/reject; act-on-request basis. | {} |
| out_duty_request_config | json | N | Out-Duty request rules: enable; allow past dates (with day limit); show holiday/weekly-off info; auto approve/reject; act-on-request basis. | {} |
| shift_change_request_config | json | N | Shift-change request rules: enable; auto approve/reject; act-on-request basis. | {} |
| absence_leave_deduction | json | N | Leave deduction when marked absent: enable; deduct-from (which leave); full-day or half-day; enable deduction on days with half-day leave/holiday. | {} |
| work_duration_deduction_policy | json | N | Leave deduction by Total Work duration: minimum hours to count half-day / full-day; work-duration leave type used for the deduction. | {} |
| display_hide_flags | json | N | Per-policy display suppression on the attendance page (break duration, location, recorded clock-in/last-punch, final work duration, early-out, overtime, paid/unpaid break, short-leave). Each is an independent boolean. | {} |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

**Sample data:**

| **policy_code** | **policy_name** | **back_dating_window_days** | **monthly_regularisation_limit** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ATPY_4 | Attendance Policy - All Employees | 32 | 7 |
| ATPY_5 | Attendance P_Policy - On Probation | 32 | 7 |
| ATPY_1 | Attendance Policy CEO | 30 | NULL |

