### 4.7.6.1 bgv_checklist_master (BGV document checklist)

Master list of background-verification checks and the documents each requires. Drives the per-step verification statuses shown to HRBP / HR Admin / Onboarding Admin during onboarding (the BGV report upload & verification screen), and feeds bgv_packages. Tenant-configurable by Org Admin.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| checklist_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| check_name | string(120) | Y | e.g. Identity, Education, Prior employment, Criminal record, Address. | — |
| required_documents | json array | Y | Documents the check requires, e.g. [“Aadhaar”,“PAN”] or [“Relieving letter”,“Last 3 payslips”]. | [] |
| is_mandatory | boolean | Y | Whether the check is mandatory for the applicable population. | TRUE |
| applicable_to | enum | Y | ALL · EXPERIENCED_HIRES · FRESHERS · SPECIFIC_UAG. | ALL |
| applicable_uag_id | uuid | N | FK → user_assignment_groups.id when applicable_to = SPECIFIC_UAG. | NULL |
| default_verification_status | enum | Y | Initial status of this step on a new case: PENDING · IN_PROGRESS. | PENDING |
| sequence | integer | N | Display order on the verification screen. | NULL |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

*Relationships: referenced by bgv_packages (§4.7.6) when assembling a verification package, and by bgv_results (§4.7.7) which records the per-check outcome (Verified · In progress · Discrepancy · Unable to verify) and the uploaded third-party report. Org Admin maintains this master via the BGV document checklist screen.*

