## 4.8 Exits & Offboarding Entities (M03)

### 4.8.1 separation_policies

Configurable separation policy register. Voluntary, Involuntary, Retirement, Death, Transfer, Default categories. Each policy defines approval flow, notice period override, FnF behaviour.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| policy_name | string(120) | Y | e.g. “Voluntary - FT”. | — |
| category | enum | Y | VOLUNTARY · INVOLUNTARY · RETIREMENT · DEATH · TRANSFER · DEFAULT. | — |
| applicability_employment_types | json array | Y | Array of employment types. | [] |
| default_notice_period_days | integer | Y | Override of employment_history.notice_period_days for this policy. Calculated using working days per Org default. | 60 |
| approval_flow_id | uuid | Y | FK → workflows.id. Default: L1 Manager → HR Admin. | — |
| reviewer_stage_enabled | boolean | Y | Optional reviewer stage between L1 Manager and HR Admin. | FALSE |
| custom_final_approver_role_code | string(50) | N | Optional elevation (e.g. Business Head replaces HR Admin). | NULL |
| fnf_clearance_workflow_id | uuid | Y | FK → workflows.id. Parallel multi-department workflow. | — |
| on_notice_state_alias | string(50) | Y | Display label. e.g. “Serving Notice”. | Serving Notice |
| confidential_field_roles | json array | Y | Array of role codes that can view confidential separation fields. | [“hr_admin”, “offboarding_admin”, “hrbp”] |
| hide_from_l1_until_approval | boolean | Y | Whether L1 Manager sees the pending request before being formally routed. | FALSE |
| allow_past_dated_resignation | boolean | Y | Policy Details toggle — “Allow past date of resignation according to notice period”. When set, the resignation date may be back-dated within the notice-period rules (HR Admin per DE02). | TRUE |
| force_separate_on_lwd | boolean | Y | Policy Details toggle — “Force separate employee on LWD as per notice period”. When set, the employee is separated automatically on the computed LWD with no further manual step. | FALSE |
| restrict_lwd_on | string(50) | N | Process Details — “Restrict Last Working Day On”. Constrains the selectable LWD (e.g. payroll / attendance cycle boundary). | NULL |
| capture_resignation_lwd_recovery | boolean | Y | Process Details — “Capture Date of Resignation, Requested LWD, Recovery Days while raising separation”. Surfaces recovery-days (notice-shortfall) capture at initiation. | TRUE |
| block_until_revoke_approval_complete | boolean | Y | Process Details — “Do not proceed with the flow until the revoke approval process is completed”. | FALSE |
| default_approval_flow_on_revoke_id | uuid | N | FK → workflows.id. Process Details “Default Approval Flow On Revoke”; applied when an initiator row does not define its own revoke flow. | NULL |
| welcome_message | text | N | Banner step — optional rich-text welcome message shown to the separating employee on the separation surface. | NULL |
| status | enum | Y | ACTIVE · INACTIVE. | ACTIVE |

**Sample data:**

| **policy_name** | **category** | **default_notice_period_days** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Voluntary FT Standard | VOLUNTARY | 60 |
| Voluntary Contractor | VOLUNTARY | 30 |
| Retirement | RETIREMENT | 0 (calendar-driven) |

### 4.8.1a separation_policy_initiators

Initiation-and-approval rows for a separation policy (Process Details > Approval Flow Configuration). One row per permitted initiator; defines the initiation form, the approval flow on raise, and the approval flow on revoke.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| separation_policy_id | uuid | Y | FK → separation_policies.id. | — |
| display_order | integer | Y | Row order in the Approval Flow Configuration grid. | — |
| initiator_role | enum | Y | SELF · HR_TEAM · ADMIN. | — |
| action_form_id | uuid | Y | FK → forms.id. Initiation form (e.g. “Exit Initiation Form”). | — |
| exclude_capture | boolean | Y | “Exclude Capture” — suppress the resignation / LWD / recovery capture block for this initiator. | FALSE |
| exception | boolean | Y | “Exception” — route via the policy exception flow. | FALSE |
| approval_flow_id | uuid | Y | FK → workflows.id. Approval flow on raise (e.g. “Resignation…”). | — |
| approval_flow_on_revoke_id | uuid | N | FK → workflows.id. Per-row revoke flow; falls back to separation_policies.default_approval_flow_on_revoke_id. | NULL |
| confidential | boolean | Y | Mark this initiation row confidential. | FALSE |

**Sample data:**

| **initiator_role** | **action_form** | **approval_flow** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SELF | Exit Initiation Form | Resignation Approval Flow |
| HR_TEAM | Exit Initiation Form | Resignation Approval Flow |
| ADMIN | Exit Initiation Form | Resignation Approval Flow |

