### 4.8.3 fnf_clearances

[Prototype sync — June 2026] The FnF clearance set includes a Timesheet clearance gate (timesheet/attendance reconciliation, status clear/pending) in addition to manager, asset/IT, finance, facilities, attendance/LOP, leave-encashment, compliance/NDA and exit-interview gates. Each clearance stage carries a configurable per-item checklist (e.g., Facilities: ID/access card, parking sticker, locker key, corporate card, library card), each item independently markable clear/pending. Item lists are configured in the separation clearance checklist (HR Admin).

FnF clearance per department. Parallel multi-department workflow — all clearances must complete before FnF payroll settlement (Phase 2) can fire.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| separation_record_id | uuid | Y | FK → separation_records.id. | — |
| department | enum | Y | Ten-stage parallel clearance set (one row per stage): MANAGER_HANDOVER (E1) · ASSET_RETURN (E2) · IT_ACCESS_REVOCATION (E3) · FINANCE (E4) · FACILITIES (E5) · ATTENDANCE_LOP (E6) · LEAVE_ENCASHMENT (E7) · COMPLIANCE_NDA (E8) · EXIT_INTERVIEW (E9) · STATUTORY (E10, Phase 2). See §5.3 Part E for stage owners, SLAs, and mandatory flags. | — |
| assigned_to_user_id | uuid | Y | FK → users.id. | — |
| status | enum | Y | PENDING · IN_PROGRESS · CLEARED · BLOCKED. | PENDING |
| cleared_at | timestamp (UTC) | N |  | NULL |
| clearance_notes | text | N |  | NULL |

**Sample data:**

| **separation_record (employee)** | **department** | **status** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| PSI000457 | IT | CLEARED |
| PSI000457 | FINANCE | CLEARED |
| PSI000457 | HR | IN_PROGRESS |

