*Relationships: One-to-many with candidates (via candidate.applied_requisition_id), offers. Many-to-one with departments, designations, entities, hiring_lead_user, etc.*

### 4.9.2 jobs

A Job is the public-facing posting and configuration container (Create Job, FR-M08-011). A Requisition (FR-M08-012) funds one or more Positions (§4.9.13); a Job advertises positions drawn from one or more requisitions. Per-channel posting and scheduling are owned by job_postings (§4.9.16). The former job_board_codes, published_at, and expires_at fields on this entity have been removed in favour of job_postings.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| requisition_id | uuid | Y | FK → requisitions.id. | — |
| job_title | string(200) | Y | Public-facing title. | — |
| job_description | text | Y | Public-facing description. | — |
| ijp_enabled | boolean | Y | Internal Job Posting flag. | FALSE |
| ijp_eligibility_rules | json | N | Rules for IJP visibility (min tenure, departments, etc.). | {} |
| status | enum | Y | DRAFT · PUBLISHED · EXPIRED · CLOSED. | DRAFT |

**Sample data:**

| **job_title** | **status** |
| --- | --- |
| Senior Backend Engineer | PUBLISHED |
| HR Business Partner | PUBLISHED |
| Engineering Manager | PUBLISHED |

