| differently_abled | enum | N | YES · NO. | NULL |
| approver_cc_user_ids | json array | N | CC users on the approval email. | [] |
| approver_cc_roles | json array | N | CC roles: MYSELF · HIRING_LEAD · ADMIN. | [] |
| trigger_custom_exception_flow | boolean | Y | Approval routes via the custom exception flow. | FALSE |
| approver_attachment_ids | json array | N | Approver-specific attachments. | [] |
| candidate_attachment_ids | json array | N | Candidate-specific attachments. | [] |

**Status mapping (offers). **offer_lifecycle_state (canonical, §4.9.18) maps to the §4.9.5 sub-statuses as follows: PENDING_FOR_APPROVAL → approval_status PENDING_APPROVAL; APPROVED_TO_SHARE_WITH_CANDIDATE → approval_status APPROVED with candidate_acceptance_status NOT_SENT; PENDING_WITH_CANDIDATE → candidate_acceptance_status SENT or VIEWED; ACCEPTED_TO_PENDING_LIST and IN_PENDING_LIST → candidate_acceptance_status ACCEPTED; EMPLOYEE_MOVEMENT_INITIATED, EMPLOYEE_MOVEMENT_APPROVED and COMPLETED → post-acceptance conversion (no acceptance-status change); REJECTED → approval_status REJECTED or candidate_acceptance_status REJECTED; EXPIRED → candidate_acceptance_status EXPIRED. The §8.7a state machine is authoritative for transitions.

## 4.10 Performance Management Entities (M09)

### 4.10.1 goal_plans

OKR goal plans bound to appraisal periods. Each employee has **at most one ACTIVE goal plan at any time** — the plan covering the current appraisal period. The platform operates **12 monthly goal cycles and 12 monthly review cycles at the tenant level** (Jan-cohort, Feb-cohort, …, Dec-cohort); each employee is assigned to one cohort derived from their anchor date using a 15th-of-month cutoff (anchor day ≤ 15 → that month; > 15 → next month; anchor = date of joining for the first plan, previous plan end + 1 day thereafter), and the plan period aligns to the 1st of that cohort month. Appraisal period is defined per employee by Performance Admin or HR Admin (joint authority, configurable in the M09 admin surface). The first plan’s start date defaults to the employee’s date of joining; subsequent plans’ start dates default to the day after the previous plan’s end date. Plan duration defaults to 12 months but is editable per employee (supports off-cycle and accelerated appraisal periods). The **next** goal plan auto-opens in DRAFT state for the employee **one month before the current plan’s plan_end_date**, giving the employee a one-month window to draft and submit the next cycle’s goals before their current plan transitions to IN_REVIEW. On plan_end_date, the current plan transitions IN_REVIEW; once the review cycle closes (CLOSED), the next plan transitions from DRAFT to ACTIVE.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| employee_id | uuid | Y | FK → employees.id. | — |
| plan_start_date | date | Y | First day of the plan window. **Defaults to the 1st of the derived monthly_cohort month** (cohort derived from the anchor date via the 15th cutoff — see monthly_cohort). Anchor = date_of_joining (first plan) or previous plan_end_date + 1 day (subsequent plans). Editable by Performance Admin or HR Admin at plan creation. | — |
| plan_end_date | date | Y | Last day of the plan window. Default = plan_start_date + 12 months; editable by Performance Admin or HR Admin (M09 admin surface) at plan creation. Must be ≥ plan_start_date. | — |
| period_set_by_user_id | uuid | Y | FK → users.id. Performance Admin or HR Admin who set or last edited the appraisal period dates. | — |
| period_set_at | timestamp (UTC) | Y | When the appraisal period dates were set or last edited. | — |
| plan_name | string(120) | N | Optional label. | NULL |
| assignment_source | enum | Y | How the plan row was created: CRON · MANUAL_SINGLE · MANUAL_BULK · OVERRIDE. | CRON |
| assignment_reason | enum | N | For manual assignments: NEW_HIRE · OFF_CYCLE · ACCELERATED · PIP · CORRECTION · OTHER. NULL for CRON. | NULL |
| monthly_cohort | enum | Y | Tenant-level monthly cohort: JAN…DEC. Determines which of the 12 monthly goal/review cycles this plan rolls into. **Default derived from the anchor date via a 15th-of-month cutoff** — anchor day ≤ 15 → cohort = anchor month; anchor day > 15 → cohort = next month. Anchor date = date_of_joining (first plan) or previous plan_end_date + 1 day (subsequent plans). Editable by Performance Admin or HR Admin. | derived |
| draft_open_date | date | Y | Computed date when the plan transitions from PENDING to DRAFT (employee can begin editing). Computed as plan_start_date − 30 days. For the first plan, draft_open_date = plan_start_date − 30 days OR date_of_joining (whichever is later). | computed |
| state | enum | Y | PENDING · DRAFT · ACTIVE · IN_REVIEW · CLOSED · CANCELLED. Created in PENDING; transitions to DRAFT 30 days before plan_start_date. | PENDING |
| review_initiation_source | enum | Y | How the ACTIVE — IN_REVIEW transition was triggered: CALENDAR (auto on plan_end_date) · ADMIN_MANUAL (FR-M09-030) · SEPARATION (FR-M09-024). | CALENDAR |
| goal_methodology | enum | Y | OKR. Platform-fixed for Phase 1. | OKR |
| minimum_goals_required | integer | Y | Default 2 per migrated config. | 2 |
| maximum_goals_allowed | integer | N | NULL = no upper limit. | NULL |
| approved_by_user_id | uuid | N | FK → users.id. L1 Manager approval required. | NULL |
| approved_at | timestamp (UTC) | N |  | NULL |

**Sample data:**

| **employee** | **plan_start_date** | **plan_end_date** | **state** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| PSI000123 | 2026-06-01 | 2027-05-31 | ACTIVE |
| PSI000457 | 2026-03-01 | 2027-02-28 | ACTIVE |
| PSI000789 | 2025-11-01 | 2026-10-31 | IN_REVIEW |

### 4.10.2 goals

Goals (Objectives). Sub-goals (Key Results) are configured as a separate child table — sub-goals enabled per migrated config.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| goal_plan_id | uuid | Y | FK → goal_plans.id. | — |
| goal_name | string(200) | Y | Mandatory per goal field config. | — |
| goal_description | text | Y | Mandatory. Detailed context: why this goal matters, dependencies, expected outcome. | — |
| goal_measurement | text | Y | **Measurement criteria** — how the goal’s achievement will be assessed. Specifies the KPI, metric formula, data source, frequency, and acceptance threshold. Mandatory; validated at goal save to be ≥ 20 characters. Shown alongside goal_description on the appraisal review screen. | — |
| goal_achievement_pct | decimal(5,2) | Y | 0–100. Entered manually per migrated config (auto-calculate = No). | 0 |
| goal_weightage | decimal(5,2) | Y | Weight in plan. Min/max not enforced per migrated config. | — |
| scorecard_pillar | string(120) | Y | e.g. “Customer” · “People” · “Operations” · “Financial”. | — |
| parent_goal_id | uuid | N | FK → goals.id (self-reference for sub-goals/KRs). | NULL |
| approval_state | enum | Y | DRAFT · PENDING_APPROVAL · APPROVED · REJECTED. Governs whether a goal is on the plan. Terminates at APPROVED. | DRAFT |
| approved_by_user_id | uuid | N | L1 Manager. | NULL |

**Sample data:**

| **goal_name** | **goal_measurement** | **goal_weightage** | **scorecard_pillar** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Migrate payment service to microservices | Service decomposition complete · ≥ 95% test coverage on new modules · zero P0 incidents post-cutover · measured at end-of-quarter via deployment manifest + incident log | 30 | Operations |
| Mentor 2 junior engineers to Lead level | 2 engineers reach Lead-eligible status by Q4 · measured via promotion-readiness scorecard reviewed in calibration | 20 | People |
| Reduce API p95 latency by 30% | p95 latency baseline 800ms → target 560ms · measured weekly via Datadog dashboard · 4-week rolling average | 25 | Customer |

### 4.10.3 review_cycles

Monthly review cycles — the platform maintains **12 monthly review cycles per fiscal year** at the tenant level (JAN through DEC cohorts). Each goal_plan is bound to one of the 12 monthly cohorts via goal_plans.monthly_cohort. When a goal_plan transitions to IN_REVIEW on plan_end_date, it slots into the corresponding monthly review_cycle for that month. Each review_cycle drives stage progression through Self → L1 Evaluator → Calibration → Acknowledgement for all goal_plans rolled into it.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| cycle_name | string(120) | Y | e.g. “May 2026 Review Cycle”. | — |
| monthly_cohort | enum | Y | JAN · FEB · MAR · APR · MAY · JUN · JUL · AUG · SEP · OCT · NOV · DEC. Links this cycle to all goal_plans with matching monthly_cohort. | — |
| fiscal_year | string(8) | Y | e.g. “FY26” — fiscal year this cycle belongs to. | — |
| cycle_start_date | date | Y |  | — |
| cycle_end_date | date | Y |  | — |
| state | enum | Y | PLANNED · OPEN · IN_PROGRESS · CALIBRATION · CLOSED. | PLANNED |
| initiated_by_user_id | uuid | Y | FK → users.id. Performance Admin. | — |
| rating_scale_id | uuid | Y | FK → rating_scales.id. | — |

**Sample data:**

| **cycle_name** | **monthly_cohort** | **fiscal_year** | **cycle_start_date** | **cycle_end_date** | **state** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| April 2026 Review | APR | FY27 | 2026-04-01 | 2026-04-30 | CLOSED |
| May 2026 Review | MAY | FY27 | 2026-05-01 | 2026-05-31 | IN_PROGRESS |
| June 2026 Review | JUN | FY27 | 2026-06-01 | 2026-06-30 | PLANNED |
| July 2026 Review | JUL | FY27 | 2026-07-01 | 2026-07-31 | PLANNED |
| … (12 cycles per fiscal year) |  |  |  |  |  |

### 4.10.4 review_records

Per-employee, per-cycle review record. Holds draft and published ratings.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| review_cycle_id | uuid | Y | FK → review_cycles.id. | — |
| employee_id | uuid | Y | FK → employees.id. | — |
| goal_plan_id | uuid | Y | FK → goal_plans.id. Plan in review. | — |
| self_review_submitted_at | timestamp (UTC) | N |  | NULL |
| self_review_responses | json | N |  | {} |
| l1_review_submitted_at | timestamp (UTC) | N |  | NULL |
| l1_reviewer_user_id | uuid | N |  | NULL |
| l1_review_responses | json | N |  | {} |
| draft_rating | string(20) | N | Restricted access — Reviewer only (per RBAC §3.8). No entitlement grant can expose pre-publish. | NULL |
| calibration_rating | string(20) | N | Set post-calibration moderation. | NULL |
| published_rating | string(20) | N | Final rating visible to employee, manager, HR Admin, Skip-level. | NULL |
| published_at | timestamp (UTC) | N |  | NULL |
| acknowledgement_state | enum | Y | PENDING · ACKNOWLEDGED · DECLINED. | PENDING |
| review_hold | boolean | Y | TRUE while the review is paused by an admin (FR-M09-030); blocks stage actions and freezes SLA clocks. | FALSE |
| hold_reason | string(500) | N | Mandatory when review_hold is set TRUE; shown to the employee and L1 Manager. | NULL |
| held_by_user_id | uuid | N | Admin who paused the review. | NULL |
| held_at | timestamp (UTC) | N | When the review was paused. | NULL |
| resumed_by_user_id | uuid | N | Admin who resumed the review. | NULL |
| resumed_at | timestamp (UTC) | N | When the review was resumed; SLA clocks restart from their remaining balance. | NULL |
| acknowledged_at | timestamp (UTC) | N |  | NULL |

**Sample data:**

| **employee** | **cycle** | **published_rating** | **ack_state** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| PSI000123 | April 2026 | Exceeds Expectations | ACKNOWLEDGED |
| PSI000457 | April 2026 | Meets Expectations | ACKNOWLEDGED |
| PSI000789 | May 2026 | — | PENDING |

