### 4.10.7 manager_feedback

Continuous feedback entries from L1 Manager to direct reportees (FR-M09-026). Independent of formal review-cycle stages. Persistent across appraisal cycles.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | — |
| employee_id | uuid | Y | FK → employees.id. Reportee receiving the feedback. | — |
| author_user_id | uuid | Y | FK → users.id. L1 Manager creating the feedback. | — |
| goal_plan_id | uuid | Y | FK → goal_plans.id. The ACTIVE plan at time of creation. | — |
| feedback_text | string(4000) | Y | The feedback content. | — |
| feedback_category | enum | Y | POSITIVE · CONSTRUCTIVE · COACHING · RECOGNITION. | — |
| visibility | enum | Y | EMPLOYEE_VISIBLE · HRBP_ONLY. Default EMPLOYEE_VISIBLE. | EMPLOYEE_VISIBLE |
| created_at | timestamp (UTC) | Y | Auto-set on creation. | NOW |
| updated_at | timestamp (UTC) | Y | Auto-set on creation; updated on edit (within 24h window only). | NOW |
| is_edited | boolean | Y | TRUE if edited after initial creation. | FALSE |
| created_during_review | boolean | Y | TRUE if created after the goal_plan transitioned to IN_REVIEW. | FALSE |

**Sample data:**

| **employee** | **author** | **category** | **visibility** | **created** | **feedback_text (excerpt)** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Rohan Mehta | Manager One (L1) | COACHING | EMPLOYEE_VISIBLE | 12 May 2026 | “Great work on the API redesign. For the next sprint, try to include the perf testing earlier…” |
| Employee One | Manager One (L1) | RECOGNITION | EMPLOYEE_VISIBLE | 8 May 2026 | “The client demo went exceptionally well — thank you for putting in the extra hours.” |
| Akash Rao | Manager One (L1) | CONSTRUCTIVE | HRBP_ONLY | 2 May 2026 | “On probation track — concerns around pacing. HRBP to align before the next review conversation.” |

### 4.10.8 feedback_responses

Employee responses to L1 Manager feedback (FR-M09-027). Two-way thread per feedback entry.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Validation / Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | — |
| feedback_id | uuid | Y | FK → manager_feedback.id. The feedback being responded to. | — |
| employee_id | uuid | Y | FK → employees.id. Responding employee (must match manager_feedback.employee_id). | — |
| response_text | string(4000) | Y | The employee’s response. | — |
| response_type | enum | Y | ACKNOWLEDGE · ADD_CONTEXT · RESPECTFULLY_DISAGREE. | — |
| created_at | timestamp (UTC) | Y | Auto-set on creation. | NOW |
| updated_at | timestamp (UTC) | Y | Auto-set on creation; updated on edit (within 24h window only). | NOW |
| is_edited | boolean | Y | TRUE if edited after initial creation. | FALSE |

**Business rules:**

- A feedback entry with visibility = HRBP_ONLY has no feedback_responses rows (employee cannot see or respond).

- A single feedback_id may have multiple feedback_responses rows (a thread).

- A RESPECTFULLY_DISAGREE response triggers an HRBP notification per FR-M09-027.

**Sample data:**

| **feedback (excerpt)** | **employee** | **response_type** | **created** | **response_text (excerpt)** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| “Great work on the API redesign…” | Rohan Mehta | ACKNOWLEDGE | 13 May 2026 | “Thanks Priya — agreed on perf testing earlier; I’ll set up the load tests in week 1 next sprint.” |
| “The client demo went exceptionally well…” | Employee One | ACKNOWLEDGE | 9 May 2026 | “Appreciate it — credit to the rest of the team too. Will pass this on.” |

## 4.11 Document Management Entities (M11)

### 4.10.9 goal_plan_templates

Goal Plan template builder. Defines the structure of goal plans assigned to employees for a review cycle — including field toggles, approval flow, and category limits.

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| goal_plan_template_id | uuid | Y | Primary key. | auto |
| template_name | string(200) | Y | Display name. | — |
| template_code | string(80) | Y | Unique within tenant. | — |
| description | string(1000) | N | Free text. | NULL |
| applicable_to_uag_id | uuid | N | FK → assignment_rules.id. | NULL |
| review_cycle_id | uuid | N | FK → review_cycles.id (when bound to a specific cycle). | NULL |
| status | enum | Y | DRAFT · ACTIVE · ARCHIVED. | DRAFT |

**Goal Field Configuration cluster** (each row in goals_field_config corresponds to a goal-level field; this header captures the goal-plan-level toggles):

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enable_goal_categories | boolean | Y | Categorize goals (Performance, Development, Behavioural, etc.). | TRUE |
| goal_category_master_id_list | array(uuid) | N | FK list → goal_categories master. | [] |
| min_goals_per_plan | integer | N | Minimum goals required. | 1 |
| max_goals_per_plan | integer | N | Maximum goals allowed. | 10 |
| min_goals_per_category | jsonb | N | Per-category minima (e.g. {“Performance”: 3, “Development”: 1}). | {} |
| max_goals_per_category | jsonb | N | Per-category maxima. | {} |
| total_weightage_required | numeric(6,2) | Y | Sum of goal weightages must equal this. Hard-enforced at submission and approval per FR-M09-019. Default 100; not configurable below 100 to preserve calibration consistency. | 100.00 |
| weightage_per_category | jsonb | N | Per-category weightage limits. | {} |
| allow_goal_cascade | boolean | Y | Goals can cascade from manager to employee. | TRUE |
| allow_self_added_goals | boolean | Y | Employee can add own goals. | TRUE |
| allow_manager_added_goals | boolean | Y | Manager can add goals to reportee plan. | TRUE |
| allow_goal_editing_after_approval | boolean | Y | Edit goals after plan approval. | FALSE |
| edit_goals_requires_reapproval | boolean | Y | Edits trigger re-approval. | TRUE |

**Sub-Goal Configuration cluster:**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enable_sub_goals | boolean | Y | Allow sub-goal nesting. | FALSE |
| max_sub_goals_per_goal | integer | N | Cap on sub-goals. | 5 |
| sub_goal_weightage_sums_to_parent | boolean | Y | Sub-goal weightages sum to parent’s. | TRUE |
| allow_self_added_sub_goals | boolean | Y | Employee can add own sub-goals. | TRUE |
| allow_sub_goal_editing_after_approval | boolean | Y | Edit sub-goals after approval. | FALSE |

**Activity Object configuration** (one activity object can be associated with each goal):

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enable_activity_object | boolean | Y | Allow attaching activities to goals. | FALSE |
| activity_object_required | boolean | Y | Mandate activity on each goal. | FALSE |
| activity_object_type | enum | Y | TASK · DELIVERABLE · MILESTONE · CUSTOM. | TASK |
| max_activities_per_goal | integer | N | Cap on activities. | 10 |

**Plan-Level Approver configuration:**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| plan_approval_required | boolean | Y | Plan requires approval before activation. | TRUE |
| plan_approval_flow_id | uuid | N | FK → workflows.id. | NULL |
| reject_routes_to | enum | Y | EMPLOYEE_REDRAFT · MANAGER_REDRAFT · HRBP. | EMPLOYEE_REDRAFT |
| allow_cascade_reject_to_employee | boolean | Y | Manager can reject down to employee for rework (FR-M09-014). | TRUE |

**Other plan-level toggles:**

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enable_ai_goal_generation | boolean | Y | Activate AI Goal Generation suggestions (FR-M09-013). | FALSE |
| ai_goal_role_context_source | enum | N | JOB_DESCRIPTION · COMPETENCY_LIBRARY · CUSTOM. | JOB_DESCRIPTION |
| ai_goal_max_suggestions_per_request | integer | N | Cap on AI suggestions. | 10 |
| enable_goal_library | boolean | Y | Allow choosing from goal library. | TRUE |
| goal_library_categories | array(uuid) | N | Categories from library to surface. | [] |
| enable_skill_mapping | boolean | Y | Map goals to skills for L&D linkage. | FALSE |
| enable_competency_mapping | boolean | Y | Map goals to competencies. | FALSE |
| enable_weightage_locked_after_approval | boolean | Y | Lock weightages post-approval. | TRUE |
| display_overall_progress_to_employee | boolean | Y | Show aggregated progress. | TRUE |
| display_overall_progress_to_manager | boolean | Y | Show on manager dashboard. | TRUE |
| display_progress_to_hrbp | boolean | Y | Show to HRBP. | TRUE |
| send_reminder_for_pending_updates | boolean | Y | Auto-reminder for stale goals. | TRUE |
| reminder_days_for_stale_updates | integer | N | Days without update before reminder. | 30 |
| send_reminder_to | array(enum) | Y | EMPLOYEE · MANAGER · HRBP. | [EMPLOYEE, MANAGER] |
| allow_goal_extension | boolean | Y | Allow target-date extension request. | FALSE |
| extension_requires_approval | boolean | Y | Extension goes through approval. | TRUE |
| extension_approval_flow_id | uuid | N | FK → workflows.id. | NULL |
| display_goal_summary_in_review | boolean | Y | Show goal summary in linked review. | TRUE |

*Relationships: Many-to-many with employees via goal_plan_assignments. One-to-many with goals_field_config and sub_goals_field_config.*

### 4.10.10 goals_field_config

Per-field configuration within goal plan template. Each row controls one goal-level field’s behaviour (visible, editable, mandatory, validation).

| **Field** | **Type** | **Required** | **Description** | **Default** |
