#### M02 — Letter Template Inventory (17 Phase 1 Templates)

The DM20 decision binds Phase 1 letter templates to the following inventory. Each template has a unique LTR_ code, default signing authority per DM22 (CEO co-signature applies only where flagged), and a target lifecycle stage. Templates are stored in the M11 letter_templates entity; template body is authored by Document Admin with Letter Admin capability; legal review applies before each template is moved from DRAFT to ACTIVE status.

| **Code** | **Template name** | **Lifecycle stage** | **Default signing authority** | **CEO co-sign threshold** | **Cluster** | **Acknowledgement required** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| LTR_IOI | Intent-to-Hire / Pre-offer letter | Recruitment — pre-offer (FR-M08-009) | HR Admin | Not applicable (non-binding) | Sign-Off | No (acceptance via portal) |
| LTR_OFFER | Offer letter — full-time | Recruitment — final offer (FR-M08-004) | HR Admin | Yes — if proposed_ctc > tenant CTC threshold (default ₹50L IC) | Sign-Off | Yes (countersignature) |
| LTR_OFFER_CONTRACT | Offer letter — contractor / fixed-term | Recruitment — final offer (FR-M08-004) | HR Admin | Yes — if proposed_ctc > tenant CTC threshold | Sign-Off | Yes (countersignature) |
| LTR_APPOINTMENT | Appointment letter (post-joining formalisation) | Onboarding — Day 1 (M02) | HR Admin | No | Sign-Off | Yes |
| LTR_CONFIRMATION | Probation confirmation letter | Performance — probation closure (M09) | HR Admin | No | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_PROBATION_EXTEND | Probation extension letter | Performance — probation extension (M09) | HR Admin | No | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_PROMOTION | Promotion letter | Compensation — cycle outcome (M09 → M01) | HR Admin | Yes — if new proposed_ctc > tenant CTC threshold | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_INCREMENT | Increment / annual revision letter | Compensation — cycle outcome (M09 → M01) | HR Admin | Yes — if new proposed_ctc > tenant CTC threshold | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_TRANSFER | Internal transfer letter | Lifecycle event (M01) | HR Admin | No | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_WARNING_1 | First warning letter | Performance / discipline (M09) | HR Admin | No | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_WARNING_FINAL | Final warning letter | Performance / discipline (M09) | HR Admin (HRBP co-sign by configuration) | No | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_PIP_INITIATION | Performance Improvement Plan (PIP) initiation letter | Performance — PIP (M09) | HR Admin (HRBP co-sign by configuration) | No | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_TERMINATION | Termination letter (employer-initiated) | Exits & offboarding (M03) | HR Admin | Yes — CEO co-signs all employer-initiated termination letters per DM22 | Reference | Yes (acknowledgement of receipt) |
| LTR_ACCEPTANCE | Resignation acceptance letter (employee-initiated) | Exits & offboarding (M03) | HR Admin | No | Reference | Yes |
| LTR_RELIEVING | Relieving letter | Exits — Last Working Day (M03) | HR Admin | No | Reference | No (delivered to ex-employee) |
| LTR_EXPERIENCE | Experience / service letter | Exits — post-LWD (M03) | HR Admin | No | Reference | No (delivered to ex-employee) |
| LTR_RECOGNITION | Recognition / appreciation letter | Engagement (M15 — Phase 2; manual generation in Phase 1) | HR Admin | No | Reference | No |

**Notes on signing authority:**

- DM22’s principle stands: HR Admin signs all standard letters; CEO co-signs where the threshold or category warrants (offer above CTC threshold, termination). CEO co-signature on LTR_OFFER and LTR_OFFER_CONTRACT is conditional on proposed_ctc > tenant_ctc_threshold; the threshold default at provisioning is ₹50L per annum (Individual Contributor) and is configurable per entity by Org Admin.

- For LTR_TERMINATION, CEO co-signature is unconditional in Phase 1 (per DM22 — “CEO + HR Admin on Offer and Termination”). Tenants requiring a lower-authority termination chain (e.g. HRBP for contractor terminations) configure exceptions in M11 signing-authority records per entity.

- The escalate_signature flag (DM22) is reserved for disciplinary letters (LTR_WARNING_FINAL, LTR_PIP_INITIATION) and routes to HRBP co-signature when set.

- Phase 2 deliverables: LTR_BOND (employment bond letter), LTR_NON_COMPETE (non-compete acknowledgement), LTR_LEAVE_APPROVAL (leave-acknowledgement letter), LTR_TRAINING_NOMINATION (training nomination letter). These are not included in the 17 Phase 1 templates above.

## 5.4 M03 — Exits & Offboarding

**FR-M03-001: Self-service resignation with two-stage approval**

**Description: **Employee self-service resignation submission. Default approval flow: L1 Manager → HR Admin. HR Admin / Admin force-initiate also enabled for involuntary cases.

**User story: ***As an Employee, I want to submit my resignation through the platform so that the notice period clock starts immediately and my manager is notified.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Employee submits resignation with date_of_resignation, target last_working_day, reason_code, and optional reason_narrative.

- System computes proposed_last_working_day from date_of_resignation + notice_period_days (working days per Org default) and applies the LWD working-day rule (rolls forward if weekly off or holiday).

- Resignation routes to L1 Manager (Stage 1), then to HR Admin (Stage 2 — final approver).

- On final approval, employee transitions to NOTICE state; staged future-dated employment changes are auto-cancelled.

**Business rules:**

- Past-dated resignation: HR Admin only, ≤ 30 days back-dated, subject to notice-period rules. Employees cannot back-date their own resignation.

- Employees can revoke their own resignation before final approval. Hide-revoke option for employee = No (revoke visible to employee per migrated config).

- HR Admin, Admin, and HRBP can revoke a separation via SeparationRequests RBAC custom permission flag.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the L1 Manager is on extended leave, the request escalates after 5 days to next-level manager + HRBP + HR Admin simultaneously.

- If LWD computed would fall on a weekly off or holiday, system rolls LWD to the next working day and notifies the employee.

**FR-M03-002: Past-dated FLWD immediate deactivation — one-way door**

**Description: **When HR Admin approves a separation with FLWD set to a past date, the M01 profile deactivates immediately and CANNOT be reactivated through the standard flow. Reactivation requires a new Rehire via M08 → M02 → M01.

**User story: ***As an HR Admin processing an involuntary separation effective in the past, I want past-dated FLWD to deactivate the profile immediately so that access is revoked without further manual steps.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- When FLWD < today and HR Admin clicks Submit, an explicit warning dialog is shown describing the one-way door consequence.

- On confirmation, employee lifecycle_state transitions to SEPARATED immediately (skipping NOTICE and LWD states).

- Access begins to wind down immediately: M04, M05, M17 access revoked; self-service reduced to payslip view; M06 (Phase 2) flags for FnF settlement.

- Reactivation is blocked — the only path back is a full Rehire flow creating a new employees row with previous_employee_id link.

**Business rules:**

- Past-dated FLWD is a Platform — not configurable setting.

- Reason narrative is mandatory on past-dated FLWD submissions and visible to confidential_field_roles per policy.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If past-dated FLWD is submitted in error, recovery requires manual cleanup by Platform Super Admin via direct database operation — there is no standard UI undo.

- Audit log captures both the warning shown and the confirmation timestamp.

**FR-M03-003: FnF clearance — parallel multi-department workflow**

**Description: **FnF clearance is a parallel workflow — IT, Finance, Admin, Manager, HR Admin, and Payroll Admin act simultaneously, not sequentially. Payroll FnF settlement (Phase 2) is blocked until all clearances are received.

**User story: ***As an HR Admin, I want all clearance departments to act in parallel so that FnF processing completes as fast as the slowest reviewer rather than the sum of all reviewers.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- FnF clearance workflow_instance is initiated at LWD − 7 days (configurable per policy).

- Each department generates an fnf_clearances row with status = PENDING and assigned_to_user_id resolved at the moment of initiation.

- All departments can act simultaneously — no sequential dependency.

- FnF cannot complete until every fnf_clearances row is in CLEARED state.

**Business rules:**

- Asset clearance (M17) is a parallel stage — FnF cannot complete until IT Admin records the return of all assigned assets.

- FnF settlement calculation (Phase 2 — M06) is triggered only after all clearances are received and HR Admin marks FnF as complete.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If a clearance reviewer raises a BLOCKED status with a reason, the FnF cannot proceed until the blocker is resolved by the assigned reviewer or escalated.

- Clearance escalation fires after 5 days of inaction per separation workflow SLA.

**Part E — FnF clearance stage register (E1–E10). **The parallel clearance block runs ten stages, opened together at LWD−7 (configurable, DE15). Each stage emits a clear / hold event; FnF settlement (M06, Phase 2) is gated until all mandatory stages clear. Stages map 1:1 to fnf_clearances.department (§4.8.3).

| **Stage** | **Clearance** | **Stage owner** | **Default assignee** | **SLA** | **Mandatory?** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| E1 | Manager handover sign-off | Reporting line | L1 Manager | 5 days from window open | Yes |
| E2 | Asset return clearance | M17 Assets & IT | IT Admin | 5 days | Yes — blocks FnF |
| E3 | IT access revocation | IT Admin | IT Admin | 3 days | Yes |
| E4 | Finance / advances / loans | Finance Admin | Finance Admin | 5 days | Yes |
| E5 | Library / corporate card / facilities | Admin Operations | Office Admin | 3 days | Conditional — if assigned |
| E6 | Attendance & leave reconciliation (LOP lock) | Attendance Admin | Attendance Admin | 3 days | Yes — feeds M06 |
| E7 | Leave encashment (PL balance → FnF) | Leave Admin | Leave Admin | 3 days | Yes — per M04 |
| E8 | Compliance / NDA refresh / IP confirmation | HR Admin / Separation Admin | HR Admin | 5 days | Yes |
| E9 | Exit interview completion confirmation | HRBP | HRBP | 5 days | Yes (Voluntary); skipped Death/Absconding |
| E10 | Statutory clearance (PF · ESI · gratuity → M07) | Payroll Admin | Payroll Admin | Post-FLWD | Yes (Phase 2) |

**Part E.1 — Configured separation workflow (Separation Workflow Updated, Ver 1). The live configuration realises Part E as a 20-stage workflow built in the Flow Builder. Clearances, letters, reminders and conditional gate questions run in Parallel / Conditional mode; trigger points are expressed relative to the Last Day (LWD) or to Evaluation of Condition (after named predecessor stages).**

| **Order** | **Stage** | **Action / form** | **Assign role** | **Visibility** | **Trigger** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Accounts | Accounts Clearance (1.0) | Accounts – Payroll | Assignee & Admin | 0, after Last Day |
| 2 | HR | HR Clearance form (1.0) | HR Team | Assignee & Admin | 0, after Last Day |
| 3 | Reporting Manager | Reporting Manager Clearance (1.0) | Manager | Everyone in workflow | 0, after Last Day |
| 4 | Admin | Admin Clearance (1.0) | Administration | Assignee & Admin | 2, before Last Day |
| 5 | Finance Team | Gate Q: “Has the FnF been completed for the employee?” (Yes / No) | Accounts – Payroll | Assignee & Admin | after stages 1,2,3,4 (Evaluation of Condition) |
| 6 | HR | Experience Letter Form (2.0) | HR Team | Assignee & Admin | after stages 1,2,3,4 (Evaluation of Condition) |
| 7 | Experience Letter | Experience Letter | Self | Everyone in workflow (+ Personal Email) | after stage 6 |
| 8 | Exit Interview Form | Exit Interview Form (1.0) | Self | Assignee & Admin | 0, after Last Day |
| 9 | NDA Acknowledgement | Gate Q: “Has the NDA Acknowledgement been sent to the employee?” (Yes / No) | HR Team | Assignee & Admin | 0, after Last Day |
| 10 | IT No-Due | IT Clearance (3.0) | IT Admin | Everyone in workflow | 0, after Last Day |
| 11 | Insurance Deletion | Gate Q: “Is the insurance details deleted for the employee?” (Yes / No) | Insurance Deletion | Assignee & Admin | 0, after Last Day |
| 12 | Email Notification | Reminder Email – HR | Manager (+ Personal Email, Primary Mobile) | Assignee & Admin | 2, before Last Day |
| 13 | Email Notification | Reminder Email – HR | HR Team (+ Personal Email, Primary Mobile) | Assignee & Admin | 2, before Last Day |
| 14 | Email Notification | Reminder Email – HR | IT Admin (+ Personal Email, Primary Mobile) | Assignee & Admin | 2, before Last Day |
| 15 | Workflow Completion | Separation Workflow Completion | IT Admin | Assignee & Admin | 10, after (Evaluation of Condition) |
| 16 | Workflow Completion | Separation Workflow Completion | HR Team | Assignee & Admin | 6, after (Evaluation of Condition) |
| 17 | Workflow Completion | Separation Workflow Completion | Accounts – Payroll | Everyone in workflow | 1, after (Evaluation of Condition) |
| 18 | Relieving Letter | Relieving Letter | Self | Employee, assignee & Admin (+ Personal Email) | after stage 6 (Evaluation of Condition) |
| 19 | Reminder for LWD | Reminder for LWD | Manager (+ Personal Email, Primary Mobile) | Assignee & Admin | 2, before Last Day |
| 20 | Reminder for LWD | Reminder for LWD | HR Team / Manager / IT Admin (+ Personal Email, Primary Mobile) | Assignee & Admin | 2, before Last Day |

Workflow Standard Configurations: Restriction Condition AND / OR; Applicable To (employment types, e.g. Full Time, Associate); Restrict LWD On; execution mode Series / Conditional; Enable Custom Escalation; Enable Custom Archival of Tasks (archive 90 days from date of trigger); Enable Custom Flow Based; Allow Past Date of Resignation according to notice period; Select Approver Before Admin. Per-event notification triggers are configured for: Employee requests separation; Manager / Reviewer / Admin approves; Manager / Reviewer rejects — each with an email template and additional recipient roles (HOD, direct (L1) Manager, dotted-line Manager, L2 Manager, HR Team) and optional additional recipient users.

**FR-M03-004: Exit interview — scheduled at LWD−7**

**Description: **Exit interview is scheduled by default at LWD − 7 days. Structured questionnaire from configurable template. Responses anonymised in aggregate analytics.

**User story: ***As an HRBP, I want to conduct a structured exit interview so that the organisation learns from separations and improves retention.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Scheduled job creates exit_interviews row with state = SCHEDULED at LWD − 7 days for every separation_records row in ON_NOTICE state.

- HRBP receives a notification to conduct the interview.

- Interview can be CONDUCTED, DECLINED (employee declines to participate), or NO_SHOW.

- Responses stored on exit_interviews.responses as JSON keyed by question.

**Business rules:**

- M16 aggregate analytics on exit interviews never expose individual identity — themes and counts only.

- Reason narrative on the separation_records is separately confidential per policy.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the employee transitions to LWD before the scheduled interview, the interview state moves to NO_SHOW unless explicitly conducted earlier.

**FR-M03-005: Rehire eligibility determination**

**Description: **On positive exit record, HR Admin can mark separation as rehire_eligible. Cross-entity rehire requires Organisation Admin confirmation.

**User story: ***As an HR Admin, I want to flag eligible-for-rehire separations so that future recruitment can prioritise re-engaging proven talent.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- rehire_eligible flag set on separation_records by HR Admin after FnF completion.

- Rehire-eligible candidates appear in M08 recruitment with a ‘Rehire’ indicator linking to their prior employee record.

- Cross-entity rehire (employee separated from Entity A, rehired into Entity B in same tenant) requires Organisation Admin approval.

**Business rules:**

- Rehire creates a new employees row; previous_employee_id is populated; group_date_of_joining is preserved; continuous_service_flag set if rehire occurs within the configured continuity window.

- BGV may be skipped or simplified for rehires per the recruitment policy.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- Rehire of an absconded-then-separated employee defaults to rehire_eligible = FALSE; HR Admin override is logged.

**FR-M03-006: Absconding flag and conversion to separation**

**Description: **M05 sets absconding flag when 7 consecutive calendar days of unauthorised absence is reached. HR Admin action required to convert absconding to separation.

**User story: ***As an HR Admin, I want absconding to be flagged automatically but require my action to convert to separation so that genuine emergencies do not auto-terminate employees.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- M05 scheduled job detects 7-day calendar absence and sets employees.absconding_flagged_at and lifecycle_state = ABSCONDED.

- Threshold configurable per tenant (Org Admin) and per entity (HR Admin).

- Notification fires to HR Admin queue with the absconding employee details.

- HR Admin can convert to separation via M03 — creating a separation_records row with category = INVOLUNTARY and state = CONVERTED_FROM_ABSCONDING, or restore the employee to ACTIVE if the absence was justified.

**Business rules:**

- Only approved leave pauses the absconding counter. Pending leave does not pause the counter.

- Weekly Off days are counted in the 7-day calendar threshold (matching source policy). Holidays and system-deducted leave days are not counted.

- Absconding is not a terminal state — HR Admin action determines the resolution.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If an absconded employee returns and clocks in, the absconding flag remains until HR Admin explicitly restores Active status; the punch is logged but does not automatically clear the flag.

- Conversion to separation with past-dated FLWD invokes the one-way door deactivation per FR-M03-002.

**FR-M03-007: Separation Policy configuration (5-step wizard)**

Description: Separation Policy is configured through a five-step wizard — Basic Details, Policy Details, Process Details, Notification & Advanced Settings, and Banner — defining applicability, resignation / LWD rules, the initiation-and-approval model, the category-to-workflow mapping, per-policy notifications, and the employee-facing banner.

User story: As a Separation Admin (or HR Admin), I want to configure a separation policy end to end so that resignation initiation, approvals, the executing workflow and notifications all behave per policy.

**Acceptance criteria:**

Basic Details capture Policy Title (mandatory), Description and Applicability (Applicable To — by employment type / UAG).

Policy Details expose two toggles: allow_past_dated_resignation (“Allow past date of resignation according to notice period”) and force_separate_on_lwd (“Force separate employee on LWD as per notice period”).

Process Details set restrict_lwd_on (“Restrict Last Working Day On”); an Approval Flow Configuration captures one row per initiator (Self / HR Team / Admin) with an initiation form (Exit Initiation Form), an Approval Flow, an Approval Flow On Revoke, and Exclude-Capture / Exception / Confidential flags (separation_policy_initiators); plus capture_resignation_lwd_recovery, block_until_revoke_approval_complete, and a Default Approval Flow On Revoke.

Process Details also map each Separation Category to a Workflow with an “Alias for On Notice Flag” via separation_policy_workflow_map (e.g. Default → Separation Workflow Updated (Ver 1) → “On Notice”).

Notification & Advanced Settings define per-policy notification rows (Type · Default Recipient · Templates · Additional Roles). For any event type configured here, standard separation notifications are suppressed and only the configured custom notifications fire; if none is configured, no notification is sent.

Banner captures an optional rich-text Welcome Message (welcome_message) with a live Preview.

**Business rules:**

Stage-level workflow templates override policy-level templates when both are set (CO07).

Recovery Days captured at initiation feed the notice-shortfall recovery handled at FnF (M03 / M06 Phase 2).

The per-initiator revoke flow falls back to the policy Default Approval Flow On Revoke when not set.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

If force_separate_on_lwd is enabled, the employee is auto-separated on the computed LWD without a further manual step; a past-dated FLWD still follows the one-way-door rule in FR-M03-002.

### M03 — Functional Specification v1 (Reference Source: M03_Exits_Offboarding_Requirements.docx)

**Spec status.** Authored per the module Requirements Specification (canonical Part A–N template). All locked decisions from the source spec’s Part L are reproduced verbatim below as the contractual rules. Configuration values and approval flows are summarised; full configuration registers remain in the source spec.

**Module boundary:** M03 owns the Active-to-Separated transition: from resignation submission (or org-initiated termination / absconding-based separation) through notice-period management, separation workflow execution, exit interview, parallel FnF clearance (asset · IT · finance · payroll · HR), letter generation (acceptance, relieving, experience), and final last-working-day (FLWD) profile deactivation. On completion, the lifecycle state in M01 advances Active → Notice → LWD → Separated. Probation and confirmation flows are owned by M01 §C lifecycle with M09 Performance input — OUT OF SCOPE for this document. Payroll FnF settlement calculation runs in M06 (Phase 2) but the M03 clearance event is the Phase 1 trigger contract. Asset clearance is owned by M17.

**Decision-code namespace.** DE / CO / EO / LO series. 30 decisions catalogued.

#### M03.FS1 — Locked decisions register

Decisions sourced from M03_Exits_Offboarding_Requirements.docx Part L. Each row carries the decision code, scope, the locked rule, supporting note, and lock-status.

