## 5.5 M04 — Leave Management

**FR-M04-001: Leave application with dynamic leave type selector**

**Description: **Leave type selector dynamically filters to types with available balance > 0. Unpaid / LOP always shown regardless of balance. Platform-wide, non-configurable.

**User story: ***As an Employee, I want the leave selector to show only leave types I can actually apply for so that I do not waste time selecting types with zero balance.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Selector filters leave_types where employee_leave_balances.available_balance > 0 for the current leave_year.

- Unpaid / LOP always shown regardless of balance.

- SPL and SBL show zero quota by default — these types do not appear in the selector until Leave Admin or HR Admin credits a balance for the specific employee.

- Probation visibility rules: only SL (if balance > 0) and Unpaid / LOP available during probation.

- **UI simplification:** Apply Leave form surfaces only the employee-relevant fields (leave type, unit, from/to dates, reason, message, attachment, application impact summary, approval flow preview). Sandwich-impact preview and eligibility-check details are NOT displayed on the employee form — these are evaluated server-side and surfaced only if they cause a rejection. Rationale: reduces cognitive load; employees do not need to understand platform-internal rule mechanics.

**Business rules:**

- Notice period visibility rules: only SL (if balance > 0) and Unpaid / LOP available during notice. Hidden: PL, PL_CC, WWC, WL, PATL, ML, ADL, MCL, SPL, SBL, OH_*_26.

- Two-stage approval flow mandatory for ML, ADL, MCL, SPL, SBL — Stage 2 (HRBP/HR Admin/Leave Admin) cannot be bypassed.

- Balance deducted only after final approval (Stage 2 for two-stage types).

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If an employee’s profile completeness is below the mandatory minimum, leave application is blocked at entry with a clear message indicating missing profile fields.

- If a leave type has gender/marital/employment-type filters that exclude the employee, it is not shown in the selector at all (e.g. ML hidden from male employees).

**FR-M04-002: Leave cycle uniform 26th – 25th**

**Description: **Leave cycle aligned to payroll cycle: 26th of previous month to 25th of current month. Uniform across all entities. LOP feed sent to M06 (Phase 2) at payroll cutoff (25th).

**User story: ***As a Payroll Admin (Phase 2), I want the leave cycle uniformly aligned 26th–25th across all entities so that LOP feeds match payroll cutoff without per-entity reconciliation.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Leave period definition: 26th of previous month inclusive to 25th of current month inclusive.

- LOP calculation performed on the same window.

- Setting is platform-uniform — not configurable per entity.

- LOP feed scheduled job runs on the 25th of each month and emits the LOP record to M06 (Phase 2).

**Business rules:**

- Payroll cutoff notification: on the 24th and 25th of every month, system sends pending attendance request notification to responsible Manager every 2 hours until all pending requests are resolved. Overrides the standard 5-day escalation cadence for these two days only.

- Leave history table refresh: by calendar year per migrated config.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the 25th falls on a weekend or holiday, the LOP feed job still runs on the 25th — the cycle is calendar-based, not working-day-based.

**FR-M04-003: Standard approval flow with 10-day escalation**

**Description: **Standard leave approval flow: L1 Manager notified at submission. Escalation after 10 days of inaction to next level manager AND HRBP / HR Admin / Leave Admin simultaneously. Any eligible role can approve at any level. No auto-approval. No auto-rejection.

**User story: ***As an HR Admin, I want consistent 10-day escalation on leave requests so that no leave application stagnates indefinitely.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- On submission, leave_applications.status moves to SUBMITTED and L1 Manager is notified.

- If no action within 10 days, escalation fires: escalation_fired_at is set, next-level manager AND HRBP / HR Admin / Leave Admin are notified simultaneously.

- Any eligible role can approve or reject at any stage — escalation does not lock out the original approver.

- Status transitions: SUBMITTED → APPROVED (Stage 1 for standard flow, or STAGE_1_APPROVED for two-stage types) → STAGE_2_APPROVED (where applicable) → APPROVED.

**Business rules:**

- Two-stage flow (ML, ADL, MCL, SPL, SBL): Stage 1 = standard flow. Stage 2 = HRBP / HR Admin / Leave Admin only — mandatory.

- Auto-approval disabled platform-wide for leave — locked decision, not configurable.

- Rejection reason mandatory — rejection without reason is blocked.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the request’s leave_type has ‘restricted leave applications during blackout window’ enabled and the dates fall within the blackout, submission is blocked at entry.

- Past-dated leave applications beyond max_past_dated_days (31 for most types) are blocked; Org Admin and Platform Super Admin can bypass via configured bypass permissions.

**FR-M04-004: PL encashment — HR Admin only, intermittent allowed**

**Description: **PL encashment: 3 to 30 days range, intermittent allowed. Authorisation is HR Admin only — Leave Admin cannot authorise individual encashment regardless of other approval rights. Formula: basic_pay / 30 × days. Blocked during probation.

**User story: ***As an HR Admin, I want sole authorisation over leave encashment so that compensation-related decisions are tightly controlled.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Encashment authorisation UI is visible to HR Admin only. Leave Admin sees encashment data but cannot trigger encashment.

- Encashment records created in leave_encashment_records with authorised_by_user_id linked to an HR Admin user.

- Formula applied: amount = basic_pay / 30 × days_encashed. Currency: INR.

- Range validation: days_encashed must be between 3 and 30.

**Business rules:**

- PL encashment is blocked during probation — system rejects with explicit error code.

- Encashment window: HR Admin opens and closes on demand. No fixed dates configured at setup.

- Encashment option is not visible to employees — HR Admin-only action.

- FnF encashment captured separately with context = FNF.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If basic_pay is not available (Phase 1 stand-alone) — Phase 2 dependency — encashment records can be created with the formula but the amount calculation is deferred until M06 is active.

- Multiple intermittent encashment requests can be submitted across the year; total encashed_to_date is tracked in employee_leave_balances.

**FR-M04-005: Past-dated revocation by HRBP / Leave Admin / HR Admin**

**Description: **HRBP, Leave Admin, and HR Admin can revoke leave whose dates have already passed. Managers cannot revoke leave under any circumstances.

**User story: ***As an HRBP, I want to revoke past-dated leave when corrections are needed so that leave balances and attendance records remain accurate.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Past-dated revocation creates a revoked_by_user_id reference on leave_applications and a corresponding balance reversal in employee_leave_balances.

- Eligible revokers: HRBP, Leave Admin, HR Admin. Managers cannot revoke.

- Audit log captures the revocation with reason text and original application reference.

**Business rules:**

- Revocation does not undo any downstream payroll impact (Phase 2) — payroll team is notified separately if revocation crosses a payroll cycle.

- Auto-revocation on resignation beyond separation date = No per migrated config. Manual revocation required.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the revocation crosses a locked payroll cycle, the system flags the revocation and requires Payroll Admin acknowledgement before the balance reversal is applied to the next payroll cycle (Phase 2).

**FR-M04-006: Holiday calendar and optional holidays**

**Description: **National holidays pre-loaded at provisioning; state holidays per office location. Optional holidays (OH_*_26) require employee opt-in via application — hidden during probation and notice period.

**User story: ***As a Leave Admin, I want to manage the holiday calendar centrally per location so that statutory and discretionary holidays are correctly applied to attendance and leave calculations.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Holiday calendar entries stored in holiday_calendar with type NATIONAL, STATE, OPTIONAL, or LOCATION_SPECIFIC.

- National holidays are platform master data pre-loaded at provisioning per geography.

- Optional holidays require employee application — message mandatory per migrated config.

- Optional holiday past-date application is disabled. Application for next calendar year’s optional holidays in advance is disabled.

**Business rules:**

- Optional holidays hidden during probation and notice period per locked decisions.

- Half-day holidays configurable = No per migrated config (reserved for future use).

- Flexible holiday dates = disabled — fixed holiday dates only.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If an optional holiday is applied on a date that already has an approved leave application, the second application is blocked with a clear concurrency error.

**FR-M04-007: Blackout windows and admin bypass**

**Description: **Configurable blackout window for leave applications. Default current setting: 30 Dec 2025 – 3 Jan 2026. Platform Super Admin and permission role holders can bypass past-dated and special leave restrictions.

**User story: ***As a Leave Admin, I want to configure blackout windows so that critical business periods are protected from leave requests.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Blackout window stored as from-date and to-date global setting.

- Leave applications with from_date or to_date within the blackout window are blocked at submission with a clear error.

- Bypass permissions: Platform Super Admin can bypass past-dated leave applications and special leave applications. Designated permission role holders can also bypass these.

- L1 Manager and HRBP bypass = disabled per migrated config.

**Business rules:**

- Multiple blackout windows can be configured for different reasons (e.g. year-end freeze, peak season).

- Blackout windows do not affect already-approved leave that falls within the window — only new applications.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If an employee submits leave that partially overlaps the blackout window, the entire application is blocked — partial-acceptance is not supported.

- Bypassed applications are audit-flagged with bypass_reason and bypassed_by user reference.

**FR-M04-008: Team leave dashboard for managers and HODs**

**Description: **Team leave dashboard for L1 Managers and HODs. Default fields shown: Employee name, Leave type, From date, To date, Status, Reporting chain position. Leave reason not shown. Team leave hidden from manager calendar — accessed via dashboard only.

**User story: ***As an L1 Manager, I want a dedicated team leave dashboard so that I can see who is on leave at a glance without manually scanning the calendar.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Team leave dashboard widget visible to Manager (L1), HOD, UAG Head.

- Default fields: Employee name, Leave type, From date, To date, Status, Reporting chain position. Leave reason explicitly not shown.

- Team leave visible on manager calendar = No per migrated config — calendar is for the manager’s own leave only.

- HOD dashboard defaults to reporting chain view; HOD can toggle to entire department view (all employees in assigned department regardless of reporting line).

**Business rules:**

- Team Leave Overview widget shows pending and approved leave for the current week.

- Leave reason field is not displayed on this widget — privacy by design.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If a manager has no direct reports, the team dashboard renders an empty state: ‘No team members assigned.’

### FR-M04-009 — Sandwich Leave Calculation

**Description.** When an employee applies for leave spanning a configured day-count threshold (default 5 days) and the leave span includes intervening weekly-offs and/or holidays, those intervening days are counted as paid-leave consumption rather than free days. Drives leave-balance debit and LOP calculation. Configuration sourced from leave_platform_settings.apply_sandwich_leave, sandwich_for_n_days, apply_clubbing_across_weekly_off_holidays, and per-policy sandwich_leave_rules.

**Default state.** apply_sandwich_leave ships **disabled** (FALSE) per the source tenant configuration (Leaves_Settings_Export.csv). When disabled, this FR’s processing rules do not fire: leave spans are debited at face value regardless of intervening weekly-offs and holidays. Enabling the rule is an Org Admin configuration action on the Leave Platform Settings page; turning it on activates the threshold check, the per-policy overrides (count_intervening_weekly_off, count_intervening_holidays), and the auto-cron month-end re-evaluation.

**Trigger.** Leave application submission, leave application edit, leave-balance projection display.

**Inputs.** Leave application (employee_id, leave_type_id, from_date, to_date, half_day flags), platform settings sandwich configuration, applicable holiday calendar, weekly-off pattern for the employee.

**Processing.**

- Compute span of working-day equivalents using the employee’s weekly-off pattern and holiday calendar.

- If span ≥ sandwich_for_n_days, mark all intervening weekly-offs and holidays as countable.

- Apply per-policy overrides (count_intervening_weekly_off, count_intervening_holidays).

- Recalculate total leave units to be debited.

- Display sandwich impact to applicant before submission (“X days requested, Y days counted due to sandwich rule”).

**Outputs.** Adjusted leave-debit count, sandwich-debit breakdown, applicant warning if balance now insufficient.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Sandwich rule is gated by the platform-level apply_sandwich_leave flag; when disabled (default), no sandwich deduction occurs and the UI shows the rule as “Disabled in current settings”.

- Sandwich rule applies only when leave span meets threshold.

- Intervening weekly-offs and holidays counted only if both platform setting and policy setting agree.

- Sandwich impact visible to applicant before approval.

- Audit log records sandwich application.

- Auto-cron (sandwich_auto_cron_from_date, sandwich_auto_cron_till_date) re-evaluates approved leave at month-end.

### FR-M04-010 — Decision Matrix for Leave Eligibility

**Description.** Replace static eligibility rules with a tenant-configurable decision matrix that combines multiple dimensions (tenure, designation, location, gender, marital status, dependent count, etc.) into a multi-input lookup table. Each row in the matrix yields a leave-rule outcome (eligible / not eligible, allotment value, accrual rate, validity period).

**Trigger.** Leave application validation, leave allotment computation, balance refresh cron.

**Inputs.** Employee profile attributes, decision matrix configuration (stored as leave_policies.decision_matrix_config jsonb), leave application.

**Processing.**

- Resolve employee’s matrix-input vector at evaluation date.

- Look up first matching matrix row (rules evaluated in sort_order).

- Apply matched row’s outcome: eligibility flag, allotment, accrual rule, validity.

- If no match, fall back to policy default.

- Cache result for the cycle; invalidate on employment-history change.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Matrix supports at least 10 input dimensions.

- Matrix lookup completes within 100ms per employee.

- Re-evaluation triggered automatically on employment-history change.

- Matrix editable via admin UI without code change.

### FR-M04-012 — Concurrent Leave Application

**Description.** Allow employees to hold multiple leave applications with overlapping date ranges, distinguishing them by leave type or half-day specification. Used when an employee plans a multi-leave-type day (e.g. half-day PL + half-day Comp-Off).

**Trigger.** Leave application submission when overlapping application exists.

**Inputs.** New application, existing approved/pending applications, platform setting enable_concurrent_leave_application.

**Processing.**

- Identify overlapping applications.

- Validate non-conflict on half-day type (no two first-half or two second-half on same day).

- Validate total non-LOP debit ≤ 1 day per calendar day.

- Permit concurrent applications when validations pass.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Concurrent applications visible in single calendar view.

- Approval flows route independently per application.

- Total leave debit per day not exceeding 1 working day equivalent.

### FR-M04-013 — Combined Leave Balance

**Description.** Pool balances from multiple leave types into a single combined balance visible to the employee and consumable up to a configured cap.

**Trigger.** Balance display, leave application against combined pool.

**Inputs.** leave_platform_settings.enable_combined_leave_balance, combined_balance_policy_ids, combined_balance_max_usable.

**Processing.**

- Sum balances across listed leave types.

- Apply cap from combined_balance_max_usable.

- When employee applies, debit balances in configured debit order within the pool.

- Display combined and per-type breakdowns.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Combined display matches sum of components minus cap overflow.

- Per-type audit trail preserved.

- Cap recalculated each cycle.

### FR-M04-014 — Holiday Pay Policy

**Description.** Tracks work performed on holidays and computes additional pay based on a leave_holiday_pay_policies definition (multiplier × hours worked).

**Trigger.** Attendance record on a holiday date, payroll cycle close.

**Inputs.** Attendance record, applicable holiday calendar entry, employee’s assigned holiday pay policy.

**Processing.**

- Identify attendance records on dates flagged in holiday_calendar.

- Resolve employee’s holiday pay policy via UAG.

- Validate min_hours_to_qualify met (and applies_to_full_day_only if set).

- Compute extra pay: pay_multiplier × hours worked × base hourly rate.

- Emit holiday-pay debit/credit record for payroll integration (Phase 2).

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Policy applies only to specified holiday types.

- Pay calculation auditable.

- Employees with no policy receive no extra pay.

### FR-M04-015 — Flexible Holiday Date Change

**Description.** Allow employees to request a holiday date be observed on an alternate date (e.g. when religious holiday falls on weekly off and employee wants to take the working day instead).

**Trigger.** Holiday observed during weekly-off, employee request to move.

**Inputs.** Employee’s date-change request, platform setting enable_flexible_holiday_dates, holiday entry.

**Processing.**

- Validate holiday is flagged flexible.

- Validate target date is a working day for the employee.

- Route through configured approval flow.

- On approval, create override record for the employee.

- On auto-movement (flexible_holiday_enable_auto_movement = TRUE), system auto-shifts holiday observance for all employees whose weekly-off falls on the holiday.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Holiday change scope is per-employee (not global).

- Original holiday remains in calendar; override is recorded.

- Date change requires reason if flexible_holiday_reason_mandatory = TRUE.

### FR-M04-016 — Smart Suggestions (CF Expiry / Comp-Off Expiry)

**Description.** Proactively notify employees of carry-forward leave and comp-off balances approaching expiry, with one-click action to plan leave.

**Trigger.** Daily cron at platform-configured time.

**Inputs.** Outstanding CF balance with expiry date, comp-off balance with lapse date, notification lead times.

**Processing.**

- For each employee, compute CF and comp-off expiring within lead-time window.

- Generate suggestion records.

- Dispatch notifications (email, in-app, mobile push) per employee preference.

- Provide CTA to leave application form pre-filled with the relevant leave type.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Notification fires once per balance per lead-time threshold (no daily spam).

- CTA correctly pre-fills leave type and remaining-balance hint.

- Honour employee notification preferences.

### FR-M04-017 — Hourly Leave

**Description.** Support leave applications in hours rather than full days for designated leave types.

**Trigger.** Hourly leave application submission.

**Inputs.** Leave application with unit = HOURS, leave-type config is_hourly_leave = TRUE, hourly_leave_min_duration_minutes, hourly_leave_multiple_minutes.

**Processing.**

- Validate unit and duration against policy.

- Round to nearest multiple per policy.

- Validate against allow_hourly_leave_across_midnight.

- Debit balance in hours; for display, convert to day-equivalents using hourly_leave_hours_in_day.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Balance display shows hours and day-equivalent.

- Cannot apply less than hourly_leave_min_duration_minutes.

- Hourly leave conflicts with full-day attendance flagged.

### FR-M04-018 — Encashment Formula Engine

**Description.** Allow tenants to define custom formulas for leave encashment payouts (e.g. (Basic + DA) / 30 × encash_days, or Gross / Working Days × encash_days × multiplier).

**Trigger.** Leave encashment application, cycle-end auto-encashment.

**Inputs.** Encashment formula expression on policy, employee salary components, encashment day count.

**Processing.**

- Resolve formula’s referenced salary components for the employee.

- Evaluate formula with safe expression evaluator.

- Apply rounding rules per policy.

- Persist computed amount on encashment record.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Formula supports +, −, ×, ÷, parentheses, named salary components.

- Division-by-zero handled gracefully.

- Computed amount visible to employee before submission.

### FR-M04-019 — NSD Multiplier for Leave

**Description.** Apply Night Shift Differential (NSD) multiplier when leave is taken from a night shift, so balance debit accurately reflects shift-weighted hours.

**Trigger.** Leave application from a night-shift employee.

**Inputs.** Shift definition with NSD multiplier, leave application, policy NSD configuration.

**Processing.**

- Identify whether the leave date falls on a night shift.

- Apply NSD multiplier to hour-equivalent leave debit when configured.

- Pass adjusted hours to payroll integration.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- NSD applied only when both shift and policy permit.

- Audit log captures multiplier.

### FR-M04-020 — LOP Order-of-Use

**Description.** Define the consumption order among multiple LOP policies for an employee. Used when an employee has multiple unpaid-leave policy applicability and the system must determine which one debits first.

**Trigger.** LOP application or LOP cron debit.

**Inputs.** Employee’s LOP policy assignments, LOP order-of-use configuration on each policy, application context.

**Processing.**

- Identify all applicable LOP policies for the employee.

- Sort by lop_order_of_use_priority (lowest first).

- Debit from the first policy until its cap reached, then proceed to the next policy.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Order-of-use deterministic.

- Per-cycle caps respected.

- Each debit audit-logged.

### FR-M04-021 — Manual Leave Balance Adjustment

**Description.** HR Admin can manually adjust an employee’s leave balance for a specific leave type to correct data errors, apply an approved exception, or reconcile migrated balances. The action is restricted to the HR Admin role only; no other role can create, edit, or reverse a manual adjustment.

**Trigger.** HR Admin initiates a balance adjustment from the leave balance page; balance-reconciliation activity.

**Inputs.** Target employee, leave type, signed adjustment quantity (credit or debit), mandatory reason, effective date.

**Processing.**

- Validate that the acting user holds the HR Admin role and that the target employee is assigned the selected leave type.

- Apply the signed adjustment to employee_leave_balances for the selected leave type from the specified effective date and record the resulting delta.

- A reason is mandatory on every adjustment; the adjustment is rejected without it.

- The adjusted balance is reflected on the employee’s leave page immediately on posting.

**Acceptance criteria.**

- Only HR Admin can create, edit, or reverse a manual balance adjustment.

- Every adjustment is audit-logged with actor, employee, leave type, signed quantity, reason, and effective date.

- Adjustments are reversible; a reversal is itself an audit-logged adjustment.

### M04 — Functional Specification v1 (Reference Source: M04_Leave_Management_Requirements.docx)

**Spec status.** Authored per the module Requirements Specification (canonical Part A–N template). All locked decisions from the source spec’s Part L are reproduced verbatim below as the contractual rules. Configuration values and approval flows are summarised; full configuration registers remain in the source spec.

**Decision-code namespace.** D series. 29 decisions catalogued.

