### Amendment — FS reconciliation (M05 Attendance, 3 June 2026, tracked).

**Prototype aligned to locked decisions (no BRD change). **The Phase-1 clickable prototype (v20.9) was corrected where it had drifted from already-binding M05 decisions: zero grace time on all migrated attendance policies (FR-M05-001); auto-approval disabled for every attendance request type (DA02); attendance lock at the 25th payroll cutoff (DA03), not the 5th; shift change performed by Attendance Admin / HR Admin only, with no employee-facing flow (DA18); the 500 m check-in fence (DA05); and 15 active fences across Mumbai, Bengaluru and Hyderabad (DA04). These rules were already authoritative in this BRD; only the prototype changed.

**Attendance reasons — auto-approval. **No attendance reason is auto-approve eligible (DA02). The auto-approve and frequency-cap values previously shown on the reasons configuration screen were illustrative; the binding reason catalogue and frequencies are the migrated set (DA10 / the reason master).

**Overtime model split (FR-M05-010 / FR-M05-017). **Day-class multipliers (weekday / weekly-off / holiday, FR-M05-010, policy-level) and hour-band indexing slabs (FR-M05-017, entity overtime_slabs §4.6.13) are distinct and configured on separate surfaces. The prototype previously conflated them on one screen and has been split accordingly.

**WFH is not a sixth request type (FR-M05-003). **The five attendance request types in FR-M05-003 stand. Work-from-home is handled as an attendance reason and / or the is_wfh_shift attribute (§4.6.1), not as a distinct request type. No change to FR-M05-003.

**Configuration vs operational surfaces. **Each attendance master entity — attendance_policies, geofencing_master (§4.6.12) and biometric_devices (§4.6.6) — has a single master CRUD surface under Settings (Org Admin); the operational Attendance-Admin screens are read-and-assign working views over the same entity. The prototype section references were corrected to §4.6.12 (geofencing) and §4.6.6 (biometric devices).

**Per-employee fence & auto-fence — Phase 2. **Per-employee geofence merge and auto-fence (attendance_platform_settings cluster 11) are out of scope for Phase 1; Phase-1 fencing is location / work-area level only (DA04). The toggles remain dormant and the per-employee fence screen is deferred to Phase 2.

**Absconding boundary (FR-M05-005 / FR-M03-006). **Absconding detection is FR-M05-005 — the daily job that flags 7 consecutive calendar days of unauthorised absence and sets lifecycle_state = ABSCONDED. The absconding queue and convert / restore actions are FR-M03-006 (M03). The prototype queue now cites FR-M05-005 (detection) alongside FR-M03-006 (queue).

**Comp-off boundary — two legs (FR-M05-008 / M04). **Comp-off splits by phase. The earning leg — overtime detection and the planned-overtime / credit request (FR-M05-008) — is built in M05, sharing the OT policy and following the same request-and-approval pattern as attendance regularisation. The consumption leg — the comp-off balance, the comp-off leave application, expiry / lapse and encashment — is built in M04 as a leave type (entity tenant_leaves_compoff, which carries its own Leave code and the full leave-application and encashment ruleset), reusing the M04 leave engine rather than duplicating it. The two legs meet at one contract: approved qualifying overtime in M05 posts a comp-off credit into the M04 balance. Encashment-window coordination remains the open M04 question in ON-AT05.

**API inventory extended (§7.4.3). **The M05 inventory gains four FS-reconciled endpoints (tracked there): attendance-request withdraw, approver-queue read, on-demand LOP report run, and master config CRUD for shifts / reasons / geofences / IP whitelist.

