## 5.7 M08 — Recruitment (ATS)

**FR-M08-001: Requisition auto-numbering with JR_ prefix and counter continuation**

**Description: **Requisition IDs auto-generated with prefix JR_ and a continuing counter. P06 Migration suppresses counter reset at cutover — the next requisition raised in PrimeSoft HRMS continues from the migrated counter value (e.g. JR_557).

**User story: ***As a Hiring Lead, I want requisition IDs to continue without renumbering across the Darwinbox → PrimeSoft migration so that historical references remain valid and audit links are preserved.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Counter is global (single rule applies across the tenant).

- On migration cutover, the counter is set to the migrated next-number value (557 per source).

- Each new requisition increments the counter by 1.

- Counter reset is suppressed in P06 migration scope.

**Business rules:**

- Auto-numbering enabled by default; prefix JR_ is the configured value.

- Requisition ID is unique across the tenant — uniqueness enforced at database layer.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If counter collisions occur during parallel writes, database unique constraint ensures only one succeeds; the failed transaction retries with the next value.

**FR-M08-002: Candidate auto-numbering — CAN_ prefix with per-type counter**

**Description: **Candidate IDs auto-generated with prefix CAN_ and separate counters per Employee Type (Full Time, Part time, Associate, Contract, Consultant, Intern). All six counters carried forward verbatim from migrated source.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin, I want separate candidate counters per employment type so that ATS reporting and tracking align with the established categorisation.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Six employee types each have an independent counter.

- Counter values at migration: Full Time = 13799, Part Time = 01, Associate = 6498, Contract = 35, Consultant = 32, Intern = 02.

- Common prefix CAN_ across all six counters.

- Region scope: All Regions; Company scope: single legal entity.

**Business rules:**

- Migration carries forward counters verbatim.

- Validation of which Employee Types are in active use should be done before go-live.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If a candidate’s target_employment_type is changed mid-process (e.g. converted from Contract to Full-Time), the candidate_id is retained — the prefix and counter are immutable post-assignment.

**FR-M08-003: Duplicity check with admin override**

**Description: **Duplicity check enabled on new candidate records to detect prior applications. Single setting ‘Duplicity Check’ applies to All Companies. Org Admins, Hiring Leads, and Permission Role Holders can override for all sources.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin, I want duplicity checks on candidate addition with override capability so that we avoid double-tracking the same candidate while permitting legitimate re-application.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- On new candidate addition, system queries existing candidates by email and mobile within the tenant.

- If a match is found within the configured window (Phase 1 default: all active candidate records), submission is blocked with a clear message referencing the existing candidate_id.

- Override permitted for Org Admin, Hiring Lead, and Permission Role Holder roles. Override creates an audit log entry with the override actor and justification.

- IJP candidates may have separate re-application rules per the duplicity_check_settings_export.

**Business rules:**

- Re-application from a known candidate state (e.g. ARCHIVED, OFFER_DECLINED) requires override unless the configured re-application window allows it.

- Duplicity check scope is All Companies (single tenant).

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If a candidate matches across multiple records, the system surfaces all matching candidate IDs for the Recruitment Admin to review and merge or override.

- Duplicity check applies at candidate addition — not at every interaction.

**FR-M08-004: Offer letter with CEO approval above CTC threshold**

**Description: **Offer letter generation requires CEO approval when proposed_ctc exceeds a configurable CTC threshold. Below threshold, **Recruitment Admin or HR Admin** can generate with HR Admin signature only (no CEO approval required).

**User story: ***As an HR Admin, I want CEO approval on high-CTC offers so that compensation decisions above the threshold receive financial oversight.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Offer creation captures proposed_ctc; system evaluates against configured threshold.

- If proposed_ctc > threshold, ceo_approval_required is set TRUE and offer state remains PROPOSED until CEO approves.

- CEO approval creates an audit-logged action and transitions offer state to APPROVED.

- Offer can then be extended to candidate (state → EXTENDED).

**Business rules:**

- Offer letter approval is separate from the hike approval chain (Phase 2) — Finance Admin’s role on offers is offer-letter-specific.

- **Recruitment Admin AND HR Admin** both have offer letter generation rights. Recruiter cannot generate offer letters. Both roles are listed as eligible drafters in the offer creation workflow; the system audit-logs the actor.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the candidate counter-negotiates and proposed_ctc is revised upward above threshold mid-flow, CEO re-approval is required.

- If CEO rejects the offer, Recruitment Admin or HR Admin can either revise the proposed_ctc or withdraw the offer entirely.

**FR-M08-005: Offer acceptance triggers Candidate→Pre-joining transition**

**Description: **On offer countersignature by candidate, M08 emits the offer acceptance event. M01 generates the employee_id and transitions lifecycle_state to PRE_JOINING. M02 receives the onboarding handover.

**User story: ***As a Candidate accepting an offer, I want my pre-joining portal access to activate as soon as I countersign so that I can begin the joining preparation immediately.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Candidate countersigns offer through the candidate portal; offers.countersigned_at is set.

- M08 emits offer_accepted event; M01 listens and creates employees row with employee_id = {entity_short_code}{6-digit sequence}.

- M01 sets lifecycle_state = PRE_JOINING.

- M02 picks up the candidate for onboarding (auto-initiation 14 days before DOJ or manual initiation by Onboarding Admin).

**Business rules:**

- Offer letter template stored in M11; personalised output stored on M01 employee_documents.

- Cross-entity handover: if offer is for a different entity than the candidate’s source, employee_id uses the new entity’s short_code.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the candidate withdraws acceptance before onboarding initiation, the employee record is soft-deleted and the candidate moves to OFFER_DECLINED state.

- If multiple offers are active for the same candidate (different requisitions), only the countersigned offer triggers employee_id creation; other offers are auto-withdrawn.

**FR-M08-006: External recruiter portal access**

**Description: **External recruiter portal enabled. 11 active recruiters and 6 recruiter groups in migrated source. Each external recruiter has portal login identity with scoped access to their submitted candidates.

**User story: ***As an External Recruiter, I want a portal to submit candidates and track progress so that engagement with the hiring company is structured and trackable.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- external_recruiters entity holds agency, contact, and portal_user_id.

- Portal user can submit candidates for requisitions they have been granted access to.

- Recruiter sees status updates on their submitted candidates only.

- Recruiter cannot see candidates from other recruiters or sources.

**Business rules:**

- External recruiter groups (6 in source) can be used for fee-share or area-of-specialism grouping.

- Source tagging is mandatory on candidate addition; external recruiter candidates auto-tagged with source_type = EXTERNAL_RECRUITER.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If a candidate submitted by external recruiter is found to be a duplicate, the override decision determines which recruiter owns the placement; conflict resolution is manual by Recruitment Admin.

**FR-M08-007: Interview scheduling with calendar integration**

**Description: **Interviews scheduled with interviewer panel; calendar integration sends interview invites to interviewer calendars. Configured interview types from migrated source. Interview Guides and Assessments are out of Phase 1 scope.

**User story: ***As a Recruiter, I want to schedule interviews with calendar invites to interviewers so that interview coordination is streamlined and absences are reduced.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Interview creation captures scheduled_at, duration_minutes, mode, meeting_link (for video), and interviewer_user_ids panel.

- Outbound integration sends calendar invite to each interviewer’s calendar via iCal.

- Interviewer feedback captured via interviews.feedback_notes, overall_rating, recommendation.

- Interview status workflow: SCHEDULED → IN_PROGRESS → COMPLETED (or CANCELLED, NO_SHOW).

**Business rules:**

- Interview types in scope: configured per migrated Interview_Types_Export (TECH_R1, TECH_R2, MANAGERIAL, HR, etc.).

- Interview Guides (D.2) and Assessments (D.3) sections are out of Phase 1 scope — empty source registers per migration data.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If an interviewer is unavailable at scheduled time, recruiter can replace; calendar invite is updated and original interviewer is notified of removal.

- Interview reschedule beyond a configured threshold (e.g. 3 reschedules) flags the candidate record for recruiter review.

**FR-M08-008: Mandatory source tagging on candidate addition**

**Description: **Every candidate must be source-tagged at addition. Sources are the union of system sources (Careers Page, IJP, Referral, External Recruiter, Job Boards) and Custom Sources.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin, I want mandatory source tagging so that source-of-hire analytics are complete and reliable.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- candidates.source_type is a required field at insert.

- Source types: CAREERS_PAGE, IJP, REFERRAL, EXTERNAL_RECRUITER, JOB_BOARD, CUSTOM_SOURCE.

- If source_type = REFERRAL, source_detail captures the referrer employee_id.

- If source_type = EXTERNAL_RECRUITER, source_detail captures the recruiter_name or external_recruiters.id.

**Business rules:**

- Source tagging is platform-mandatory — not configurable to off.

- M16 source-of-hire reports group by source_type.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If a candidate’s source_type changes mid-process (e.g. corrected after addition), the original tag is retained in audit log; the current tag is updated with a note.

### FR-M08-009: Pre-offer / Intent-to-Hire issuance

**Description: **After interview rounds clear and the hiring panel has formally recommended hire, the Recruitment Admin (or HR Admin) issues a non-binding Pre-offer / Intent-to-Hire (IOI) letter to the candidate. The pre-offer communicates the indicative compensation band, target joining date, and the document checklist the candidate must furnish. The pre-offer is not a contractual offer — it expresses intent contingent on document review (FR-M08-010). The pre-offer triggers candidate document collection and starts the verification SLA.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin, I want to issue a non-binding Intent-to-Hire letter so that the candidate can begin gathering documents and serving notice at their current employer while we complete pre-joining checks, without committing to the final compensation until we verify their inputs.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Pre-offer can only be issued when the candidate’s state is INTERVIEW_PASSED. Attempting to issue from other states is blocked with a validation error.

- Pre-offer letter template = LTR_IOI (registered in M11 D.1 template inventory). Signature configuration follows DM22 — HR Admin signs standard IOIs; HR Admin signs all standard IOIs (Pre-offer/Intent-to-Hire letters are non-binding and do not require CEO sign-off, even for above-threshold proposed bands).

- Pre-offer captures: indicative_ctc_min, indicative_ctc_max, target_doj, document_checklist (multi-select from M11 DM17 document master), pre_offer_validity (default 5 working days from issuance; tenant-configurable up to a maximum of 14 working days).

- On issuance, M08 emits the pre_offer_extended event. Candidate state transitions to PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED. The candidate portal surfaces the IOI for acceptance and the document upload checklist.

- Candidate can Accept (state → PRE_OFFER_ACCEPTED), Reject (state → PRE_OFFER_DECLINED · cooldown applies per FR-M08-003), or request Revision (state → PRE_OFFER_REVISION · routes back to Recruitment Admin / HR Admin for re-issuance).

- Pre-offer acceptance does NOT create the employees row in M01 — that happens only on final offer countersignature per FR-M08-005.

- Threshold approvals (Finance Admin · CEO) under FR-M08-004 do NOT apply to pre-offer — by design, since the indicative band is non-binding. Threshold approvals apply at final offer release in FR-M08-004.

**Business rules:**

- Either Recruitment Admin OR HR Admin can issue pre-offers (joint authority, mirroring final offer in FR-M08-004). Recruiters cannot issue pre-offers.

- Pre-offer validity default 5 working days · configurable per tenant up to a maximum of 14 working days · validity expiry moves the candidate to PRE_OFFER_EXPIRED state; Recruitment Admin or HR Admin can re-extend the pre-offer once with a new validity clock.

- The indicative compensation band issued in the pre-offer must lie within the requisition’s approved CTC band. Variance outside the band requires re-approval through the requisition raise path.

- Indicative CTC range cannot be wider than 30% of the band midpoint (prevents bait-and-switch where final offer falls far below pre-offer intent).

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If the candidate’s requisition is closed or put on hold after pre-offer issuance, the pre-offer auto-expires and the candidate is notified.

- If the candidate is being considered for multiple requisitions concurrently and a pre-offer is issued for one, the other requisitions remain unaffected; the candidate stays in those pipelines.

- If pre-offer is issued in error, only Recruitment Admin or HR Admin can revoke before candidate response. Post-acceptance revocation requires reason capture and audit-logs the action.

### FR-M08-010: Post-pre-offer document review by Recruitment Admin / HR Admin

**Description: **After pre-offer acceptance, the candidate uploads requested documents to the candidate portal. The Recruitment Admin or HR Admin reviews each uploaded document against the M11 DM17 verification rules, validates the candidate’s declared compensation against salary slips, validates designation and notice period against the relieving letter, and validates education credentials. On successful review, the final offer is generated and released (FR-M08-004 path). On discrepancy, the verifier flags the document and routes back to the candidate with reason; on serious discrepancy (e.g. fabricated relieving letter), the candidate is moved to BLACKLISTED state with HRBP review per Table 8.6.2.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin or HR Admin, I want to verify the candidate’s submitted documents before releasing the binding final offer so that compensation mismatches, exaggerated experience claims, and identity discrepancies surface before we commit contractually.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Document review can only proceed when candidate state is PRE_OFFER_ACCEPTED and all mandatory documents (per pre-offer checklist) have been uploaded.

- Reviewer sees each uploaded document with extracted metadata (M11 OCR for PAN, Aadhaar, etc.), verification status (Pending · Verified · Discrepancy · Rejected), discrepancy category (Identity mismatch · CTC mismatch · Designation mismatch · Experience gap · Other), and reviewer notes.

- Approved comparisons captured: declared_current_ctc vs salary_slip_amount (warn if > 15% variance) · declared_designation vs relieving_letter_designation · declared_notice_period vs relieving_letter_notice · declared_qualification vs education_certificate.

- On full set verified, state → DOCUMENT_REVIEW_PASSED. Final offer (FR-M08-004) is auto-drafted with the verified CTC and routed to the configured signature chain (HR Admin standalone for below-threshold offers · CEO co-signs (with HR Admin) for above-threshold offers).

- On flagging, state → DOCUMENT_REVIEW_FLAGGED · candidate notified with the specific discrepancy and asked to re-upload or clarify. Maximum 2 re-upload cycles before mandatory HRBP escalation.

- Recruiter can flag documents during first-pass review but cannot mark a document Verified — verification rights are restricted to Recruitment Admin and HR Admin (joint authority per DM22 + FR-M08-004 pattern).

**Business rules:**

- Mandatory documents at onboarding (per M11 DM17): PAN Card, Aadhaar Card, highest education certificate, previous relieving letter, previous salary slips (last 3 months), bank account proof, and photograph. All mandatory documents must be marked Verified before the final offer can be released.

- Document review SLA = 5 working days (default, configurable per tenant) from candidate upload completion · breach escalates to HRBP. Reviewer assignment defaults to the same role that issued the pre-offer; another Recruitment Admin or HR Admin can take over.

- CTC variance threshold (configurable, default 15%) gates auto-progression. Above threshold, the verifier must either re-negotiate the offer band (sends pre-offer back to revision) or escalate to the hiring lead.

- Documents are stored in M11 vault per DM13 architecture. Verification status writes to candidates.verification_status field for audit.

- If candidate cannot produce a relieving letter (current employer hostile termination), an undertaking is acceptable provided the candidate’s previous-2 employers’ relieving letters and 3 months of salary slips reconcile.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- If candidate uploads documents that match an existing employee record (duplicate PAN or Aadhaar against active PSI employee), the duplicity check (FR-M08-003) re-fires and the candidate is flagged for admin override.

- If a serious discrepancy is detected (e.g. claimed Series A startup founder, but EPF record shows employment continuation at a different company), the candidate enters BLACKLISTED state with HRBP review; the candidate cannot re-apply for 24 months.

- If candidate uploads sensitive documents to the wrong slot (e.g. PAN file uploaded as education cert), the system flags but does not auto-correct — candidate must re-upload to the correct slot for audit clarity.

FR-M08-011 to FR-M08-016 below extend M08 with the screen-level behaviour captured in the recruitment UI specifications (Create Job, Raise Requisition, Offer Letter / Generate Offer Letter, Hiring Flow, Overview, My Interviews, IJP Openings, IJP Jobs Applied, Refer, My Referrals, Link Accounts). They complement FR-M08-001 to FR-M08-010 and the M08 data model in section 4.9; no prior requirement is superseded.

### FR-M08-011: Job creation — five-step Create Job wizard

**Description: **Recruitment Admin, HR Admin or Hiring Lead creates a Job from the Job Openings page via a five-step wizard: (1) Job Details, (2) Job Posting, (3) Job Application, (4) Hiring Workflow, (5) Hiring Team. A Job is the public-facing posting and configuration container; one or more Requisitions (FR-M08-012) supply the funded Positions that a Job advertises. A Job carries a JOB_ code and a status of Open, Draft, On Hold or Archived. Every step supports Save as Draft and Cancel; the final step exposes Post.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin, I want a guided wizard to define a job, where it is posted, what the application asks, the interview stages, and who runs the hiring, so that a complete, consistent posting goes live in one flow.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Job Openings list shows tabs All Openings, Open, Drafts, On Hold and Archived with live counts, a "My Positions Only" filter, search, and columns Job Title & Job Code, Mapped Designation, Job Status, Remote Job, Location and Department.

- Step 1 Job Details (Basic Job Details) captures: Select Company (mandatory), Select Department (mandatory), Select Designation (mandatory), Employee Type (mandatory), Job Location (mandatory), Job Name on Careers / IJP / Refer pages (optional — defaults to the designation title if left blank), Job Tags, Tag as Remote Job (toggle), Job Description Summary, and Experience Range (From / To / unit).

- Step 1 also exposes Target Time To Fill (in days) and a Job Description block; where no JD is configured for the selected designation the system shows "No Job Description has been configured for the selected designation" with a Create Manually action.

- Step 1 includes an Add & Manage Positions surface (being superseded by the All Positions tab — path Job Openings > Job Details > All Positions) showing position counters (Total, Selected/Filled, Open, On-hold, Draft, Auto Archived, Archived) and a position table (Requisition ID, Position No, Position ID, Status, Recruiter, Specific Requirements) with bulk actions.

- Step 5 Hiring Team captures Select Hiring Lead (mandatory), Select Screening Team, Select Scheduling Team, Select Hiring Group, and Select Collaborator.

- Save as Draft persists an incomplete job in Draft status; Post transitions the job to Open and activates the configured posting channels (FR-M08-014).

**Business rules:**

- Job code uses the JOB_ prefix and is unique within the tenant.

- Only Recruitment Admin, HR Admin and Hiring Lead can create or post a job; Recruiters operate on jobs to which they are assigned (consistent with section 3.7.2 scope).

- A job cannot be posted until Step 1 mandatory fields, the Step 4 hiring workflow, and the Step 5 Hiring Lead are complete.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- Posting a job with no funded positions (no linked requisition) is allowed in Draft but warns at Post that the job will advertise zero open positions.

- Changing the mapped designation after a JD is created manually prompts whether to retain the manual JD or reload the designation default.

### FR-M08-012: Requisition raise — four-step wizard with New and Replacement positions

**Description: **A Requisition funds the Positions a Job fills and is raised via a four-step wizard: (1) Basic Details, (2) Job Details, (3) Position Selection, (4) Other Details. A single requisition can request New and Replacement positions, each configured individually. The Requisitions page summarises Total Requisitions, Total Positions, Active Offer Positions and Closed Positions, and lists each requisition with its JR_ code, designation/department/location, status, and position counts (Total with New/Replacement split, Active Evaluation, Active Offer, Draft, Closed).

**User story: ***As a Hiring Manager, I want to raise a requisition that captures the role plus the number of new and replacement positions and project-staffing details, so that recruiting against funded headcount is auditable and approval-gated.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Step 1 Basic Details captures Hiring Manager (mandatory), Company (mandatory), Department (mandatory) and Designation (mandatory).

- Step 2 Job Details captures Job Description (Create Manually where none exists), Experience Range (From / To / unit), Recruitment Start Date (mandatory), Hiring Lead (mandatory), and free-text Position Specific Requirements and Position Specific Skills for recruiter instructions beyond the standard JD.

- Step 3 Position Selection captures Number of New Position(s), Number of Replacement Position(s) and a computed Number of Position(s) total, enforcing the configured maximum (default 100 positions per requisition).

- Step 3 Position Details renders one row per position (legend New / Replacement) with Position Number, Location (mandatory), Replacement For (mandatory for replacement rows; NA for new), Reporting Manager, Employee Group (mandatory), Contribution Level (mandatory), Employee Type and Designation Alias; copy-to-all is available per column.

- Step 4 Other Details captures Comments / Instructions, Project Manager (mandatory) and Duration of Project (mandatory); project-staffing requisitions additionally capture Number of Rounds required, Interview Rounds, Client Location, Project Start Date and Customer Name.

- Submit routes the requisition through the configured approval flow; on approval the requisition becomes Approved Active and its positions become available to Jobs.

**Business rules:**

- Requisition code uses the JR_ prefix with a continuing counter (FR-M08-001); each position is addressable as {JR_code}:{position_no} (for example JR_328:4).

- Maximum positions per requisition is tenant-configurable (default 100).

- Who may raise requisitions and at what scope is governed by the Raise Requisition Scope configuration (LC03 / LC04).

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- A replacement position must reference the employee being replaced; the system blocks submission of a replacement row with an empty Replacement For.

- Reducing the position count below the number already linked to active offers is blocked.

### FR-M08-013: Per-job configurable hiring workflow and stage controls

**Description: **Each Job carries its own hiring workflow built from ordered stages (for example Shortlisting, Screening, Group Discussion, Technical Round 1..n, HR Round, Offer Stage). The workflow seeds from the company default and is editable per job. Stage-level controls govern parallel evaluation, pre-offer enablement and interviewer feedback access. The per-candidate Hiring Flow view tracks a candidate stage by stage.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin, I want to tailor the interview stages and stage behaviour per job so that each role follows the right hiring path without affecting other jobs.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Step 4 Hiring Workflow lets the user add (+ Add Round), reorder, rename, edit the evaluation type of, and delete stages; the first stage and the last stage (Offer Stage) cannot be deleted.

- Changes to a job hiring workflow apply only to candidates added after the change; in-flight candidates keep their original stage set.

- Toggles: "Can the interviews/evaluations be done in parallel?" (Yes/No); "Enable Pre-Offer?" (Yes/No); "Enable stage feedback access for Interviewers?" (Yes/No).

- When Pre-Offer is enabled the Pre-Offer field configuration in Step 3 Job Application must be completed; the system surfaces this dependency.

- The per-candidate Hiring Flow view renders each stage with its status (Completed, Selected, Pending for feedback, Pending for scheduling, Pending) and stage actions (Schedule Interview, Re-Schedule Interview, Mark as Completed, Initiate Pre-Offer), the interviewer panel (primary plus optional interviewers), the interviewer decision, event name, interview type (Online / Face to face), and interview From / To in the employee timezone.

**Business rules:**

- Pre-Offer is an optional stage gated by the per-job Enable Pre-Offer toggle; it is not mandatory for every job (this complements, and does not contradict, FR-M08-009).

- Interview types are restricted to the configured set (Face to face, Online — LC07).

- Stage feedback is visible to interviewers only when the per-job toggle is enabled.

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- Deleting a stage that currently holds candidates is blocked; the stage may be deleted only once empty or the change is scoped to future candidates.

- Marking a stage Completed while interviewer feedback is still pending warns the actor before proceeding.

### FR-M08-014: Per-channel posting windows and the application field-visibility matrix

**Description: **Step 2 Job Posting controls where and when a job is advertised; Step 3 Job Application controls what each channel application form asks. Posting channels are Careers Page, Refer, IJP, External Recruiter, Job Boards, Social Networks and Custom Sources / Links. The application form is configured field by field with independent View and Mandatory settings per channel.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin, I want to control the posting window per channel and the exact fields each channel applicants must complete, so that the candidate experience and the data captured match each source.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Job Posting Options lists each channel (Careers Page, Refer, IJP) with Display From, Display To, a Job Status (Active / Inactive) and an activate/deactivate action; a posting is visible on a channel only within its Display window.

- The Sources tab exposes Careers Page, Refer, IJP, External Recruiter, Job Boards, Social Networks and Custom Sources / Links; applicable channels carry a per-job re-application window ("No. of days before re-application by candidate via [channel] for this job", default 180).

- Step 3 Job Application presents a field matrix grouped by section (Resume, Biographical, Address, Contact, Emergency, Education, Work Experience, Skill, Employment, Personal Identity and further sections). Each field carries a Display Name in Application plus per-channel toggle pairs: Careers View / Careers Mandatory, IJP View / IJP Mandatory, Refer View / Refer Mandatory, and Pre-Offer View.

- Resume parsing is configurable per channel (Careers, IJP, Refer) and per country (for example India).

- Step 3 also exposes Pre Screening Settings and Screener Fields sub-tabs, plus View JD and Preview Application actions.

**Business rules:**

- A field set Mandatory for a channel must also be set View for that channel.

- Source tagging remains platform-mandatory at candidate addition (FR-M08-008); channel configuration governs the application form, not whether a source is recorded.

- Job Boards and Social Networks posting respects the configured portals (Glassdoor, LinkedIn, Naukri — LC08) and any cross-border data-residency constraints (Phase 2).

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- A Display To date earlier than the Display From date is rejected.

- Disabling a field View across all channels removes it from every application form for that job; the system warns if that field is otherwise mandatory at onboarding.

### FR-M08-015: Offer letter generation wizard and extended offer lifecycle

**Description: **Offers are generated from the Offer Letter workspace via a three-step wizard — (1) Offer Letter, (2) Job / Candidate Details, (3) Pay Details — with Template, Preview and Approval tabs. The workspace tracks each offer through an explicit lifecycle from approval through candidate acceptance and conversion to an employee record. This extends FR-M08-004 (CTC-threshold approval) with the screen-level fields, statuses and approval-email configuration.

**User story: ***As a Recruitment Admin or HR Admin, I want to assemble an offer, preview it, route it for approval, and track it to acceptance and conversion, so that offer issuance is controlled and visible end to end.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Step 1 Offer Letter captures Offer Expiry Date (mandatory) and Template (mandatory).

- Step 2 Job / Candidate Details captures Company (mandatory), Department (mandatory), Designation (mandatory), Location, Employee Type, Reporting Manager, Probation Period, Designation Alias, HRBP, Dotted Line Manager, Contribution Level, First Name (mandatory), Middle / Last / Legal Name, and Date of Joining.

- Step 3 Pay Details captures Choose Salary Structure (Old / New), Pay Scale Group, Salary Structure, Currency, Fixed CTC, Show Total CTC in Salary Breakup (toggle), Differently Abled, Metro, Previous Total CTC and Percentage Fixed CTC Increment.

- The Approval tab composes the approver email (editable subject and rich-text body with merge fields), CC users and CC roles (Myself / Hiring Lead / Admin), an optional Trigger Custom Exception Flow, and Approver-Specific and Candidate-Specific attachments; Send for Approval routes the offer. No approver email fires when there are no approvers.

- The Offer Letter list is scoped by Company and grouped into Active Offers, Rejected Offers and Completed Offers, with status filters: Offers Pending For Approval, Offers Approved And To Be Shared With The Candidate, Offers Pending With The Candidate, Offers Accepted And To Be Added To The Pending List, In The Pending List, Employee Movement Initiated, and Employee Movement Approved.

- Send Reminder composes a status-specific reminder email (for example "Pending from Candidate") to the relevant party.

- On candidate acceptance the offer moves to Accepted And To Be Added To The Pending List; conversion proceeds via Employee Movement Initiated then Employee Movement Approved, which triggers the Candidate to Pre-joining handover (FR-M08-005).

**Business rules:**

- Offer generation is restricted to Recruitment Admin and HR Admin (joint authority); Recruiters cannot generate offers (FR-M08-004). CEO co-signature still applies above the CTC threshold (FR-M08-004).

- Offer-list position references use the {JR_code}:{position_no} convention (for example JR_328:4).

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- An offer past its Offer Expiry Date with no candidate response moves to an expired / rejected state and frees the position.

- If approvers are configured but none act within SLA, the offer escalates per the approval flow or the custom exception flow.

### FR-M08-016: Recruitment self-service and operational surfaces

**Description: **Beyond admin configuration, M08 provides operational dashboards and employee / interviewer self-service surfaces: a recruiter Overview, the per-candidate Hiring Flow (FR-M08-013), an interviewer My Interviews surface, employee IJP Openings and IJP Jobs Applied, the Refer page, My Referrals, and Link Accounts.

**User story: ***As a recruiter, interviewer or employee, I want role-appropriate surfaces to action recruiting tasks, conduct interviews, apply internally and refer candidates, so that recruiting work is centralised and visible.*

**Acceptance criteria:**

- Overview shows Priority Tasks and Follow-Ups tabs with counts and per-task Act actions (for example "Add [candidate] to Pending List", "Schedule [round] for N candidate(s)") with due dates and job reference; an All Tasks panel summarises Offer Generation, My Approvals, Hiring Stage Tasks, Screening / Shortlisting and Misc Tasks counts; and an Events panel (Self / Team).

- All Candidates list supports search by Name / Email / Phone / Candidate ID, columns Candidate Name & ID (CAN_ code), CV, Experience, Email & Phone, Job Applied and contextual Actions (for example Screen, Schedule [round]) with a per-row overflow menu; add-candidate, filter, view and export controls are available.

- My Interviews (interviewer view) shows Upcoming Interviews and History tabs, a date strip, and a Pending Feedback panel.

- IJP Openings lists internal postings (Job Title & Job Code, Remote Job, Company Name, Location, Department & Business Unit, Employee Type, Expires on) searchable by job code or title; IJP Jobs Applied lets an employee track their internal applications (Job, Job Status, Email & Phone, Applied Date, Status, Action).

- Refer lists referable openings; My Referrals tracks an employee submitted referrals; Link Accounts lets an employee link external accounts for referral / application purposes.

**Business rules:**

- IJP and Refer surfaces honour the per-job channel posting windows and field configuration (FR-M08-014) and the duplicity / re-application rules (FR-M08-003).

- Interviewer surfaces honour the per-job "stage feedback access for interviewers" toggle (FR-M08-013).

**Edge cases ****&**** error handling:**

- An IJP application from an employee who does not meet the configured eligibility is blocked with the reason surfaced.

- Tasks for jobs a recruiter is not assigned to do not appear in that recruiter Overview.

