| DM16 | Default category seed | Eight categories at the post-migration go-live per §B.1. Migrated from Darwinbox HR_Policies_Export. New categories added by Document Admin. | CLOSED |
| DM17 | Document master scope | Eighteen document types in C.1 — identity, education, contract, statutory. Drives M02 cluster contents and M03 separation release. Shared master across M11, M01, M02, M03. | CLOSED |
| DM19 | Vault access matrix | Per §C.2 — Employee sees own only · HRBP scoped to subordinates · HR Admin / Document Admin / Org Admin tenant-wide · Auditor read-only. | CLOSED |
| DM20 | Letter template inventory | Seventeen templates per D.1. Covers full lifecycle from offer to FnF. | CLOSED |
| DM21 | Merge field catalogue | 24 standard merge fields across EMP / PAY / OFFER / SEP / SYS namespaces. Every template field must resolve at Publish time. | CLOSED |
| DM22 | Signature configuration | CEO + HR Admin on Offer and Termination · HR Admin on all other standard letters · escalate_signature flag for elevated disciplinary cases. | CLOSED |
| DM23 | Bulk letter throughput | 500 letters per 10 minutes. Asynchronous queue with per-record success/failure log. | CLOSED |
| DM24 | Sign-off task SLA | Policy sign-off SLA = 14 days with reminders at 7/12/14 · escalation to Manager L1 at 15 · HRBP at 21. Letter acknowledgement SLA = 7 days. | CLOSED |
| DM25 | Acknowledgement record fields | 11 fields per E.2 including IP, device fingerprint, and acknowledgement text version for non-repudiation. | CLOSED |
| DM26 | User assignment dimensions | 9 dimensions per F.1 — department, location, designation, grade, employment type, entity, lifecycle state, custom group, reporting chain. | CLOSED |
| DM27 | Role permissions | Per §F.3 matrix. Document Admin owns category/policy/letter configuration. Letter Admin capability flag owns letter templates only. Auditor read-only across all surfaces. | CLOSED |
| DM01 | Module scope — letter generation in M11? | IN M11. Letter templates, merge fields, render engine, signature embedding, and bulk generation all belong to M11. Consuming modules (M02, M03, M08, M09, M10) invoke M11 to render; they do not own template logic. | May 2026 |
| DM05 | Acknowledgement text — per-policy override | No per-policy override in Phase 1. Single global text per A.2 applies to all policies. Per-template override considered for Phase 2. | May 2026 |
| DM09 | Document Admin role and Letter Admin capability flag | Document Admin = distinct Module Admin role (matches Leave Admin / Attendance Admin / Onboarding Admin pattern in RBAC §4). Letter Admin = capability flag on Document Admin / HR Admin, not a separate role (parallel to BGV Admin in M02 DO11). | May 2026 |
| DM14 | Retention windows | Statutory PII · Contract documents · Non-statutory PII all retained 7 years post-exit (or per local regulation, whichever is longer). Policy documents indefinite while published · 10 years post-archival. Acknowledgement records indefinite (ledger backbone). | May 2026 |
| DM18 | Right-of-erasure carve-out for sign-off records | Sign-off and acknowledgement records (E.2) are NOT erasable under DPDPA right-of-erasure. They form the non-repudiation backbone for compliance documents the employee signed during employment. | May 2026 |

## 6.1 Authentication & Authorisation

All API endpoints require a valid authenticated session. Authentication mechanisms:

- JWT bearer tokens with HMAC-SHA256 signing. Access token lifetime: 15 minutes. Refresh token lifetime: 7 days, rotated on every use.

- Google SSO via OAuth 2.0 with PKCE flow. Tenant-configured Google Workspace domain.

- Username/password with bcrypt hashing (cost factor 12).

- MFA required for HR Admin and Organisation Admin roles. TOTP (RFC 6238) or SMS OTP.

Authorisation enforcement is multi-layered:

- Module-level: every endpoint declares its required module access; checked against user’s role assignments.

- Field-level: response payloads are filtered at the application layer to remove fields the requestor cannot view.

- Row-level: database queries are scoped at the data access layer via row-level security policies (tenant_id, entity_id, data_scope predicates).

## 6.2 Standard Response Format

All API endpoints return JSON. Success responses use HTTP 2xx with the resource payload. Error responses use HTTP 4xx or 5xx with a standardised error format:

| **Field** | **Type** | **Description** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| error.code | string | Stable machine-readable error code (e.g. FIELD_ACCESS_DENIED, VALIDATION_FAILED, RECORD_NOT_FOUND, RATE_LIMITED). |
| error.message | string | Human-readable English message. |
| error.field | string | For VALIDATION_FAILED, the specific field that failed. |
| error.details | object | Additional context for the error. |

Example error response:

*{** ****“error”****: {** ****“code”****:** ****“VALIDATION_FAILED”****,** ****“message”****:** ****“Nominee percentage sum must equal 100 per class.”****,** ****“field”****:** ****“nominee_percentage.GRATUITY”****,** ****“details”****: {** ****“current_sum”****: 80 } } }*

## 6.3 Rate Limiting

- Per-user rate limits: 600 requests/minute on read endpoints, 60 requests/minute on write endpoints.

- Bulk endpoints (upload, export): 5 concurrent operations per tenant.

- AI Chat Agent: 30 queries/minute per user; 1000 queries/day per tenant.

- Rate-limit responses return HTTP 429 with Retry-After header indicating seconds until reset.

