## 6.6 External Integrations

| **Integration** | **Direction** | **Protocol** | **Purpose** | **Phase 1?** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Naukri job board | Outbound | REST API + scheduled sync | Publish requisitions; receive applications | Yes |
| LinkedIn Jobs | Outbound | REST API | Publish requisitions | Yes |
| Careers portal (PrimeSoft) | Bidirectional | REST API | Application intake, candidate updates | Yes |
| BGV vendor (primary) | Bidirectional | REST API + webhook | Verification case creation, result webhook | Yes |
| Biometric device protocol | Inbound | Device-specific TCP + webhook normaliser | Punch event ingestion | Yes |
| Calendar (iCal) | Outbound | SMTP + iCal attachment | Interview invites, meeting scheduling | Yes |
| Anthropic Claude API | Outbound | REST API | Chat Agent grounding queries | Yes |
| SMTP email gateway | Outbound | SMTP/SES | Notification dispatch | Yes |
| SMS gateway | Outbound | REST API | OTP, urgent notifications | Yes |
| Google SSO | Inbound auth | OAuth 2.0 + PKCE | Identity federation | Yes |
| EPFO portal (ECR) | Outbound file | File generation only | PF challan output | Phase 2 |
| ESIC portal | Outbound file | File generation only | ESI challan output | Phase 2 |
| TRACES portal | Outbound file | File generation only | TDS quarterly Form 24Q | Phase 2 |
| Bank disbursement | Outbound file | NEFT/RTGS file format | Salary disbursement | Phase 2 |

Integration governance principles:

- All outbound API credentials are encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM with per-tenant KMS keys.

- All inbound webhooks require HMAC signature verification using a per-integration secret.

- Integration calls are logged in security_audit_log with endpoint, timestamp, response status, latency. Payload hashes (SHA-256) are logged — never raw content.

- Retry policy: exponential backoff with jitter, max 5 retries, dead-letter queue after final failure.

- Circuit breaker pattern applied to each external integration — failing endpoints are short-circuited for 60 seconds to prevent cascading delays.

# 7. Non-Functional Requirements

## 7.1 Performance

| **Metric** | **Target** | **Measurement** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Standard API p95 latency | < 500 ms under 300 concurrent users | Synthetic load test against staging matching production topology |
| Cached-read API p95 latency | < 300 ms | Same conditions |
| Write API p95 latency | < 1500 ms | Same conditions |
| Largest Contentful Paint (page load on 4G) | < 2.5 seconds | Synthetic Lighthouse and field RUM |
| Bulk upload — 500 employee records | < 90 seconds end-to-end | Wave-1 dry-run pattern |
| Report generation — standard reports | < 30 seconds | Synthetic |
| Chat Agent response (end-to-end including AI API call) | < 8 seconds | P95 measurement across all queries |
| Org chart drill-down (≤ 4 levels) | p95 < 1500 ms | Per BRS D.1 / M01 §J.1 |
| Dashboard widget initial render | < 2 seconds for first byte; < 4 seconds for full widget | RUM measurement |
| Search and filter on employee directory | < 1 second for 500-employee tenants | Functional test |

**M17 Assets & IT service-desk performance targets. **The asset and service-desk surfaces carry module-specific performance and operational NFRs:

- Asset list / search: p95 < 800 ms for up to 10,000 records; asset record view p95 < 500 ms including assignment history.

- Ticket creation p95 < 1.5 s; agent queue view p95 < 800 ms for up to 200 tickets; KB search p95 < 600 ms; catalog browse p95 < 700 ms.

- Bulk asset import (5,000 rows): dry-run < 60 s, full run < 5 minutes.

- SLA timer accuracy ± 30 seconds (± 5 seconds for P1); audit emission to P05 within 5 s of every state change.

- Concurrent ticket creation peak 100 tickets/minute sustained for 15 minutes; notification delivery within 60 s (p95).

- Service desk surface availability 99.5% during business hours; the P1 incident creation path is 24×7 firm.

- Agent leave handoff: auto-reassignment within 5 minutes of leave start.

## 7.2 Availability & Reliability

| **Metric** | **Target** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Uptime | ≥ 99.5% per calendar month | Equivalent to ≤ 3.6 hours of downtime per month |
| Recovery Time Objective (RTO) | < 4 hours | For any failure scenario |
| Recovery Point Objective (RPO) | < 1 hour | Maximum data loss |
| Maintenance window | Sunday 01:00 – 04:00 IST | Pre-announced; user-impacting changes only |
| Production deployments | Zero-downtime | Blue-green or rolling deployment pattern |
| Backup frequency | Continuous (transaction log) + hourly snapshot + daily full backup | Test restores monthly |
| Database failover | Automatic to standby replica | < 30 seconds detection + < 60 seconds failover |

## 7.3 Scalability

- Concurrent active users — 300 in Release 1 without performance degradation.

- Per-tenant scale — 500 active employees plus 5 years of historical data in Release 1.

- Architecture must support up to 100 tenants without re-engineering. the post-migration go-live operates at single-tenant scale.

- Application layer is stateless — all state lives in the database, cache, or object storage. Horizontal scaling by adding application servers behind the load balancer.

- Database read replicas for reporting and read-heavy workloads. Write-master with synchronous and asynchronous replication patterns.

- Background job queue (Phase 1: jobs entity) is horizontally scalable — multiple worker processes can consume from the queue.

- AI Chat Agent calls are rate-limited per tenant to prevent runaway costs (1000 queries/day per tenant in Phase 1).

## 7.4 Security

| **Control** | **Implementation** | **Verification** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TLS in transit | TLS 1.3 minimum enforced. No fallback to TLS 1.2 or below. | Automated weekly scan |
| Encryption at rest | AES-256-GCM with per-tenant KMS-managed keys. Envelope encryption for key rotation without data re-encryption. | Audit at deployment time |
| MFA enforcement | Required for HR Admin and Organisation Admin roles by default. TOTP and SMS OTP supported. | Configuration audit at provisioning |
| PII access logging | 100% of Tier 1 PII access events logged in security_audit_log with viewer, field, employee, timestamp, IP. | Continuous audit |
| VAPT | External Vulnerability Assessment & Penetration Testing ahead of the single post-migration go-live. Zero Critical / High CVEs in production at go-live. | Pre-go-live gate |
| Application security scanning | Automated SAST and DAST on every deployment. | CI/CD pipeline |
| Dependency scanning | Daily scan of all dependencies for known vulnerabilities (e.g. via Dependabot, Snyk). | CI/CD pipeline + daily report |
| Secrets management | All credentials (database, integration API keys, encryption keys) stored in dedicated secrets management; never in code or environment files committed to source control. | Audit at deployment |
| Session management | Server-side session store. Access tokens 15 min, refresh tokens 7 days rotated on use. Logout invalidates refresh token immediately. | Functional test |
| IP restriction | Configurable per tenant by Organisation Admin. Login attempts from outside the allowed IP range are blocked at API gateway. | Configuration audit |
| Account lockout | Configurable threshold (default 5) and duration (default 30 min). All lockout events logged. | Functional test |
| CSRF protection | Synchroniser-token pattern on all state-changing requests. SameSite cookie attribute set. | Automated test |
| XSS protection | Content Security Policy headers. All user input HTML-escaped at output. No inline JavaScript. | Automated test + manual review |
| SQL injection protection | Parameterised queries only. No string concatenation for SQL. | Code review + automated test |

## 7.5 Data Integrity

- No hard deletes on any table — soft delete with deleted_at, deleted_by timestamp/user only.

- Foreign key constraints enforced at database layer for all relationships.

- Unique constraints enforced at database layer for: employee_id (per tenant), company_email (per tenant), pan (per active employees), Aadhaar (per active employees), asset_tag (per tenant), serial_number (per asset_category).

- 100% of mutations captured in immutable audit_log via database trigger — no application bug can suppress an audit entry.

- Consistency: all multi-table operations executed in database transactions. Partial commits not permitted.

- Statutory data has legally mandated retention periods — hard delete is blocked at both application and database layers.

- Audit log retention minimum 7 years. After 2 years, entries may be archived to cold storage but must remain queryable within 24 hours.

## 7.6 Compliance

- DPDPA 2023 — Consent capture at onboarding, right of access (employee can export own record with PII unmasked), right of correction via sensitive-field change workflow, right of erasure for non-statutory data (statutory data has mandated retention), data principal request register, data fiduciary obligations.

- POSH Act 2013 — Mandatory policy publication and acknowledgement, complaint intake via M01 Grievance Register with anonymous opt-in, ICC routing for POSH-category grievances, training tracking via M11.

- Shops & Establishments Act — State-wise leave entitlements and working-hour rules; location-based policy overrides.

- Audit log structure complies with legal evidentiary requirements — timestamp, actor, IP, user agent, before-value, after-value (PII masked).

## 7.7 Accessibility

- WCAG 2.1 AA compliance — all web screens pass automated accessibility checks.

- Keyboard navigation — all interactive elements reachable and operable via keyboard only.

- Screen reader compatibility — semantic HTML, ARIA labels where appropriate.

- Colour contrast — minimum 4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for large text and UI components.

- Touch target minimum size 44 × 44 px on all interactive elements (mobile breakpoint 375 px).

- No content reliant on colour alone for meaning — supplementary indicators (icons, labels) provided.

## 7.8 Browser & Platform Support

- Modern evergreen browsers — latest two major versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari.

- No support for Internet Explorer (deprecated).

- Responsive web breakpoints: 375 px (mobile), 768 px (tablet), 1280 px (desktop).

- Native mobile applications and offline capability are Phase 2 deliverables — out of Phase 1 scope.

## 7.9 Maintainability

- Test coverage minimum 80% for backend code, 70% for frontend code, measured via automated coverage tooling on CI.

- Documentation maintained for: API endpoints (OpenAPI / Swagger), database schema (auto-generated from migrations), deployment runbooks, incident response playbooks.

- All configuration externalised from code — environment variables, secrets management, database configuration tables.

- Logging structured (JSON) with correlation IDs propagated across requests, queue jobs, and integration calls.

- Monitoring — metrics, traces, and logs in a unified observability platform. Alerting on SLO breaches.

# 8. Workflow & State Diagrams

This section captures the state machines that drive Phase 1 module behaviour. State transitions are presented as tables (Current State → Action → Next State → Side Effects) to be precise and unambiguous for the build.

## 8.1 Employee Lifecycle State Machine (M01)

This state machine starts where the M08 candidate state machine (§8.6) ends. The handoff occurs when M08 emits the offer_accepted event on candidate countersignature, which causes M01 to create the employees row and set lifecycle_state = PRE_JOINING. The Candidate starting state shown below is a label for the moment immediately preceding handoff — M01 does not actually hold the candidate; M08 does, per §8.6 Table 8.6.2.

| **Current State** | **Action / Trigger** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| (none) | Candidate added to ATS (M08) — handoff boundary, see §8.6 | Candidate (M08-owned) | candidates row created in M08. No M01 record. |
| Candidate | Offer countersigned by candidate (M08) | Pre-joining | employees row created. employee_id assigned. lifecycle_state = PRE_JOINING. Pre-joining portal access activated. |
| Candidate | Offer withdrawn / declined | (soft-deleted) | candidates state → OFFER_DECLINED. No M01 record created. |
| Pre-joining | Onboarding completes (M02) | Active (probation) | lifecycle_state = ACTIVE. probation_flag = TRUE. Full self-service access activated. Joining letter (M11) generated and stored. |
| Pre-joining | Pre-joining cancelled (HR Admin) | (soft-deleted) | Soft-delete of employees row. |
| Active (probation) | Probation confirmation (M09) | Active (confirmed) | probation_flag = FALSE. probation_end_date set. Confirmation letter (M11) generated. Full leave types unlocked per M04 rules. |
| Active (probation) | Probation extension (M09) | Active (probation) | New employment_history version with extended probation_end_date. |
| Active (probation) | Not confirmed (M09) | Notice | Triggers separation flow (M03) with category = INVOLUNTARY. |
| Active (any) | Resignation submitted and approved (M03) | Notice | separation_records.state = APPROVED then ON_NOTICE. Notice clock starts. Staged future-dated employment changes auto-cancelled. |
| Active (any) | Absconding detected (M05 — 7 calendar days) | Absconded | absconding_flagged_at set. HR Admin notification queued. Access restricted. |
| Active (any) | HR Admin force-initiates separation with past-dated FLWD | Separated | ONE-WAY DOOR. Immediate deactivation. Reactivation blocked — only rehire via M08. |
| Notice | LWD reached (scheduled job) | Last Working Day | FnF clearance section unlocked. Limited module access — FnF clearance only. |
| Notice | Resignation revoked (employee or HR Admin) before LWD | Active | separation_records.state = REVOKED. Notice clock cleared. Access restored. |
| Last Working Day | All FnF clearances completed (M03) | Separated | Read-only flag set. lifecycle_state = SEPARATED. read_only_until = LWD + 180 days. Self-service reduced to own payslip / document view. |
| Absconded | HR Admin converts to separation (M03) | Separated | separation_records.state = CONVERTED_FROM_ABSCONDING. |
| Absconded | HR Admin restores | Active | absconding_flagged_at cleared. Access restored. Audit-logged. |
| Separated | Rehire (M08 new application) | (new employees row) | New employees row created with previous_employee_id = old.id. group_date_of_joining preserved. |

## 8.2 Leave Application Workflow (M04)

| **Current State** | **Action** | **Next State** | **Side Effects / Rules** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | Employee submits application | SUBMITTED | applied_on_date set. L1 Manager notified. SLA timer starts (10 days). |
| SUBMITTED | L1 Manager (or eligible role) approves Stage 1 | STAGE_1_APPROVED (if two-stage) OR APPROVED (if single-stage) | stage_1_decision_at set. For two-stage types (ML/ADL/MCL/SPL/SBL), routed to HRBP / HR Admin / Leave Admin. |
| SUBMITTED | L1 Manager rejects | REJECTED | Mandatory rejection_reason captured. Employee notified. |
| SUBMITTED | 10 days inaction | ESCALATED | escalation_fired_at set. Next-level manager + HRBP + HR Admin notified. |
| SUBMITTED / STAGE_1_APPROVED | Employee withdraws | WITHDRAWN | Balance not deducted. Reversible — employee can resubmit. |
| STAGE_1_APPROVED | HRBP / HR Admin / Leave Admin approves Stage 2 | APPROVED | stage_2_decision_at set. Balance deducted. Employee notified. |
| STAGE_1_APPROVED | Stage 2 approver rejects | REJECTED | Mandatory reason. Balance not deducted (was held pending). |
| APPROVED (past-dated) | HRBP / Leave Admin / HR Admin revokes | REVOKED | Balance restored. Audit-logged with reason. |

## 8.3 Attendance Request Workflow (M05)

| **Current State** | **Action** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | Employee submits (regularisation, OD, OT, etc.) | SUBMITTED | applied_on_date set. L1 Manager notified. SLA timer starts (5 days standard; 2-hourly on 24th-25th of month). |
| SUBMITTED | L1 Manager / HRBP / HR Admin / Attendance Admin approves | APPROVED | decision_at set. attendance_records updated accordingly (e.g. Status = PRESENT for regularisation, status = OUT_DUTY for Out Duty). |
| SUBMITTED | Approver rejects | REJECTED | Mandatory reason. Underlying attendance_record remains absent / unchanged. |
| SUBMITTED | 5 days inaction (24th-25th: 2 hours) | ESCALATED | Next-level manager + HR Admin + Attendance Admin notified simultaneously. |
| SUBMITTED / APPROVED | Employee withdraws | WITHDRAWN | If APPROVED, attendance_records reverts to prior status. |
| — | Submit when monthly limit reached | (blocked) | Submission blocked. Error: REGULARISATION_LIMIT_EXCEEDED. |

## 8.4 Separation Workflow (M03)

[Prototype sync — June 2026] The clearance phase of the separation state machine includes a Timesheet clearance node (clear/pending), gating Full-and-Final settlement alongside the other clearance gates.

| **Current State** | **Action** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | Employee submits resignation OR HR Admin force-initiates | SUBMITTED | separation_records created. L1 Manager notified. |
| SUBMITTED | L1 Manager approves (Stage 1) | (awaiting Stage 2) | approval_stage_1_at set. HR Admin notified. |
| SUBMITTED | L1 Manager rejects | REJECTED | Rejection reason mandatory. Employee notified. |
| (awaiting Stage 2) | HR Admin approves (Stage 2) | APPROVED → ON_NOTICE | approval_stage_2_at set. lifecycle_state = NOTICE. Notice clock starts. Staged future-dated changes cancelled. Exit interview scheduled at LWD-7. |
| (awaiting Stage 2) | HR Admin approves with past-dated FLWD | APPROVED → SEPARATED (one-way door) | Immediate deactivation. Warning shown and confirmed. |
| ON_NOTICE | Employee or HR Admin revokes (before LWD) | REVOKED | lifecycle_state restored to Active. Notice clock cleared. |
| ON_NOTICE | Revoke requested while “block until revoke approved” is set | (revoke pending) | Revoke routed through the row / Default Approval Flow On Revoke; separation stays ON_NOTICE until the revoke is approved (block_until_revoke_approval_complete). |
| ON_NOTICE | LWD reached while “Force separate on LWD” is enabled | SEPARATED | Auto-separation on the computed LWD per policy (force_separate_on_lwd); FnF clearance completion still gated per Part E / E.1. |
| ON_NOTICE | LWD reached | LWD | FnF clearance workflow initiated. Limited access. |
| LWD | All FnF clearances complete + HR Admin marks FnF complete | FNF_COMPLETE | FnF payroll settlement (Phase 2) ready. Asset returns confirmed. |
| FNF_COMPLETE | Final separation (HR Admin) | SEPARATED | Read-only access. Separation letter (M11) generated. read_only_until set to LWD + 180 days. |

## 8.5 Onboarding State Machine (M02)

| **Current State** | **Action / Trigger** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | Auto-initiation (14 days before DOJ) OR manual initiation | INITIATED | onboarding_instances created. Pre-joining portal access activated. Welcome email sent. |
| INITIATED | Candidate starts form | FORM_IN_PROGRESS | Auto-save every 30 seconds. onboarding_form_responses rows created in DRAFT state. |
| FORM_IN_PROGRESS | Candidate submits form | DOCUMENTS_PENDING | Field responses moved to SUBMITTED. Document upload tasks surfaced. |
| DOCUMENTS_PENDING | All required documents uploaded | BGV_IN_PROGRESS | BGV vendor case created. Verification Reports tab populated. |
| BGV_IN_PROGRESS | All BGV checks return VERIFIED or admin disposition complete | ADMIN_REVIEW | Onboarding Admin notified for final review. |
| ADMIN_REVIEW | Onboarding Admin marks complete | COMPLETED | M01 lifecycle_state transitions to ACTIVE. Sign-off cluster acknowledgements verified. |
| (any) | Cancellation (HR Admin) | CANCELLED | Employee record soft-deleted. Pre-joining portal access revoked. |

## 8.6 Candidate State Machine (M08)

This state machine covers the M08 candidate lifecycle from initial application through final offer countersignature. On countersignature (OFFER_EXTENDED → OFFER_ACCEPTED), the candidate hands off to M01 — the employee lifecycle machine in §8.1 takes over with lifecycle_state = PRE_JOINING.

The legacy direct INTERVIEW → OFFER_PROPOSED transition is retained as an opt-in shortcut for organisations that don’t use pre-offers (controlled by a tenant-level toggle on the M08 settings).

| **Current State** | **Action** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | Candidate added (manual or job board) | NEW | candidates row created. Duplicity check applied (FR-M08-003). |
| NEW | Recruiter starts screening | SCREENING | Screening tasks tracked. |
| SCREENING | Candidate passes screening | SHORTLISTED | Visible to hiring panel. |
| SCREENING / SHORTLISTED | Rejected (any reason) | REJECTED | Candidate notified per template. |
| SHORTLISTED | Interview scheduled | INTERVIEW | interviews row created. Calendar invites sent (FR-M08-007). |
| INTERVIEW | All rounds completed positively | INTERVIEW_PASSED | Hiring panel formally recommends hire. interviews.outcome = PASSED. |
| INTERVIEW_PASSED | RA / HR Admin opens pre-offer flow | PRE_OFFER_PROPOSED | Pre-offer issuance flow initiated by RA / HR Admin (FR-M08-009). |
| INTERVIEW_PASSED | Pre-offer disabled at tenant — direct-offer shortcut | OFFER_PROPOSED | Legacy direct-offer path (skip pre-offer). |
| PRE_OFFER_PROPOSED | RA / HR Admin issues Pre-offer (LTR_IOI) | PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED | Pre-offer email + portal link sent to candidate. |
| PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED | Candidate accepts | PRE_OFFER_ACCEPTED | Document collection workflow auto-initiates; checklist derived from M11 DM17 (mandatory_at_onboarding = Yes). |
| PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED | Candidate declines | OFFER_DECLINED | Recruiter notified; requisition slot freed. |
| PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED | Validity expires (default 5 working days, configurable per tenant) | PRE_OFFER_EXPIRED | One extension allowed with reason capture. |
| PRE_OFFER_EXPIRED | RA / HR Admin re-extends | PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED | Validity clock resets. |
| PRE_OFFER_ACCEPTED | Candidate uploads documents | DOCUMENT_REVIEW | Documents staged in M11 vault (DM13); review queue surfaces them to RA / HR Admin. |
| DOCUMENT_REVIEW | Admin marks all mandatory docs Verified | DOCUMENT_REVIEW_PASSED | candidates.verification_status = PASSED. Final Offer auto-drafts with verified CTC. |
| DOCUMENT_REVIEW_PASSED | RA / HR Admin releases final offer | OFFER_PROPOSED | Final Offer flow becomes available (FR-M08-004). |
| DOCUMENT_REVIEW | Admin marks doc as Discrepancy (CTC mismatch, designation mismatch, etc.) | DOCUMENT_REVIEW_FLAGGED | Notification to candidate with discrepancy category; re-upload requested. |
| DOCUMENT_REVIEW_FLAGGED | Candidate re-uploads and admin verifies | DOCUMENT_REVIEW | Re-verification cycle (max 2 cycles before HRBP escalation). |
| DOCUMENT_REVIEW_FLAGGED | Discrepancy unresolved and admin re-negotiates band | PRE_OFFER_REVISION | One revision permitted before final Offer (FR-M08-009). |
| DOCUMENT_REVIEW | Material fraud detected | BLACKLISTED | Audit-logged with reason; candidate cannot re-apply for 24 months. |
| DOCUMENT_REVIEW | Candidate fails to upload all docs in 14 days | HRBP_ESCALATION | HRBP decides extension or withdrawal. |
| PRE_OFFER_REVISION | RA revises Pre-offer | PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED | One revision permitted; candidate must accept revision. |
| OFFER_PROPOSED | CEO approval (if > CTC threshold) | OFFER_EXTENDED | CEO co-signature applied to offer letter; offer sent to candidate. |
| OFFER_PROPOSED | Below threshold — RA / HR Admin extends | OFFER_EXTENDED | Offer sent to candidate. |
| OFFER_EXTENDED | Candidate countersigns | OFFER_ACCEPTED | M01 employee record created (FR-M08-005). lifecycle_state = PRE_JOINING. Candidate state → ONBOARDING. |
| OFFER_EXTENDED | Candidate declines | OFFER_DECLINED | Audit-logged with decline reason if provided. |
| OFFER_EXTENDED | Validity expires | OFFER_EXPIRED | RA re-extension possible. |

**State machine note.** Eleven new states were added to support the pre-offer flow: PRE_OFFER_PROPOSED, PRE_OFFER_EXTENDED, PRE_OFFER_ACCEPTED, PRE_OFFER_EXPIRED, PRE_OFFER_REVISION, DOCUMENT_REVIEW, BLACKLISTED, HRBP_ESCALATION. Tenant-level toggle enable_pre_offer_flow defaults to true on new tenants; existing tenants migrating from Darwinbox default to false to preserve historical behaviour and can opt in at any time.

## 8.7 Requisition State Machine (M08)

| **Current State** | **Action** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | Hiring Lead drafts requisition | DRAFT | requisitions row created with status DRAFT. |
| DRAFT | Submitted for approval | (in workflow) | Workflow instance initiated. |
| (in workflow) | Approval workflow completes positively | APPROVED | Requisition becomes available for job board posting. |
| APPROVED | Job posted (manual or auto) | OPEN | opened_at set. Job boards updated via outbound integration. |
| OPEN | Position filled (offer accepted, positions_filled = positions_count) | CLOSED | closed_at set. Outbound ‘closed’ notifications to job boards. |
| OPEN | Hiring Lead pauses | ON_HOLD | Visible only internally. |
| ON_HOLD | Resume | OPEN | Job re-posted to boards if previously syndicated. |
| (any) | Cancel | CANCELLED | Candidates notified per template. Job boards de-posted. |

## 8.7a Offer Lifecycle State Machine (M08)

This machine covers an offer from generation through approval, candidate response, and conversion to an employee record, as surfaced in the Offer Letter workspace (FR-M08-015). It refines the offers.approval_status and offers.candidate_acceptance_status enums (4.9.5) with the operational offer_lifecycle_state (4.9.18). On Employee Movement Approved the Candidate → Pre-joining handover in §8.6 / FR-M08-005 fires.

| **Current State** | **Action** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | RA / HR Admin generates offer and sends for approval | PENDING_FOR_APPROVAL | Approver email triggered (no email if there are no approvers). |
| PENDING_FOR_APPROVAL | Approver approves | APPROVED_TO_SHARE_WITH_CANDIDATE | Offer ready to share with candidate. |
| PENDING_FOR_APPROVAL | Approver rejects | REJECTED | Moves to Rejected Offers; reason captured. |
| APPROVED_TO_SHARE_WITH_CANDIDATE | Offer shared with candidate | PENDING_WITH_CANDIDATE | Offer letter sent; Send Reminder available. |
| PENDING_WITH_CANDIDATE | Candidate accepts | ACCEPTED_TO_PENDING_LIST | Offer accepted; queued for the pending list. |
| PENDING_WITH_CANDIDATE | Candidate rejects | REJECTED | Position freed; reason captured. |
| PENDING_WITH_CANDIDATE | Offer expiry date passes | EXPIRED | RA / HR Admin may re-extend. |
| ACCEPTED_TO_PENDING_LIST | Added to pending list | IN_PENDING_LIST | Candidate appears in the pending-joiners list. |
| IN_PENDING_LIST | Employee movement initiated | EMPLOYEE_MOVEMENT_INITIATED | Conversion to employee begins. |
| EMPLOYEE_MOVEMENT_INITIATED | Movement approved | EMPLOYEE_MOVEMENT_APPROVED | Triggers Candidate → Pre-joining handover (FR-M08-005); M01 employee_id created. |
| EMPLOYEE_MOVEMENT_APPROVED | Conversion complete | COMPLETED | Offer moves to Completed Offers. |

## 8.8 Performance Review State Machine (M09)

| **Current State** | **Action** | **Next State** | **Side Effects** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| — | Performance Admin initiates cycle | PLANNED → OPEN | review_cycles created. review_records rows created per in-scope employee. |
| OPEN | Self-review opens for employees | (self review window) | Employees notified. Deadline tracked. |
| (self review window) | Employee submits self-review | (L1 review pending) | self_review_submitted_at set. |
| (L1 review pending) | L1 Manager submits L1 review with draft_rating | (calibration pending) | l1_review_submitted_at set. Draft rating visible to Reviewer only. |
| (calibration pending) | HR Admin / Performance Admin completes calibration | (acknowledgement pending) | calibration_rating set. published_rating set. Employee notified. |
| (acknowledgement pending) | Employee acknowledges | ACKNOWLEDGED | acknowledged_at set. |
| (acknowledgement pending) | Employee declines | DECLINED | Decline reason captured. Manager notified. |

The Performance module spans two coupled state machines: the goal plan (goal_plans.state) and the per-cycle review record (review_records stage). Both are governed by FR-M09-001 (plan states), FR-M09-003 (review workflow), FR-M09-024 (closure), and FR-M09-030 (admin on-demand activation, pause, and resume).

- goal_plans.state: PENDING → DRAFT (30 days before plan_start_date) → ACTIVE (on plan_start_date) → IN_REVIEW (on plan_end_date, or earlier via FR-M09-030 admin open) → CLOSED (on cycle close). CANCELLED is reachable from any non-terminal state by admin action.

- review_records stage: SELF → L1_EVALUATION → CALIBRATION → PUBLISHED → ACKNOWLEDGED / DECLINED. Sendback (FR-M09-016) returns L1_EVALUATION → SELF and discards the L1 evaluation; auto-acknowledge fires on the acknowledgement-SLA breach (FR-M09-024).

- Admin pause (FR-M09-030) sets review_records.review_hold = TRUE at any stage, freezing stage progression and SLA clocks; resume restores the stage and the remaining SLA balance. There is no recall.

- review_initiation_source on goal_plans records how IN_REVIEW was entered: CALENDAR (period end) · ADMIN_MANUAL (FR-M09-030) · SEPARATION (FR-M09-024).

## 8.9 Asset Lifecycle State Machine (M17)

Eight states, engine-enforced (FR-M17-005). Invalid transitions rejected; Disposed and Written Off are read-only (soft-delete only).

| **State** | **Allowed transitions** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| In Stock | → Reserved, In Use, Under Maintenance, Lost | Default for new/returned available stock |
| Reserved | → In Use, In Stock | Auto-reverts to In Stock after 14 days if unassigned |
| In Use | → Under Maintenance, In Stock, Lost, Retired | Set on acknowledgement of assignment |
| Under Maintenance | → In Use, In Stock, Retired, Written Off | Manual write-off needs IT + Finance sign-off |
| Retired | → Disposed, Written Off | End of useful life |
| Lost | → In Use (recovery), Written Off (auto 30d) | Opens loss-investigation ticket; 30-day clock (tenant-configurable) |
| Disposed | — (terminal) | Read-only |
| Written Off | → In Use (reversal, Finance sign-off → re-onboard as new record) | Read-only; auto from Lost at 30 days |

## 8.10 Service Ticket State Machine (M17)

Eleven states, engine-enforced (FR-M17-008). In Progress → Resolved is blocked until Resolution Notes are populated. Pending pauses SLA timers.

| **State** | **Allowed transitions** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| New | → Open, Cancelled, Out-of-Scope | On creation (REQ-{YYYY}-{5d}) |
| Open | → In Progress, Pending, Cancelled | Assigned to queue/agent |
| In Progress | → Pending, Pending Approval, Resolved* | *blocked until resolution_notes populated |
| Pending | → In Progress, Resolved | SLA paused; Pending Reason captured |
| Pending Approval | → In Progress, Resolved, Cancelled | Access/catalog approval chain |
| Resolved | → Closed (auto 3 business days), Reopened | CSAT window opens |
| Closed | → Reopened | Terminal unless reopened; P1 → post-mortem |
| Cancelled | — (terminal) |  |
| Out-of-Scope | — (terminal) | Non-IT request; redirect message |
| Reopened | → In Progress | Within reopen window |

# 9. Notification & Communication

This section catalogues every triggering event that produces an outbound notification across Phase 1 modules. Each event is dispatched through P01 Workflow Engine via the notifications entity. Channels supported: EMAIL, SMS, IN_APP. Templates are managed in M11 letter_templates (for formal letters) or platform notification_templates (for transactional messages).

## 9.1 Notification Channels and Defaults

| **Channel** | **Use case** | **Default for** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| IN_APP | Real-time, workflow-related, low-friction acknowledgement | Approval requests, dashboard updates, task assignments |
| EMAIL | Persistent record, formal communications, off-platform reach | Approvals, escalations, letter delivery, birthday/anniversary, milestone events |
| SMS | Time-critical, off-platform reach when email may not be timely | OTP, urgent escalations on payroll cutoff (24th/25th), emergency-contact alerts |

Multi-channel events fire in parallel — IN_APP plus EMAIL is the standard pattern for approval requests so the recipient sees the alert wherever they are.

## 9.2 Leave Management (M04) — Notification Matrix

| **Event code** | **Trigger** | **Channel(s)** | **Recipients** | **Template content** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| LEAVE_SUBMITTED | Employee submits leave application | IN_APP + EMAIL | L1 Manager (Stage 1 approver) | Application number, requestor, leave type, dates, action link |
| LEAVE_APPROVED_STAGE_1 | Stage 1 approval on two-stage type (ML/ADL/MCL/SPL/SBL) | IN_APP + EMAIL | Stage 2 approver pool (HRBP / HR Admin / Leave Admin) | Application number, requestor, leave type, Stage 1 approver, action link |
| LEAVE_APPROVED | Final approval (Stage 1 for single-stage; Stage 2 for two-stage) | IN_APP + EMAIL | Requestor | Approval confirmation, dates, deducted balance |
| LEAVE_REJECTED | Any stage rejection | IN_APP + EMAIL | Requestor | Rejection notice with mandatory reason |
| LEAVE_ESCALATED | 10 days of inaction at Stage 1 | IN_APP + EMAIL | Original approver + Next-level manager + HRBP + HR Admin | Escalation notice with application reference and days outstanding |
| LEAVE_REVOKED | Past-dated revocation by HRBP / Leave Admin / HR Admin | EMAIL | Original requestor + L1 Manager | Revocation notice with reason and balance reversal detail |
| LEAVE_REVOKE_REQUESTED | Employee requests revocation of an approved leave application (D26) | IN_APP + EMAIL | Leave Admin (first), then HRBP / HR Admin | Application number, requestor, leave type, dates, revoke reason, action link |
| LEAVE_WITHDRAWN | Requestor withdraws before final approval | IN_APP | Original Stage 1 approver | Withdrawal notice for awareness |
| LEAVE_ENCASHMENT_AUTHORISED | HR Admin authorises PL encashment | EMAIL | Employee | Encashment confirmation: days, formula, amount, settlement timeline (Phase 2) |

## 9.3 Attendance (M05) — Notification Matrix

| **Event code** | **Trigger** | **Channel(s)** | **Recipients** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| ATTENDANCE_REQUEST_SUBMITTED | Employee submits regularisation / OD / OT / overnight outside-fence / shift change | IN_APP + EMAIL | L1 Manager (eligible approver pool) | Standard SLA 5 days |
| ATTENDANCE_REQUEST_APPROVED | Approver approves | IN_APP | Requestor | Confirmation and updated attendance record |
| ATTENDANCE_REQUEST_REJECTED | Approver rejects | IN_APP + EMAIL | Requestor | Mandatory rejection reason |
| ATTENDANCE_ESCALATION_STANDARD | 5 days inaction | EMAIL | Original approver + next-level manager + HR Admin + Attendance Admin | Standard cadence |
| ATTENDANCE_ESCALATION_PAYROLL_CUTOFF | Pending requests on 24th and 25th of month | EMAIL + SMS | L1 Manager + HR Admin + Attendance Admin | Cadence overrides to every 2 hours until cleared. Applies to all request types except shift change. |
