## 9.9 Notification Governance

- Every notification has a defined event_code, recipient resolution rule, and template — no notification fires from inline code without entry in the catalogue above.

- Templates support merge fields bound to the relevant entity context (employee, application, separation, etc.). Localisation per geography reserved for future (Phase 1 English only).

- Users can suppress non-mandatory IN_APP notifications via notification preferences. EMAIL for approval workflow and statutory notifications is non-suppressible.

- Notification delivery failures are retried with exponential backoff up to 5 attempts. Dead-letter queue surfaces persistent failures to Platform Super Admin.

- Audit log captures every notification dispatch including event_code, recipient, channel, and final delivery state.

- Digest mode (daily / weekly summary) is configurable per user for non-urgent IN_APP notifications. Approval workflow and escalations are never digested.

