## 10.3 Custom Report Builder

- Available to Analytics Admin (entity-scoped by default; tenant-scoped with Org Admin entitlement) and Org Admin.

- Field selection limited by viewer’s data-scope and PII protection ceilings. Tier 1 PII and compensation fields are not selectable for roles without permitted access — they are hidden from the selector.

- Filters supported: equality, in-list, range (numeric/date), null/not-null, contains-text.

- Presentation: tabular, line chart, bar chart, pie chart, KPI tile.

- Scheduling: on-demand execution; or scheduled delivery (email, in-app) with cron-like patterns.

- Sharing: with specific roles, specific users, or department/UAG scopes. All share events audit-logged.

- Custom reports always applied row-level security at query execution — the viewer never sees data outside their own entitlement, regardless of how the report was constructed.

## 10.4 Data Freshness and Caching

| **Data class** | **Freshness target** | **Caching** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Operational (leave applications, attendance records, requisitions) | Real-time on read | No caching of individual records |
| Aggregate metrics (headcount, attrition rate) | Daily refresh at 02:00 IST | Computed in background jobs and cached. Cache TTL configurable by Org Admin — default 4 hours. |
| Dashboard widget snapshots | On-demand at page load | Per-user per-widget cache 60 seconds to absorb scroll/refresh patterns |
| Org chart materialised view | Refreshed on org restructure events plus daily 03:00 IST safety refresh | Maintained as a database materialised view |
| Audit log queries | Real-time (no caching) | Direct query against audit_log; archived entries retrieved from cold storage within 24 hours |

## 10.5 Export and Delivery

- Reports exportable as CSV (default), XLSX, and PDF (formatted).

- Bulk export operations queued via the jobs entity — large exports do not block the requesting session.

- Scheduled email delivery uses the same notification dispatch pipeline — failed deliveries retried with exponential backoff.

- All export and download events are logged in security_audit_log with event type PII_EXPORT for reports containing PII fields.

- Exported files are watermarked with the requestor’s name, timestamp, and report code for traceability.

# 11. Migration & Launch

## 11.1 Migration Approach — Darwinbox as Source System

Phase 1 migration scope covers PrimeSoft’s existing Darwinbox tenant as the primary source system for Release 1. The migration is structured as a three-wave plan over the ETL+V (Extract → Validate → Transform → Load → Verify) pattern, with strict gating between dry runs and production cutover. P06 Migration Toolkit owns the framework; HR Admin participates in field mapping review and data verification at the entity level.

Core principles:

- Idempotent scripts — running the same script twice produces the same result. Idempotency keyed on darwinbox_source_id.

- Source traceability — every migrated record carries a darwinbox_source_id column populated on insert. This is the permanent traceability link from source to current state and is never overwritten.

- Counter reset suppression — JR_ requisition counter and the six per-employee-type CAN_ candidate counters are carried forward verbatim. Counter values at migration: JR_ = 557 · CAN_ Full Time = 13799 · CAN_ Part Time = 01 · CAN_ Associate = 6498 · CAN_ Contract = 35 · CAN_ Consultant = 32 · CAN_ Intern = 02.

- Three mandatory dry runs against a staging environment before any production cutover. Production cutover is gated on Dry Run 3 achieving < 0.5% failure rate for Waves 1 and 2.

- Wave 3 (payroll history, Phase 2) requires zero tolerance for numeric discrepancies in payroll amounts.

- Darwinbox kept in read-only mode for a minimum of 4 weeks after production cutover before the customer’s Darwinbox subscription is cancelled.

## 11.2 Migration Waves

| **Wave** | **Phase 1 dependency** | **Scope** | **Volume estimate (Release 1)** | **Gating criterion** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Wave 1 | the post-migration go-live prerequisite | Employee master · employment types · org structure (departments, designations, grades, locations) · leave balances + 2 years of leave history · attendance records (24 months) · holiday calendars | Up to 500 active employees plus history | Dry Run 3 < 0.5% failure rate |
| Wave 2 | Phase 1 concurrent (can complete before or with go-live) | Performance history (last 4 cycles) · job history and promotions · employee contracts · separation records · active recruitment pipeline (requisitions, candidates, offers, interviews) | Cumulative ~ 5,000 records across categories | Dry Run 3 < 0.5% failure rate |
| Wave 3 | Phase 2 — payroll go-live prerequisite | Payroll history · statutory filings history | 24-36 months of records | Zero numeric discrepancies on payroll amounts |

## 11.3 ETL+V Pattern — Per-Wave Execution

| **Stage** | **Owner** | **Activity** | **Output** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Extract | Platform Super Admin via P06 Migration Toolkit | Pull source data from Darwinbox export or API. Raw data staged in P06 with darwinbox_source_id retained. | Staged raw dataset |
| Validate | P06 + HR Admin (entity-level data verification) | Apply validation rules per the field policy register: mandatory fields enforced, data type / format / range checks, enum-value mapping, referential integrity within source. | Per-record validation report — pass / fail with reason |
| Transform | P06 | Apply field mappings, value translations (e.g. Darwinbox status codes → PrimeSoft lifecycle states), and structural reshaping (e.g. wide leave balance rows → tall employee_leave_balances rows). Apply tenant-specific configuration overrides. | Transformed dataset ready for load |
| Load | P06 | Insert into target tables in dependency order: master data first (entities, departments, designations, grades, locations) → users → employees → employment_history → leave/attendance balances → transactional history. All inserts carry darwinbox_source_id. | Loaded records with new platform IDs |
| Verify | Platform Super Admin + HR Admin | Row count reconciliation per table. Spot-check sample records. Field-level diff between source and loaded target. Re-run validation on loaded data. | Verification report — discrepancies enumerated with darwinbox_source_id traceability |

## 11.4 Dry Run Schedule and Exit Criteria

| **Run** | **Goal** | **Exit criterion** | **Action on miss** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Dry Run 1 | End-to-end framework validation; identify systemic mapping issues | All scripts execute end-to-end without infrastructure failure. Documented mapping issues for remediation. | Remediate mappings; do not gate Dry Run 2 timeline. |
| Dry Run 2 | Field mapping accuracy and rule conformance | Failure rate < 5%. All Critical and High severity discrepancies resolved. | Re-run after remediation. Multiple Dry Run 2 iterations permitted. |
| Dry Run 3 | Production-readiness gate | Failure rate < 0.5% for Waves 1 and 2. Zero Critical discrepancies. HR Admin signs off on entity-level data verification. | Production cutover blocked until criterion met. Additional dry runs scheduled. |
| Production Cutover | Live migration to production target | All records loaded with darwinbox_source_id. Reconciliation report signed off by Head of HR and CTO. | Rollback plan invoked if go-live readiness checks fail. |

## 11.5 Phased Product Rollout

PrimeSoft HRMS rolls out in three phases. Phase 1 covers foundation and core operations as a responsive web application. Phase 2 adds payroll, hike, and mobile applications. Phase 3 adds expense, benefits, engagement, and social modules.

| **Phase** | **Scope** | **Target window** | **Key dependencies** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Phase 1 | M01 · M02 · M03 · M04 · M05 · M08 · M09 · M11 · M16 · M17 · P01-P06. Responsive web only. | Release 1 | Wave 1 migration complete; VAPT zero Critical/High; UAT exit zero P1 defects |
| Phase 2 | M06 Payroll · M07 Statutory Compliance · M10 Hikes & Compensation · Native mobile applications · Offline capability · Wave 3 migration | Release 2 | Phase 1 production stable for 90 days; Phase 2 functional spec sign-off |
| Phase 3 | M12 Expense & Travel · M14 Benefits & Insurance · M15 Engagement & Surveys · M18 Internal Social · Resume parsing / OCR · ID verification package | Release 3 | Phase 2 production stable for 90 days; partner integrations signed |

## 11.6 the post-migration go-live Checklist

### 12.6.1 Functional Readiness

- All Phase 1 functional requirements implemented and signed off on UAT.

- Zero P1 defects outstanding at UAT exit. P2 defects with documented workarounds.

- Wave 1 migration complete with Dry Run 3 < 0.5% failure rate. Wave 2 either complete or in-flight with go-live mitigation plan.

- Pre-built reports (Section 11.1) execute correctly with target latency.

- Dashboard widgets render correctly per role at 375 px, 768 px, 1280 px breakpoints.

- All 18 roles configured with their default permission sets validated.

### 12.6.2 Security and Compliance Readiness

- VAPT complete with zero Critical and zero High findings unresolved.

- MFA enforced for HR Admin and Organisation Admin role assignments. Tested with TOTP and SMS OTP.

- TLS 1.3 enforced; AES-256-GCM at rest verified across all PII tables; per-tenant KMS keys created.

- Audit log database trigger validated — sample mutations confirmed to produce audit entries.

- DPDPA consent capture validated at onboarding flow.

- POSH policy published, ICC committee configured, grievance routing tested.

### 12.6.3 Operational Readiness

- Production environment provisioned in India home region with DR replica in second Indian region.

- Backup and restore tested — RTO < 4 hours, RPO < 1 hour validated on a sample restore.

- Monitoring and alerting configured for SLO breaches (latency, availability, integration errors).

- Incident response runbooks complete and on-call rotation established.

- Customer training delivered to HR Admin, Org Admin, IT Admin, and key managers.

- Chat Agent grounded on the customer’s published policy documents and platform help guides.

### 12.6.4 Cutover Day

- Darwinbox set to read-only for end users at cutover start.

- Final Wave 1 production load executes. Reconciliation report generated and signed off.

- DNS and routing switched to PrimeSoft HRMS production endpoint.

- Smoke tests across login, leave application, attendance punch, requisition list, dashboard render.

- Customer go-live communication sent to all employees with login URL and SSO/credentials guidance.

- Darwinbox remains in read-only mode for 4 weeks post-cutover for verification and dispute resolution before subscription cancellation.

## 11.7 Rollback Plan

- Pre-cutover rollback: if Dry Run 3 fails to meet exit criterion, cutover is rescheduled. No production impact.

- Cutover-day rollback (within 24 hours of cutover): DNS reverted to Darwinbox; Darwinbox set back to read-write; any changes made on PrimeSoft HRMS during the cutover window logged for manual reconciliation. Rollback decision rests with CTO and Head of HR jointly.

- Post-cutover rollback (beyond 24 hours): not supported. Issues are remediated forward on PrimeSoft HRMS. Darwinbox read-only window serves as data verification reference, not rollback target.

- Migration scripts are idempotent on darwinbox_source_id — selective re-load of a subset of records is supported post-cutover for correction.

# 12. Glossary

Definitions for terms used across this BRD. Where a term has both a generic and a PrimeSoft-specific meaning, the platform-specific meaning is given.

## 12.1 Tenancy and Organisation

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| Tenant | Top-level customer organisation in PrimeSoft HRMS. One tenant has one tenants row. All queries automatically scoped to tenant_id. |
| Entity | Legal entity within a tenant. In a Group Company deployment, one tenant has multiple legal entities. Each entity has independent statutory configuration. **No transactional flow crosses entity boundaries** — leave, attendance, payroll, statutory filings, and FnF settlement are entity-scoped. Cross-entity transfer is modelled as separation from the source entity plus a new hire into the target entity. **Cross-entity visibility** for HR data (e.g. group-level headcount, group attrition, ex-employee history across entities) belongs to **Org Admin**; HR Admin scope remains single-entity. |
| Deployment Model | STANDALONE (single org, single entity) · MULTI_TENANT_SAAS (shared infrastructure, tenant isolation) · GROUP_COMPANY (one parent, multiple legal entities, shared HRMS instance). |
| UAG (User Assignment Group) | Named group of one or more employees assigned to a specific individual (UAG Head or HRBP). Created and managed by Organisation Admin. An employee may belong to more than one UAG. |
| HRBP | HR Business Partner. Operates HR for directly assigned employees (individually or via UAG). Business unit assignment optional. |
| HOD | Head of Department. Has department-wide read visibility within their assigned department, regardless of reporting line. |
| Contribution Level | Additional filter applied within a role’s normal scope. Levels: INTERN · ASSOCIATE · INDIVIDUAL_CONTRIBUTOR · LEAD · SENIOR_LEAD · MANAGER · SENIOR_MANAGER · CEO. |

## 12.2 Employee Lifecycle

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| Pre-joining | M01 lifecycle state after offer countersignature and before onboarding completes. Pre-joining portal access only. |
| Active | Working employee state. Sub-state Probation tracked via probation_flag on employment_history (not a separate lifecycle state). |
| Notice | M01 lifecycle state after separation approval and before LWD. Reduced workflow initiation rights; restricted leave types. |
| LWD (Last Working Day) | Last day of employment service. After this date the employee transitions to Separated state via FnF clearance completion. |
| FLWD (Final Last Working Day) | Approved last working day on a separation_records row. May differ from proposed_last_working_day. Past-dated FLWD is a one-way door — immediate deactivation, reactivation blocked. |
| Separated | Terminal post-employment state. Read-only access for own payslips and documents for configurable period (default LWD + 180 days). |
| Absconding | Non-terminal state set automatically when 7 consecutive calendar days of unauthorised absence is detected. HR Admin action required to resolve (restore to Active or convert to Separated). |
| Rehire Eligible | Flag on a separation_records row indicating positive exit; supports future re-engagement via M08. |
| Group date of joining | Set on first employment in the group; preserved across cross-entity transfers and rehires. Never changes thereafter. |
| FnF (Full and Final settlement) | Multi-department parallel clearance workflow at end of employment. Payroll settlement (Phase 2) blocked until all departmental clearances complete. |

## 12.3 Recruitment and Onboarding

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| ATS (Applicant Tracking System) | M08 Recruitment module functionality covering requisitions, candidates, interviews, and offers. |
| BGV (Background Verification) | Pre-employment verification of candidate-supplied data. Configurable per package per vendor. Result statuses: PENDING · VERIFIED · DISCREPANCY · UNABLE_TO_VERIFY. |
| Hiring Lead | User designated as primary hiring decision-maker per requisition. Recruitment Admin or higher in the hiring chain. |
| JR_557 | Concrete example of a migrated requisition counter value. Counter is global per tenant; carried forward verbatim from Darwinbox source. |
| CAN_ | Candidate ID prefix. Six separate counters per Employee Type (Full Time, Part Time, Associate, Contract, Consultant, Intern). All carried forward verbatim from migrated source. |
| IJP (Internal Job Posting) | Job posting visible only to internal employees per eligibility rules (minimum tenure, departments, etc.). |

## 12.4 Performance Management

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| OKR (Objectives and Key Results) | Goal methodology used in M09. Phase 1 platform-fixed methodology. Sub-goals (Key Results) supported via parent_goal_id self-reference. |
| KRA | Key Result Area. Synonymous with sub-goal under OKR in Phase 1 implementation. |
| MSF (Multi-Source Feedback) | L1 Manager-initiated peer feedback during review cycle. Contributors are runtime assignments — no RBAC role or capability flag. |
| Calibration | HR-led moderation of L1 draft ratings across a peer set. Run by HR Admin and Performance Admin; viewable by Skip-level Managers and HODs with module entitlement. |
| Probation Confirmation | Calendar-driven trigger at probation_end_date. L1 Manager recommends Confirm / Extend / Not Confirm; HR Admin confirms. |

## 12.5 Leave and Attendance

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| SL · PL · PL_CC · WWC · WL · PATL · ML · ADL · MCL · SPL · SBL · OH_*_26 · Unpaid/LOP | Leave type codes migrated from Darwinbox. See data model §4.5.1 for full mapping. |
| Encashment | Conversion of leave balance to cash. Phase 1: PL only; HR Admin authorisation only (not Leave Admin); intermittent allowed in 3-30 day range; blocked during probation. |
| Regularisation | Attendance request type for correcting incomplete or absent attendance records. Subject to 7-per-month limit on ATPY_4/ATPY_5 policies. |
| Out Duty | Attendance request type for legitimate work-related absence from office (field work, client visits). Approved Out Duty counts as present day for payroll. |
| Geofence | Configurable radius around an office location for in-fence / outside-fence determination on attendance punches. |
| ATPY_4 · ATPY_5 · ATPY_1 | Attendance policy codes — All Employees primary · On Probation · CEO Flexible. Migrated from Darwinbox source. |
| Two-stage flow (leave) | Mandatory two-stage approval for ML / ADL / MCL / SPL / SBL. Stage 1 = standard; Stage 2 = HRBP / HR Admin / Leave Admin only. Cannot be bypassed. |

## 12.6 Security, RBAC, and Privacy

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) | Four-layer access control: Module · Field & Section · Data-level (row-level security) · Action-level (View / Edit / Approve / Download / Admin Rights). |
| Conflict Resolution Rule | Where a user holds more than one role, the more restrictive permission applies. A less permissive role never elevates access granted by a more permissive one. |
| PII Tiers | Tier 1 Restricted (PAN, Aadhaar, Passport, Bank, Salary — encrypted at rest, masked in display) · Tier 2 Sensitive (DOB, marital status, nominees) · Tier 3 Personal (addresses, personal email) · Directory (name, designation, official email, profile photo, office location). |
| PII Protection Ceiling | System-enforced upper bound on PII access per role. No Organisation Admin, Module Admin, or individual entitlement grant can override these ceilings upward. |
| Capability Flag | Grantable role extension. Phase 1 defines four: BGV review, Letter Admin, Asset Custodian, and Department Head — Asset Audit Certify (plus two HOD configurable grants). Granted by Organisation Admin to a specific role assignment, audit-logged. |
| Individual Entitlement | Time-bound access beyond a role’s default profile. Granted by Organisation Admin within PII protection ceilings. Mandatory expiry date. Auto-revoked on expiry. All grants and revokes audit-logged. |
| MFA (Multi-Factor Authentication) | Required for HR Admin and Organisation Admin roles. Methods: TOTP (RFC 6238) and SMS OTP. |
| SSO (Single Sign-On) | Tenant-configured Google Workspace OAuth 2.0 with PKCE. Username/password also supported. |
| Soft delete | Mark record as deleted (set deleted_at, deleted_by) without physical removal from database. Phase 1 universal pattern — no hard deletes anywhere. |
| Effective-date versioning | New employment_history row written on every change to a versioned field. Past, present, and future-dated changes supported. Future-dated changes applied by scheduled job at 00:00 IST daily. |
| Audit log | Immutable database-trigger-driven mutation log. 100% of mutations captured. Audit log table has no UPDATE or DELETE permission — sole exception is system-initiated PII redaction under right-to-erasure. |

## 12.7 Compliance and Statutory

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| POSH (Prevention of Sexual Harassment at the Workplace Act 2013) | Indian statutory requirement for workplace anti-harassment. Phase 1 implements mandatory policy publication, acknowledgement tracking, complaint intake (M01 Grievance Register with anonymous opt-in), and ICC routing for POSH-category grievances. |
| DPDPA (Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023) | Indian personal data protection regulation. Phase 1 implements consent capture, right of access, right of correction, right of erasure for non-statutory data, data principal request register, data fiduciary obligations. |
| ICC (Internal Complaints Committee) | POSH-Act-mandated committee for handling POSH complaints. Identity of complainant revealed only to ICC for POSH grievances — not HR Admin (HR Admin sees aggregate count only). |
| Statutory nominee | Gratuity nominee · PF nominee · ESI nominee. Captured at M02 Onboarding (Phase 1). Operationally consumed by M07 (Phase 2). |
| Right of access (DPDPA) | Employee can export own record with PII unmasked. |
| Right of erasure (DPDPA) | Subject to statutory retention. Non-statutory PII deleted; statutory data archived but never deleted. |
| Audit log redaction marker | Replacement value written in audit log when right-to-erasure overwrites a PII value. Audit entry structure preserved; PII value replaced. |

## 12.8 Platform and Architecture

| **Term** | **Definition** |
| --- | --- |
| Workflow Engine (P01) | Single configurable engine driving all approval and notification processes. Five patterns: SEQUENTIAL · PARALLEL_ALL_OF · PARALLEL_ANY_OF · CONDITIONAL · DYNAMIC_APPROVER. |
| Chat Agent (P03) | Document-grounded AI policy Q&A. Two grounding sources: organisation-uploaded policy documents and platform help guides. All API calls backend-only; PII stripped before AI call. |
| Migration Toolkit (P06) | Darwinbox ETL+V framework. Three mandatory dry runs; production cutover gated at < 0.5% failure rate for Waves 1 and 2; zero numeric discrepancies for payroll amounts in Wave 3. |
| darwinbox_source_id | Permanent traceability column on every migrated record. Indexed. Never overwritten. |
| Idempotent | Property of migration scripts: running the same script twice produces the same result. Keyed on darwinbox_source_id. |
| UAG Head workflow approval | Hard system ceiling — cannot be granted under any configuration. Distinct from HOD approval authority which is off by default but per-workflow per-user configurable by Org Admin. |
| Office Admin grants (PAN / Aadhaar / Passport / Driving Licence / DOB / Bank entry) | Platform-level fixed grants. Not configurable upward or downward. Survive the Conflict Resolution Rule because they are not ‘less permissive’ grants of an existing role. |

# 13. Appendices

- **FR-M08-004 offer letter generation rights extended.** Both Recruitment Admin AND HR Admin can generate offer letters (either role acting alone is sufficient — no joint sign-off required). Recruiter still cannot generate offer letters. Role definitions for HR Administrator and Recruitment Admin both updated to reflect joint capability; FR-M08-004 description, business rule, and edge case all reflect the dual ownership.

- **Multi-entity within tenant — cross-entity visibility model clarified.** A tenant deployed as GROUP_COMPANY holds multiple legal entities. **No HR transaction crosses entity boundaries** (leave, attendance, payroll, statutory filings, and FnF stay entity-scoped; cross-entity transfer is modelled as separation-plus-new-hire per FLOW-EMP-005). **Cross-entity HR data visibility within a tenant is owned by Org Admin alone** — the only role with cross-entity reach inside a tenant. HR Admin remains single-entity scoped. **Platform Super Admin is explicitly NOT the answer for cross-entity within a tenant** — Platform Super Admin’s scope is cross-tenant (cross-customer) and must not be used to bridge entities inside a single customer’s group. Entity glossary definition, Org Admin role mandate, and §3.3 introduction all updated to reinforce this model.

## Appendix A — Indian Statutory Compliance (Phase 1 Summary)

Phase 1 embeds three statutory obligations directly into module behaviour. Full statutory deductions, government filings, and gratuity / PF / ESI / TDS / PT / LWF outputs are Phase 2 (M06 Payroll + M07 Statutory Compliance) and are out of Phase 1 scope. The table below summarises Phase 1 statutory coverage.

| **Statute** | **Phase 1 obligations covered** | **Module(s)** | **Phase 2/3 dependency** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| POSH Act 2013 | Mandatory policy publication and acknowledgement · Complaint intake with anonymous opt-in · POSH category routes to ICC committee (not HR Admin) · Training completion tracking | M11 · M01 (Grievance Register) · M16 (aggregate count) | — |
| DPDPA 2023 | Consent capture at onboarding · Right of access (employee export with PII unmasked) · Right of correction via sensitive-field change workflow · Right of erasure for non-statutory data · Data principal request register · Audit log redaction marker for erased PII | M02 · M01 · P05 · platform consent_records | — |
| Shops & Establishments Act (state-wise) | State-wise leave entitlements and working-hour rules · Location-based policy overrides | M04 · M05 · locations master | — |
| EPF & MP Act 1952 | Phase 1: PF nominee data captured at M02 Onboarding. Reserved schema fields for UAN, EPS, PF account. | M01 (statutory_identities) | Phase 2: M07 PF enrolment, ECR challan generation |
| ESI Act 1948 | Phase 1: ESI nominee data captured at M02 if employee meets eligibility. Reserved schema fields for ESIC number. | M01 (statutory_identities) | Phase 2: M07 ESI enrolment, challan generation |
| Income Tax Act (TDS Section 192) | Phase 1: PAN captured and validated. Schema reserved for TDS configuration. | M01 (statutory_identities) | Phase 2: M07 TDS computation, Form 24Q, Form 16 |
| Payment of Gratuity Act 1972 | Phase 1: Gratuity nominee captured at M02 Onboarding; mandatory at probation confirmation. | M01 (dependents) | Phase 2: M07 gratuity computation and FnF payout |
| Maternity Benefit Act 1961 (as amended 2017) | Phase 1: ML / ADL / MCL leave types active with two-stage approval; per-event credit; Indian statutory caps applied | M04 | — |
| Professional Tax (state-wise) | Phase 1: PT state captured per entity; PT slab applicability schema reserved | Entities master | Phase 2: M07 PT deduction calculation |
| Labour Welfare Fund (state-wise) | Phase 1: LWF state captured per entity | Entities master | Phase 2: M07 LWF deduction calculation |

## Appendix B — PII Classification Tiers (Detail)

| **Tier** | **Examples** | **Encryption at rest** | **Display rule** | **Audit on view** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Tier 1 — Restricted | PAN · Aadhaar · Passport · Driving Licence · Bank Account · CTC / Salary | AES-256-GCM with per-tenant KMS keys | Always masked in display except for explicit platform-level grants (Office Admin for IDs/bank entry; HR Admin via sensitive-field change workflow) | Yes — every view event logged in security_audit_log with viewer, field, employee, timestamp, IP, user agent |
| Tier 2 — Sensitive | Date of Birth · Marital status · Nominees · Performance ratings (draft and published) | Database-level encryption (table-level) | Visible to authorised roles per RBAC §3 matrix | Yes — Tier 2 access events logged at sampling rate per Org Admin configuration |
| Tier 3 — Personal | Current address · Permanent address · Personal email · Personal mobile · Emergency contacts | Database-level encryption | Visible to employee (own) and authorised HR roles | No — standard application logging only |
| Directory | Display name · Designation · Department · Official email · Official mobile · Office location · Profile photo | Standard storage | Visible to all authenticated users within tenant | No |

## Appendix C — Audit Log Structure

Two distinct audit logs are maintained. They serve different evidentiary and operational purposes.

### C.1 Data Audit Log (audit_log entity)

- Scope: every INSERT, UPDATE, soft-DELETE on any business table.

- Owner: database trigger — not application code. No application bug, developer action, or API bypass can suppress an entry.

- Mutability: audit_log has no UPDATE or DELETE permission granted to any database user. Sole exception: system-initiated PII redaction under right-to-erasure workflow.

- Fields: table_name · record_id · operation · field_name (on UPDATE) · old_value (PII-masked) · new_value (PII-masked) · changed_by_user_id · changed_at · ip_address · user_agent.

- Retention: minimum 7 years. After 2 years entries may be archived to cold storage but remain queryable within 24 hours.

### C.2 Security Audit Log (security_audit_log entity)

- Scope: authentication events · authorisation events · administrative actions · integration calls · PII view events · PII export events.

- Event types: LOGIN_SUCCESS · LOGIN_FAILURE · LOGOUT · MFA_PROMPT · MFA_SUCCESS · MFA_FAILURE · ACCOUNT_LOCKED · ACCESS_DENIED · RBAC_CHANGE · ROLE_ASSIGNMENT · INTEGRATION_CALL · PII_VIEW · PII_EXPORT.

- Fields: event_type · user_id · timestamp · ip_address · user_agent · resource_identifier · integration_endpoint · payload_hash (SHA-256, never raw content) · response_status · latency_ms · details.

- Integration calls log payload hashes — never raw content. Preserves traceability without leaking sensitive payload data.

## Appendix D — Workflow Engine Pattern Reference

Five workflow patterns are supported by P01. Each is illustrated with a Phase 1 example.

| **Pattern** | **Behaviour** | **Phase 1 example** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SEQUENTIAL | Stage 1 must complete before Stage 2 starts. Linear progression through stages. | Leave application standard flow: L1 Manager → (if escalated) next-level manager + HRBP + HR Admin |
| PARALLEL_ALL_OF | All stages execute simultaneously. Workflow completes only when all stages have approved. | FnF clearance: IT · Finance · Admin · Manager · HR · Payroll all clear simultaneously; FnF cannot complete until every clearance is CLEARED |
| PARALLEL_ANY_OF | All stages notified simultaneously. Workflow completes when any one stage approves. | Leave Stage 1 escalation: any eligible role (L1 Manager · HRBP · HR Admin · Leave Admin) can approve |
| CONDITIONAL | Stage routing depends on data values at runtime. Multiple branches possible. | Offer letter: if proposed_ctc > threshold then CEO approval and CEO co-signature required; else Recruitment Admin or HR Admin can extend directly with HR Admin signature |
| DYNAMIC_APPROVER | Approver identity resolved at runtime based on context (reporting chain position, cost centre head, named role). | Leave Stage 1: approver resolved as employee’s current L1 Manager from employment_history |

