## Appendix G — Phase 1 Binding Decisions

This appendix records decisions that carry functional-requirement consequences and are binding for the Phase 1 build.

| **Item** | **Resolution** | **Source for FR / data model alignment** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CTC threshold for CEO offer approval (M08) | Threshold value at provisioning: INR 50,00,000 per annum (fifty lakh) for Individual Contributor roles. Offers with proposed_ctc above this value require CEO approval and CEO co-signature on the offer letter before transitioning offers.state to APPROVED. Threshold is a tenant-level configuration value managed by Organisation Admin and supports separate threshold values per band/grade if configured. Threshold can be revised by Org Admin at any time, audit-logged; revision does not affect in-flight offers (they continue on the threshold value captured at creation). | Binds FR-M08-004 — CEO approval condition and threshold default |
| Absconding threshold override policy (M05) | Platform default 7 consecutive calendar days remains the binding value. Per-tenant override by Org Admin permitted within bounds 5–14 days. Per-entity override by HR Admin within the same bounds. Values outside 5–14 days require a Platform Super Admin override request audit-logged with justification. Three-tier governance prevents accidental drift while preserving customisation flexibility. | Binds FR-M05-005 — sets the configuration range and governance |

## Appendix H — Scope Decisions & Boundaries

The following scope decisions and boundaries apply to the Phase 1 baseline.

### Scope decisions

- **Profile_View_settings.csv** authoritative for field-level visibility configuration in M01.

- **Country IDs** modeled as catalogue pattern via geo_master (§4.2.13).

- **Assignment system** elevated to first-class master entity (§4.2.17), not enumerated list.

- **Translations** out of scope (deferred to a later phase).

- **Multi-Site Federation (MSF)** + Marketplace deferred to Phase 2.

- **RBAC** full 152×18 cell appendix inline in §3.7.4.

- **M09 templates** fully documented (goal plan templates, review templates, calibration).

- **M04 Leave** all 30+ clusters documented in §4.5.7.

- **Visual styling** out of scope (rendered via the prototype separately).

- **Department head roles** modeled as multiple FK fields on Department entity, not separate role entity.

### Confirmed out-of-scope

- **System-assigned / org-level Goals** — not in scope. All goals are employee-created or manager-cascaded; no goal plan has cascade enabled. GoalsExport empty by design; no dangling references.

- **Band master** — not in scope. No grade references a band and no assignment rule filters on band. BandExport empty by design; no dangling references.

- **Recruitment Assessments and Interview Guides** — not in scope. No workflow stage schedules an assessment. Assign_Assessments and Interview_Guides empty by design; no dangling references.

### Deferred to a later phase

- Translation / multi-language UI configuration.

- Multi-Site Federation (MSF) data model.

- Marketplace catalogue and integration framework.

- Payroll module (M06) detailed entity schemas.

- Travel module (M12) detailed entity schemas.

- Helpdesk module (M14) detailed entity schemas.

- Asset & IT module (M17) detailed entity schemas.

- R&R module detailed entity schemas.

## Appendix I — Configured Flow Catalog

