## Appendix J — Onboarding Form Catalog

Catalog of the onboarding forms configured for Phase 1: two candidate self-fill variants and seven workflow (stakeholder-fill) forms, with section structure and the workflow stage each form is tagged to. This catalog is intentionally section-level. Field-level definitions — field types, mandatory flags, validation rules, and System-Field-to-M01 database mapping — are deferred to the M02 Functional Specification and the onboarding configuration workbook, consistent with the §N FS boundary (Part B completion).

| **Form** | **Type** | **Sections / structure** | **Tagged to (stage)** | **Population** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| BGV Form Standard | Candidate self-fill | Personal · Disability (repeatable) · Address (current + permanent) · Emergency Contact · Education (repeatable) · Personal Identity (PAN/Aadhaar/Passport) · Previous Employer (repeatable, incl. references & documents) · Visa (repeatable) · Vaccination · Personal Documents · Others | Candidate portal — Onboarding Form stage | Experienced / lateral hires ("Employment Check") |
| BGV Form – Associates | Candidate self-fill | Same section skeleton with education-verification emphasis; reduced employment-history depth; Middle Name mandatory | Candidate portal — Onboarding Form stage | Fresh hires ("Education Check") |
| Admin Form | Workflow form | Cubicle Assigned, Welcome kit, ID Card given, Bank Account opened, Parking sticker & allocation (all mandatory) + Comments | Admin Task | All |
| IT Form | Workflow form | Profile-synced identity (read-only) + IT Induction Status | IT Induction | All |
| IT Assets Form | Workflow form | Access card, ID Card, PrimeSoft Laptop, Client Laptop, Mobile, Other Assets + Comments | IT asset allocation (M17-integrated) | All |
| HR Induction Form | Workflow form | HR Induction Completed, POSH Policy Explained, Office Tour done, Introductions to RM/Team/IT/Admin/Accounts/Senior Managers (all mandatory) + Comments | HR Induction | All |
| Manager Induction Form | Workflow form | 10-item induction checklist (project roles, study material, coding/QA guidelines, repo access, customer tools, comms etiquette, standup schedule, status report, training plan, goals set) + Comments | Manager Induction | All |
| Manager Induction Checklist | Workflow form | Profile-synced identity + Induction Comments | Manager Induction Checklist | All |
| External BGV | Workflow form | Profile-synced Full Name + Date of Joining + BGV Status | BGV | All |

Population split. The two candidate variants are assigned by hiring population: BGV Form Standard ("Standard and Employment Check") targets experienced / lateral hires and emphasises prior-employment verification; BGV Form – Associates ("Standard and Education Check") targets fresh hires and emphasises education verification with a reduced employment-history set. Contract employees run a separate onboarding workflow (WF_14 per Appendix I).

Workflow form behaviour. Workflow forms are stakeholder-fill forms embedded in onboarding workflow stages (Appendix I). Identity fields shown as profile-synced are read-only and populated from the Employee Profile (M01); the action field on each form (e.g. IT Induction Status, BGV Status, induction checklist responses) is the stakeholder-completed input that drives stage completion.

